{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:55:28.319Z","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>wdps7v5g5</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01Ty86F6zaSqkpaJThzjt57k</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/tasks/wdps7v5g5.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Dynamic workflow \"Adversarial review of MM23 pass 2 by lens (L4, L6, L7, simulation, general), then refutation of each finding\" completed</summary>\n<result>[{\"lens\":\"L4\",\"review\":{\"findings\":[],\"checked\":\"Lens L4 (is freeSound_derived circular?). Reviewed the committed MM23.lean at 579808d. No finding survived checking.\\n\\n1. **Is the conservation imposed and derived, or assumed?** It is imposed by Repr and derived along the trace, so there is no circularity.\\n   - `ReprB.provTokens` (MM23.lean:116) requires that every root r with `provOf r = some pr` has all its leaves in an allocation with `freeAuth = some (ptok pr)`.\\n   - `freeSound_derived` (1766) is a projection of that clause, combined with `FreeCompatInst`. The brief asks for exactly this: \\\"content = conservation along the trace ... (Repr imposes it)\\\".\\n   - The token is set when the allocation is created: `assoc` maps `.alloc pr` to `allocOps ... (some (π.ptok pr))`, and `r6_alloc` uses `hprov : provOf (n+i) = some pr`.\\n   - It is then preserved through `Dom` (MM23.lean:330, which includes `a'.freeAuth = a.freeAuth`) in ReprB.change, transport, shrink, repr_deallocs and repr_extend.\\n   - MM02 `State.write`, `dealloc` and `alloc` never change an existing `freeAuth`.\\n   - `simulation` re-establishes Repr at every step. Nothing about the token is assumed in a form that already contains FreeSound: FreeSound reads `k`, `auth` and `s2`, while provTokens reads only `ptok`, `provOf` and `s2`.\\n   - The pass-1 `FreeSound` definition is unchanged. It is no longer a hypothesis anywhere; its only use is as the conclusion of `freeSound_derived`, which `r6_free` calls (1795).\\n\\n2. **Does the ghost change only at alloc, and can it be chosen per step to fit?**\\n   - `provStep` changes the ghost only for `.alloc`. `SimRun`/`Trans` start from `fun _ =&gt; none` and thread `provStep op s3 pv` through each step, so the ghost is fixed by the run and `π`. It cannot be chosen per step.\\n   - `simulation` also proves `pv r = none` for every `r` beyond `P.length`. Indices are never reused, so a value, once set, never changes. The per-step `FreeOblig` is therefore equivalent to one instantiation for the whole execution.\\n   - Only enterP, allocP and transferEff modify P.\\n\\n3. **Instantiation and direction in FreeOblig.**\\n   - `FreeOblig` is `k.FreeCompat p auth → ∃ pr, pv p = some pr ∧ C auth (ptok pr)`, which matches `CanDealloc` (`Compatible auth d`).\\n   - FreeStep requires FreeCompat, so the implication is never vacuous on a free step.\\n   - FreeCompat is only a gate on `free`. Keeping only the → direction therefore weakens a hypothesis without weakening any conclusion.\\n\\n4. **Reached states of a SimRun.**\\n   - **Alloc'd roots never have provOf none:** provStep maps every index in `[len, len + ls.length)` to `some pr`.\\n   - **Statics never have provOf some:** the ghost starts at `none`, and `repr_init` takes `hprov = none`.\\n   - **Frame locals never have provOf some:** enter does not touch the ghost, and the beyond-length invariant gives `none`, which `r6_enter` uses through `hprov`.\\n   - **Owner kind is invariant:** shapeOwner gives an alloc'd root a place owner. mvTo maps a place owner to a place owner and leaves frame owners alone (heldIn of a frame is False). So an alloc'd root never meets the `tokens` (`tok f`) clause or `exitOps`.\\n   - **Uncovered frees are outside the envelope:** a free of a static or of a non-alloc'd root cannot meet FreeOblig. Under L1 (`Deallocable` false on statics, `NoOwner` in `Step3`), such a free never takes an ok step anyway.\\n   - **Parts also receive the provider in the ghost:** this changes no behaviour. provTokens quantifies only over RootPlace, and free requires OwnedRoot.\\n\\n5. **Checks run in Lean.**\\n   - Ern/MM23.olean was absent, and the working tree has an uncommitted 8-line `example` added to MM23.lean, which I did not review. I therefore compiled a copy of `git show 579808d:formal/Ern/MM23.lean` with my experiments appended:\\n     - copy: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review/L4/full.lean\\n     - experiments: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review/L4/ghost.lean\\n     - output: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review/L4/full.out\\n   - Result: no errors. `freeSound_derived`, `simulation` and `r6_free` each depend only on [propext, Quot.sound].\\n   - On the CaseSim run, `decide` confirms:\\n     - `pvA 4 = some 1`, and `pvA` is `none` on frame locals 0, 1, 2, 3, 7 and 8;\\n     - `¬ ReprB` with a wrong ghost (4 ↦ 2) at x3/n3, so the ghost is not free inside Repr;\\n     - `¬ FreeOblig` for a free of frame local 1 when FreeCompat holds.\\n\\n6. **Strength of statements against L4.**\\n   - `r6_alloc` now fixes the token to `ptok pr`.\\n   - `r6_free` now takes the FreeCompatInst implication instead of FreeSound.\\n   - The `hp : RootPlace` hypothesis of `freeSound_derived` matches O13 precondition 1 (OwnedRoot), and `r6_free` derives it.\\n   - No statement is stronger or weaker than L4.\\n   - Out of lens, not reported: the module header (MM23.lean lines 5–15) still says \\\"pass 1\\\" and lists transfer, store, issue, DDSound and pinned addresses as out of scope.\"},\"verdicts\":[]},{\"lens\":\"L6\",\"review\":{\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"L6-1\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"location\":\"formal/Ern/MM23.lean:2459-2477 (regionProv, regionAddr, ptrBytes, issueOps, storeOps); pointer_sound_issue 2585-2593 and pointer_sound_store 2559-2566 (hypothesis `hl : _.head? = some l`)\",\"cause\":\"formalization error. The issue part goes against what L6 fixes. For store with an empty footprint the brief does not define the address, and that case is not in the report.\",\"claim\":\"The pointer's provenance and address are taken from the head of the region list. For an empty region, which MM-03 accepts for issue and (via split) for store, the definitions write a pointer with address 0 and provenance none. For issue, L6 sets the provenance to the allocation of the arena storage, so this provenance is wrong. pointer_sound_issue and pointer_sound_store exclude exactly this case with the hypothesis `hl`, so no theorem shows the loss.\",\"evidence\":\"Brief L6: \\\"issue ↦ WriteStep of ptrBytes of the block on dst range (prov: allocation of arena storage)\\\". File /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review/L6/IssueRegion.lean, checked with exit=0 and no messages. It shows: `Step3 KS (.issue 0 5 [] 7) x9 y10` is ok; `regionAddr n9 L [] = 0 ∧ regionProv L [] = none ∧ (L 4).alloc = 4 ∧ LiveAlloc n9 4`, where 4 is the arena storage allocation; r6_issue holds; `rangeBytes (exec n9 (issueOps pe n9 L [] 7)) L 7 = some ((List.range 8).map fun _ =&gt; .init 0 none)`; block authority 9 is active, held by 7, with footprint []. File /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review/L6/StoreEmpty.lean, exit=0. It shows: `split 6 [[]]` is ok and gives authority 10 with footprint [] (MM-03.3 O2 allows zero-size sub-regions: \\\"La construction de sous-régions de taille nulle...\\\"); `store 10 8` is ok; regionAddr = 0 and regionProv = none; r6_store holds; leaf 8 receives eight `.init 0 none` bytes. Report question (e) 2 mentions only the issue case, as an open question, although L6 already fixes the provenance.\"},{\"id\":\"L6-2\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"location\":\"formal/Ern/MM23.lean:2452-2461 (regionAddr, regionProv), used by ptrBytes, storeOps and issueOps, and certified by pointer_sound_issue and pointer_sound_store\",\"cause\":\"formalization error. The brief's parenthetical \\\"(base + off of first leaf)\\\" is read silently as \\\"head of the List\\\". The report (c) 10 does not discuss list order or field order.\",\"claim\":\"The pointer address is base plus offset of the head of the List that represents the region. In the spec the region is a Set, and K1 fixes no field order. So the same block gets different addresses depending on list order or layout, and the add\n... (truncated 42958 chars, full result in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/tasks/wdps7v5g5.output)</result>\n<diagnostics>Per-agent results: /Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/subagents/workflows/wf_ad77d6e4-e1d/journal.jsonl — one {\"type\":\"result\",...} line per completed agent with its full return value.\nIf the result above is empty or unexpected, Read this file BEFORE diagnosing — do not assume agents returned non-empty results.\nTo re-run with edited post-processing: Workflow({scriptPath: '/Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/workflows/scripts/mm23-p2-review-wf_ad77d6e4-e1d.js', resumeFromRunId: 'wf_ad77d6e4-e1d'}) — agents whose (prompt, opts) are unchanged replay from cache.</diagnostics>\n<usage><agent_count>9</agent_count><agents_done>9</agents_done><agents_error>0</agents_error><agents_skipped>0</agents_skipped><agents_empty_result>0</agents_empty_result><subagent_tokens>1453591</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>217</tool_uses><duration_ms>1069927</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
