{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-31T23:20:26.740Z","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>w9ztvw6fy</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01XeszgKhHcaBDVEx5RMvyV7</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/tasks/w9ztvw6fy.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Dynamic workflow \"Second targeted check of the MM23 pass-2 review fixes, report facts and completeness, with refutation\" completed</summary>\n<result>[{\"lens\":\"FIX\",\"review\":{\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"FIX-1\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"formal/Ern/MM23.lean:2543-2546 (docstring of r6_issue)\",\"claim\":\"fe0bd8c changed the statement of r6_issue from `ptrBytes` to `issueBytes` but did not update its docstring. The docstring still says the write is \\\"with `ptrBytes` of the block\\\". `ptrBytes pe s2 L region` carries provenance `regionProv L region`, while the statement writes `issueBytes`, whose provenance is `arenaProv`. The two differ on an `ok` issue: for the empty block, `ptrBytes` has no provenance and `issueBytes` has the storage allocation. So the docstring names bytes that the theorem does not write.\",\"evidence\":\"Docstring at fe0bd8c: \\\"R6 for `issue` (MM-03.3 §9.2, O18; L6: `WriteStep` of the range of the destination with `ptrBytes` of the block; ...)\\\". The statement has `hdec : ObW.dec s2 (leafAcc s2 L .write dst) (issueBytes pe s2 L s3 i region)` and concludes on `issueOps pe s2 L s3 i region dst`. Lean check /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review2/fixes/a.lean: `example : (ptrBytes pe n9 L [] 0).2 = none ∧ (issueBytes pe n9 L x9 0 [] 0).2 = some 4 := by decide` compiles with no error. The issue of `[]` in x9 is `ok` and extends the SimRun of CaseSim (c.lean, theorem `ri`, compiles).\"},{\"id\":\"FIX-2\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"formal/Ern/MM23.lean:2456-2459 (docstring of regionAddr, added in fe0bd8c)\",\"claim\":\"The new sentence \\\"It is the first byte of the region when that leaf has the lowest offset\\\" is false when that leaf has size zero, which K1 (d) allows. The head leaf can have the lowest offset and an empty range. `regionAddr` then names an address that is no byte of the region, and the first byte of the region is higher. The report's question (e) 3 leaves this case open (\\\"Et que faire d'une feuille de taille nulle placée avant les autres ?\\\"), but the docstring states it as settled.\",\"evidence\":\"Lean check /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review2/fixes/a.lean, with `Lz := fun q =&gt; if q = 5 then ⟨4, 0, 0⟩ else L q`. All of the following compile with no error: `LayoutWF Lz x9 n9 ∧ ReprB π.tok π.ptok pvA Lz x9 n9`; `(Lz 5).off &lt; (Lz 6).off ∧ (Lz 5).len = 0 ∧ regionAddr n9 Lz [5, 6] = 104`; `∀ x &lt; 130, (∃ l ∈ [5, 6], leafAddr n9 Lz l ≤ x ∧ x &lt; leafAddr n9 Lz l + (Lz l).len) ↔ (112 ≤ x ∧ x &lt; 120)`, so the region's bytes start at 112, not 104; and `Step3 KS (.issue 0 5 [5, 6] 7) x9 ...`, so the issue of `[5, 6]` is `ok` in the reached state x9. The first error the file reported came from a recursion-depth limit, which shows the checker does report failures.\"}],\"checked\":\"Lens: the fixes of fe0bd8c, from `git diff 579808d fe0bd8c -- formal/Ern/MM23.lean`. Read against the brief task_mm23_p2.md (L6), MM-03.3 O2 and O18, and the MM03 definitions (Arena, ArenaInv, ArenasInv, IssueStatic, IssueStep, IssueAt, reachable_access_invariant_underDD).\\n\\nWhat holds, with no finding:\\n- `arenaProv`, `issueBytes`, `issueOps`, `assoc` for `.issue` and `r6_issue` say what L6 says: the provenance of `issue` is the allocation of the arena storage. Under `LayoutWF` every leaf of the storage is in one allocation. A missing entry is irrelevant because `IssueAt` rejects it.\\n- For non-empty blocks, `issue_prov_storage` shows the new provenance equals the old one (the allocation of the first leaf). It changes no verdict.\\n- For the empty block, the provenance changes from none to the storage allocation. L6 fixes the provenance without excluding empty blocks, so this follows L6. The address 0, which L6 leaves undefined, is unchanged and is flagged as question (e) 2.\\n- `ArenasInv` is needed: without `ArenaInv`, the footprint of `internal` need not match the storage. It is `(reachable_access_invariant_underDD hdd h).2.2` (under `DDSound k`, like WF3/NoDangling/FpLeaves), and `CaseSim.inv` uses it.\\n- `issue_prov_storage` and `pointer_sound_issue` say what their docstrings say. `#print axioms` on `issue_prov_storage`, `pointer_sound_issue`, `r6_issue`, `simulation` and `CaseSim.inv` gives only `[propext, Quot.sound]` (d.lean).\\n- The docstrings of `r6_transfer`, `simulation`, `pointer_sound_store`, `pointer_sound_issue` and the module header match their statements. `Op3` has 19 constructors, each covered by an R6 theorem.\\n\\nCaseSim witnesses, re-checked by extending the SimRun:\\n- The empty-block issue witness and the split `[[]]` then `store 10 8` witness both extend the SimRun of the case (c.lean: `ri`, `re`, `rs`).\\n- `L0`: I rebuilt the run with `π0 := {π with L := L0}` from x0 to x11 (b.lean, `r0`..`r11` compile). The witness's claims hold on that run's own MM-02 state, so the state is really reached.\\n- `x10e`: the split does create authority 10 (`x10.A.length = 10 ∧ x10e.A.length = 11`).\\n- The `[6, 5]` and `Lsw` witnesses prove exactly what their docstrings claim.\\n\\nNot checked:\\n- Whether `ArenasInv` holds on reached states without `DDSound`, so the docstring wording \\\"true on the reached states\\\" (which drops `DDSound`) is not assessed.\\n- The report text outside its summary of the fixes.\\n\\nThe repository is unmodified (`git status` is clean). All experiment files are under /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review2/fixes/.\"},\"verdicts\":[{\"id\":\"FIX-1\",\"real\":true,\"severity\":\"minor\",\"reason\":\"fe0bd8c changed r6_issue from `ptrBytes` to `issueBytes` (the report says so: \\\"`r6_issue` est inchangé hors du passage de `ptrBytes` à `issueBytes`\\\"). The docstring at formal/Ern/MM23.lean:2543-2544 was not updated and still names the Lean definition `ptrBytes`. `ptrBytes` takes provenance `regionProv L region`; the statement writes `issueBytes`, which takes `arenaProv L s3 i`. The brief's L6 text does say \\\"WriteStep of ptrBytes of the block on dst range (prov: allocation of arena storage)\\\", but the docstring leaves out the provenance qualifier, and that qualifier is exactly what the fix changed. The two byte functions differ on an `ok` issue of the empty block. The docstrings of issueOps and issueBytes are correct. Only the r6_issue docstring is stale, so this is documentation only and minor.\",\"evidence\":\"`git show 579808d:formal/Ern/MM23.lean` lines 2524-2525 and the current lines 2543-2544 have the same docstring: \\\"R6 for `issue` (MM-03.3 §9.2, O18; L6: `WriteStep` of the range of the destination with `ptrBytes` of the block; ...\\\". The fe0bd8c diff changes only the statement: `hdec : ObW.dec s2 (leafAcc s2 L .write dst) (issueBytes pe s2 L s3 i region)` and `issueOps pe s2 L s3 i region dst`. I reran the check in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review2/refute_fix/a.lean. `example : (ptrBytes pe n9 L [] 0).2 = none ∧ (issueBytes pe n9 L x9 0 [] 0).2 = some 4 := by decide` compiles and the file exits 0. Negative control in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review2/refute_fix/neg.lean: `example : (issueBytes pe n9 L x9 0 [] 0).2 = none := by decide` fails with \\\"Tactic `decide` proved that the proposition ... is false\\\".\"},{\"id\":\"FIX-2\",\"real\":true,\"severity\":\"minor\",\"reason\":\"The sentence added to regionAddr in fe0bd8c, \\\"It is the first byte of the region when that leaf has the lowest offset\\\", states as settled a case that report (e) 3 leaves open (\\\"Et que faire d'une feuille de taille nulle placée avant les autres ?\\\"). The statement is false when the head leaf has the lowest offset but size zero, which K1 (d) allows and the module's LayoutWF accepts. A size-zero leaf contributes no byte, so regionAddr names an address that is no byte of the region, and the region's first byte is higher. The definition itself does what L6 says (\\\"base + off of first leaf\\\"). Only the docstring claim is wrong, so this is minor.\",\"evidence\":\"I re\n... (truncated 30162 chars, full result in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/tasks/w9ztvw6fy.output)</result>\n<diagnostics>Per-agent results: /Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/subagents/workflows/wf_4fc48b1e-eb2/journal.jsonl — one {\"type\":\"result\",...} line per completed agent with its full return value.\nIf the result above is empty or unexpected, Read this file BEFORE diagnosing — do not assume agents returned non-empty results.\nTo re-run with edited post-processing: Workflow({scriptPath: '/Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/workflows/scripts/mm23-p2-second-check-wf_4fc48b1e-eb2.js', resumeFromRunId: 'wf_4fc48b1e-eb2'}) — agents whose (prompt, opts) are unchanged replay from cache.</diagnostics>\n<usage><agent_count>6</agent_count><agents_done>6</agents_done><agents_error>0</agents_error><agents_skipped>0</agents_skipped><agents_empty_result>0</agents_empty_result><subagent_tokens>974220</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>181</tool_uses><duration_ms>950361</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
