{"parentUuid":"ee112ea9-edb6-4d89-84f2-d9f143657633","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgcfZrW6H2V9djn7B6Mf8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Runs named; the MM3-H module rebuilds. Writing `Ern/MM03/LockOptions.lean`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15497,"cache_read_input_tokens":694016,"output_tokens":6209,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":24},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15497,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6209,"cache_read_input_tokens":694016,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15497,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15497},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d514f7b9-1a72-4324-978d-b4782324a6b1","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgcfZrAkpot3T5Qhx8JLs","requestRef":"fc7ca6f0-66ae-4a2f-80ae-13662e071546","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"2a21fddf-0ad1-40cd-b596-5e6ec93cfab4","timestamp":"2026-11-01T18:16:26.807Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/validation_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
{"parentUuid":"2a21fddf-0ad1-40cd-b596-5e6ec93cfab4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgcfZrW6H2V9djn7B6Mf8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DysUHts8rb1EjgbRyjBvL8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/MM03/LockOptions.lean","content":"import Ern.MM03.Horrors\n\n/-!\n# Measure of the `NoLock` options (jalon 3, step 4)\n\nThe options of the jalon-3 material (`ERN_Jalon3_materiel.md` v2, §5), measured on the kernel as it\nis (option 1, no rule), without modifying it:\n\n* option 2, a local rule: an operation does not place an authority into a place it covers\n  (`SelfLock`); `store` already rejects it (O8.3), so the rule is measured on `transfer` and\n  `issue` (`opt2`);\n* option 3, `NoLock`: no self-lock, as a separate clause, and the relation \"`b` blocks `a`\"\n  (`Blocks`) acyclic, checked on the arrival state of `transfer`, `issue` and `store` (`opt3`).\n\nFor each case of the list \"doit être accepté\" of §5 (H11, H19, H29b, H35 to H37, H44 to H47, W1\nto W3) and for H49 to H51, `decisions` gives the decision of an option on each `transfer`, `issue`\nand `store` of the run of the case (`Ern.MM03.Horrors`), decided on the state where the step runs;\n`true` is acceptance. The cost: option 2 is decided from the authorities the operation moves and the\nplaces that receive them (`opt2_transfer_local`); option 3 is not, the decision depends on\nauthorities the operation does not touch (`opt3_not_local`). No option is adopted (material §5:\n\"la décision revient à l'arbitrage\").\n-/\n\nnamespace Ern.MM03.LockOptions\n\nopen Ern.MM03 Ern.HandlePool Ern.MM03.Horrors\n\n/-! ## Option 2: self-lock -/\n\n/-- Self-lock of the authority `a` (material §5, options 2 and 3): `a` is active and held by a place\none of whose leaves it covers. -/\ndef SelfLock (s : S3) (a : Nat) : Prop :=\n  OptP (s.A[a]?) (fun y => y.active = true ∧ match y.holder with\n    | .place p => ∃ l ∈ y.footprint, l ∈ footprint s.P p\n    | .frame _ => False) False\n\ninstance (s : S3) (a : Nat) : Decidable (SelfLock s a) := by\n  unfold SelfLock OptP; split\n  · rename_i y _; cases y.holder <;> infer_instance\n  · infer_instance\n\n/-- Option 2 on `transfer src dst` (material §5): no authority moved by the transfer, one held within\nthe source, is self-locked in the arrival state. -/\ndef Opt2Transfer (s : S3) (src dst : Nat) : Prop :=\n  ∀ j ∈ List.range s.A.length, OptP (s.A[j]?) (fun y => heldIn s.P src y.holder) False →\n    ¬ SelfLock (transferEff s src dst) j\n\ninstance (s : S3) (src dst : Nat) : Decidable (Opt2Transfer s src dst) := by\n  unfold Opt2Transfer; infer_instance\n\n/-- Option 2 on `issue` of `region` to `dst` (material §5): the block, the new authority, is not\nself-locked in the arrival state. -/\ndef Opt2Issue (s : S3) (ar : Arena) (region : List Nat) (dst : Nat) : Prop :=\n  ¬ SelfLock (issueEff s ar region dst).1 s.A.length\n\ninstance (s : S3) (ar : Arena) (region : List Nat) (dst : Nat) :\n    Decidable (Opt2Issue s ar region dst) := by\n  unfold Opt2Issue; infer_instance\n\n/-! ## Option 3: `NoLock` -/\n\n/-- \"`b` bloque `a`\" (material §5, option 3): `b ≠ a`, both active, and the footprint of `b` contains\na leaf of the holder of `a`. -/\ndef Blocks (s : S3) (b a : Nat) : Prop :=\n  b ≠ a ∧ s.Active b ∧ s.Active a ∧ OptP (s.A[a]?) (fun y => match y.holder with\n    | .place p => ∃ l ∈ s.afp b, l ∈ footprint s.P p\n    | .frame _ => False) False\n\ninstance (s : S3) (b a : Nat) : Decidable (Blocks s b a) := by\n  unfold Blocks OptP; split\n  · rename_i y _; cases y.holder <;> infer_instance\n  · infer_instance\n\n/-- The authorities blocked by one of `xs`. -/\ndef blockedBy (s : S3) (xs : List Nat) : List Nat :=\n  (List.range s.A.length).filter fun a => decide (∃ b ∈ xs, Blocks s b a)\n\n/-- The authorities reached from `xs` by at most `n` steps of `Blocks`, `xs` included. -/\ndef blockReach (s : S3) : Nat → List Nat → List Nat\n  | 0, xs => xs\n  | n + 1, xs => blockReach s n (xs ++ blockedBy s xs)\n\n/-- Acyclicity of `Blocks` (material §5, option 3): no authority is reached from itself by one or\nmore steps. Every step leads to an authority of `A`, so a cycle has at most `A.length` steps and the\nsearch with that bound is complete (report, (f)). -/\ndef BlocksAcyclic (s : S3) : Prop :=\n  ∀ a ∈ List.range s.A.length, a ∉ blockReach s s.A.length (blockedBy s [a])\n\ninstance (s : S3) : Decidable (BlocksAcyclic s) := by unfold BlocksAcyclic; infer_instance\n\n/-- `NoLock` (material §5, option 3): no self-lock (separate clause) and `Blocks` acyclic. -/\ndef NoLock (s : S3) : Prop :=\n  (∀ a ∈ List.range s.A.length, ¬ SelfLock s a) ∧ BlocksAcyclic s\n\ninstance (s : S3) : Decidable (NoLock s) := by unfold NoLock; infer_instance\n\n/-! ## Decisions along the runs -/\n\n/-- Option 2 on an operation from the extended state `ps` (`true`: accepted by the rule). Only\n`transfer` and `issue` are checked; `store` is left to O8.3. -/\ndef opt2 (ps : PS) : Op → Bool\n  | .transfer src dst => decide (Opt2Transfer ps.s src dst)\n  | .issue i _ region dst =>\n    match ps.s.arenas[i]? with\n    | some ar => decide (Opt2Issue ps.s ar region dst)\n    | none => true\n  | _ => true\n\n/-- Option 3 on an operation from `ps` (`true`: accepted by the rule): `NoLock` of the arrival\nstate of `transfer`, `issue` and `store`. -/\ndef opt3 (ps : PS) : Op → Bool\n  | .transfer src dst => decide (NoLock (transferEff ps.s src dst))\n  | .issue i _ region dst =>\n    match ps.s.arenas[i]? with\n    | some ar => decide (NoLock (arenaSet (issueEff ps.s ar region dst).1 i\n        (issueEff ps.s ar region dst).2))\n    | none => true\n  | .store a p => decide (NoLock (storeEff ps.s a p))\n  | _ => true\n\n/-- The operations checked by the options: `transfer`, `issue`, `store`. -/\ndef checked : Op → Bool\n  | .transfer .. => true\n  | .issue .. => true\n  | .store .. => true\n  | _ => false\n\n/-- The decisions of the option `D` on the checked steps of a run of `K0` from `ps`, each on the\nstate where the step runs, in order, as long as the steps are `ok` in the kernel. -/\ndef decisions (D : PS → Op → Bool) (ps : PS) : List Op → List Bool\n  | [] => []\n  | o :: os =>\n    match pexec K0 ps o with\n    | some ps' => (if checked o then [D ps o] else []) ++ decisions D ps' os\n    | none => []\n\n/-- The run from `S3.init []` of a case. -/\ndef dec2 (os : List Op) : List Bool := decisions opt2 (PS.init []) os\ndef dec3 (os : List Op) : List Bool := decisions opt3 (PS.init []) os\n\n/-! ## Cases that must be accepted (material §5) -/\n\n/-- The runs of the cases that must be accepted, with their names: each is a run of\n`Ern.MM03.Horrors` reached under `K0`, except H21's arena which is not on the list. -/\ndef mustAccept : List (String × List Op) :=\n  [(\"H11\", h11p ++ [.endUse 3, .endUse 6, .reset 0 0]),\n   (\"H19\", h19p ++ [.endUse 2, .reset 0 0]),\n   (\"H29b\", h29bo), (\"H35\", h35o), (\"H36\", h36o), (\"H37\", h37o), (\"H44\", h44o),\n   (\"H45\", h45o), (\"H46\", h46o), (\"H47\", h47o), (\"W1\", w1o),\n   (\"W2\", w2o ++ [.release 12, .release 11, .release 10, .transfer 9 16, .transfer 12 19]),\n   (\"W3\", w3o ++ [.endUse 5, .endUse 2, .endUse 3, .endUse 4, .reset 0 0, .issue 0 0 [10] 2]),\n   (\"W3v\", w3vo ++ [.endUse 2, .reset 0 0, .issue 0 0 [7] 3])]\n\n/-- Every run of the list is `ok` in the kernel at each step, so the decisions cover all its\nchecked steps. -/\ntheorem mustAccept_runs : mustAccept.all (fun c => (prun K0 (PS.init []) c.2).isSome) = true := by\n  decide\n\n/-- The decisions of option 2 on the checked steps of each case. -/\ntheorem opt2_decisions : mustAccept.map (fun c => (c.1, dec2 c.2)) =\n    [(\"H11\", [true, true, true, true]), (\"H19\", [true]), (\"H29b\", [true]), (\"H35\", []),\n     (\"H36\", []), (\"H37\", [true]), (\"H44\", [true]), (\"H45\", [true, true, true, true]),\n     (\"H46\", [true]), (\"H47\", [true]), (\"W1\", []), (\"W2\", [true, true]),\n     (\"W3\", [true, true, true, true, true, true, true]), (\"W3v\", [true, true, true, true])] := by\n  decide\n\n/-- The decisions of option 3 on the checked steps of each case. -/\ntheorem opt3_decisions : mustAccept.map (fun c => (c.1, dec3 c.2)) =\n    [(\"H11\", [true, true, true, true]), (\"H19\", [true]), (\"H29b\", [true]), (\"H35\", []),\n     (\"H36\", []), (\"H37\", [true]), (\"H44\", [true]), (\"H45\", [true, true, true, true]),\n     (\"H46\", [true]), (\"H47\", [true]), (\"W1\", []), (\"W2\", [true, true]),\n     (\"W3\", [true, true, true, true, true, true, true]), (\"W3v\", [true, true, true, true])] := by\n  decide\n\n/-- No false rejection (material §5, criterion): neither option rejects a checked step of a case that\nmust be accepted. -/\ntheorem no_false_rejection : mustAccept.all (fun c => (dec2 c.2).all id && (dec3 c.2).all id) =\n    true := by\n  decide\n\n/-! ## Residual blockings (H49 to H51) -/\n\n/-- H49 (the cycle closed through a helper then its `release`): option 2 accepts every checked step,\nso the blocking of H49 remains; option 3 rejects the `store` that closes the cycle (the 7th checked\nstep), the helper notwithstanding. -/\ntheorem H49_options : dec2 h49o = [true, true, true, true] ∧\n    dec3 h49o = [true, true, true, false] := by\n  decide\n\n/-- The state and the step of H49 where option 3 rejects: `store 8 6` with the helper 9 active; in\nits arrival state, 7 and 8 block each other. -/\ntheorem H49_cycle : Blocks (storeEff (run K0 [] (h48o ++ [.derive 7 6 .modify])).s 8 6) 7 8 ∧\n    Blocks (storeEff (run K0 [] (h48o ++ [.derive 7 6 .modify])).s 8 6) 8 7 :=\n  by decide\n\n/-- H50 (an authority transferred or issued into the place it covers): both options reject the\n`transfer` and the `issue`, by the self-lock. -/\ntheorem H50_options : dec2 h50ao = [true, false] ∧ dec3 h50ao = [true, false] ∧\n    dec2 h50bo = [false] ∧ dec3 h50bo = [false] := by\n  decide\n\n/-- H51 (an element of a storage owned by `v` holds a view on `v`): option 2 does not check `store`,\nso the blocking remains; option 3 rejects the `store`: in its arrival state, the root of the storage,\nheld by `v`, and the view, held by the element, block each other. -/\ntheorem H51_options : dec2 h51o = [true] ∧ dec3 h51o = [false] ∧\n    Blocks (storeEff (run K0 [] (h51o.take 6)).s 4 3) 2 4 ∧\n    Blocks (storeEff (run K0 [] (h51o.take 6)).s 4 3) 4 2 := by\n  decide\n\n/-! ## Cost of the check -/\n\n/-- Locality of option 2 on `transfer`: the decision depends on the state only through the places and\nthe authorities held within the source, the ones the transfer moves. Two states with the same places\nand the same such authorities, at the same identities, get the same decision. -/\ntheorem opt2_transfer_local {s s' : S3} {src dst : Nat} (hP : s'.P = s.P)\n    (hA : ∀ j y, (s.A[j]? = some y ∨ s'.A[j]? = some y) → heldIn s.P src y.holder →\n      s'.A[j]? = s.A[j]?) :\n    Opt2Transfer s' src dst ↔ Opt2Transfer s src dst := by\n  have key : ∀ (t t' : S3), t'.P = t.P →\n      (∀ j y, (t.A[j]? = some y ∨ t'.A[j]? = some y) → heldIn t.P src y.holder →\n        t'.A[j]? = t.A[j]?) → Opt2Transfer t src dst → Opt2Transfer t' src dst := by\n    intro t t' hP hA h j hj hheld hsl\n    obtain ⟨y, hy, hh⟩ := optP_false_iff.1 hheld\n    rw [hP] at hh\n    have e := hA j y (.inr hy) hh\n    have hj' : j < t.A.length := lt_of_getElem? (e ▸ hy)\n    refine h j (List.mem_range.2 hj') (optP_false_iff.2 ⟨y, e ▸ hy, hh⟩) ?_\n    have ga : (transferEff t' src dst).A[j]? = (transferEff t src dst).A[j]? := by\n      rw [transfer_A_get, transfer_A_get, e, hP]\n    unfold SelfLock at hsl ⊢\n    rw [ga] at hsl\n    have gp : (transferEff t' src dst).P = (transferEff t src dst).P := by\n      simp only [transferEff, hP, ← e]\n      congr 1\n    rw [gp] at hsl\n    exact hsl\n  refine ⟨key s' s ?_ ?_, key s s' hP hA⟩\n  · exact hP.symm\n  · intro j y hy hh\n    rw [hP] at hh ⊢\n    exact (hA j y hy.symm (hP ▸ hh)).symm\n\n/-- Option 2 on `issue` reads only the region and the destination: the block is self-locked exactly\nwhen the destination's footprint meets the region. -/\ntheorem opt2_issue_local (s : S3) (ar : Arena) (region : List Nat) (dst : Nat) :\n    Opt2Issue s ar region dst ↔ ¬ ∃ l ∈ region, l ∈ footprint s.P dst := by\n  unfold Opt2Issue SelfLock\n  simp only [issueEff, S3.addAuth, List.getElem?_append_right (Nat.le_refl _), Nat.sub_self,\n    List.getElem?_cons_zero, OptP, true_and]\n\n/-- Option 3 is not local: from two reached states that agree on the authority stored, 8 (same\nentry), on the target 6 (same footprint) and on the number of authorities, the `store 8 6` gets\ndifferent decisions. They differ on the authority 7, which the step does not touch: stored into the\nnode 5 in the first (H48), held by the frame in the second (its twin). -/\ntheorem opt3_not_local :\n    PReach K0 [] h48 ∧ PReach K0 [] h48t ∧ h48.s.A[8]? = h48t.s.A[8]? ∧\n    footprint h48.s.P 6 = footprint h48t.s.P 6 ∧ h48.s.A.length = h48t.s.A.length ∧\n    h48.s.A[7]? ≠ h48t.s.A[7]? ∧\n    ¬ NoLock (storeEff h48.s 8 6) ∧ NoLock (storeEff h48t.s 8 6) :=\n  ⟨H48.1, H48.2.2.1, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide⟩\n\nend Ern.MM03.LockOptions\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15497,"cache_read_input_tokens":694016,"output_tokens":6209,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":24},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15497,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6209,"cache_read_input_tokens":694016,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15497,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15497},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01DysUHts8rb1EjgbRyjBvL8":{"file_path":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/MM03/LockOptions.lean","content":"import Ern.MM03.Horrors\n\n/-!\n# Measure of the `NoLock` options (jalon 3, step 4)\n\nThe options of the jalon-3 material (`ERN_Jalon3_materiel.md` v2, §5), measured on the kernel as it\nis (option 1, no rule), without modifying it:\n\n* option 2, a local rule: an operation does not place an authority into a place it covers\n  (`SelfLock`); `store` already rejects it (O8.3), so the rule is measured on `transfer` and\n  `issue` (`opt2`);\n* option 3, `NoLock`: no self-lock, as a separate clause, and the relation \"`b` blocks `a`\"\n  (`Blocks`) acyclic, checked on the arrival state of `transfer`, `issue` and `store` (`opt3`).\n\nFor each case of the list \"doit être accepté\" of §5 (H11, H19, H29b, H35 to H37, H44 to H47, W1\nto W3) and for H49 to H51, `decisions` gives the decision of an option on each `transfer`, `issue`\nand `store` of the run of the case (`Ern.MM03.Horrors`), decided on the state where the step runs;\n`true` is acceptance. The cost: option 2 is decided from the authorities the operation moves and the\nplaces that receive them (`opt2_transfer_local`); option 3 is not, the decision depends on\nauthorities the operation does not touch (`opt3_not_local`). No option is adopted (material §5:\n\"la décision revient à l'arbitrage\").\n-/\n\nnamespace Ern.MM03.LockOptions\n\nopen Ern.MM03 Ern.HandlePool Ern.MM03.Horrors\n\n/-! ## Option 2: self-lock -/\n\n/-- Self-lock of the authority `a` (material §5, options 2 and 3): `a` is active and held by a place\none of whose leaves it covers. -/\ndef SelfLock (s : S3) (a : Nat) : Prop :=\n  OptP (s.A[a]?) (fun y => y.active = true ∧ match y.holder with\n    | .place p => ∃ l ∈ y.footprint, l ∈ footprint s.P p\n    | .frame _ => False) False\n\ninstance (s : S3) (a : Nat) : Decidable (SelfLock s a) := by\n  unfold SelfLock OptP; split\n  · rename_i y _; cases y.holder <;> infer_instance\n  · infer_instance\n\n/-- Option 2 on `transfer src dst` (material §5): no authority moved by the transfer, one held within\nthe source, is self-locked in the arrival state. -/\ndef Opt2Transfer (s : S3) (src dst : Nat) : Prop :=\n  ∀ j ∈ List.range s.A.length, OptP (s.A[j]?) (fun y => heldIn s.P src y.holder) False →\n    ¬ SelfLock (transferEff s src dst) j\n\ninstance (s : S3) (src dst : Nat) : Decidable (Opt2Transfer s src dst) := by\n  unfold Opt2Transfer; infer_instance\n\n/-- Option 2 on `issue` of `region` to `dst` (material §5): the block, the new authority, is not\nself-locked in the arrival state. -/\ndef Opt2Issue (s : S3) (ar : Arena) (region : List Nat) (dst : Nat) : Prop :=\n  ¬ SelfLock (issueEff s ar region dst).1 s.A.length\n\ninstance (s : S3) (ar : Arena) (region : List Nat) (dst : Nat) :\n    Decidable (Opt2Issue s ar region dst) := by\n  unfold Opt2Issue; infer_instance\n\n/-! ## Option 3: `NoLock` -/\n\n/-- \"`b` bloque `a`\" (material §5, option 3): `b ≠ a`, both active, and the footprint of `b` contains\na leaf of the holder of `a`. -/\ndef Blocks (s : S3) (b a : Nat) : Prop :=\n  b ≠ a ∧ s.Active b ∧ s.Active a ∧ OptP (s.A[a]?) (fun y => match y.holder with\n    | .place p => ∃ l ∈ s.afp b, l ∈ footprint s.P p\n    | .frame _ => False) False\n\ninstance (s : S3) (b a : Nat) : Decidable (Blocks s b a) := by\n  unfold Blocks OptP; split\n  · rename_i y _; cases y.holder <;> infer_instance\n  · infer_instance\n\n/-- The authorities blocked by one of `xs`. -/\ndef blockedBy (s : S3) (xs : List Nat) : List Nat :=\n  (List.range s.A.length).filter fun a => decide (∃ b ∈ xs, Blocks s b a)\n\n/-- The authorities reached from `xs` by at most `n` steps of `Blocks`, `xs` included. -/\ndef blockReach (s : S3) : Nat → List Nat → List Nat\n  | 0, xs => xs\n  | n + 1, xs => blockReach s n (xs ++ blockedBy s xs)\n\n/-- Acyclicity of `Blocks` (material §5, option 3): no authority is reached from itself by one or\nmore steps. Every step leads to an authority of `A`, so a cycle has at most `A.length` steps and the\nsearch with that bound is complete (report, (f)). -/\ndef BlocksAcyclic (s : S3) : Prop :=\n  ∀ a ∈ List.range s.A.length, a ∉ blockReach s s.A.length (blockedBy s [a])\n\ninstance (s : S3) : Decidable (BlocksAcyclic s) := by unfold BlocksAcyclic; infer_instance\n\n/-- `NoLock` (material §5, option 3): no self-lock (separate clause) and `Blocks` acyclic. -/\ndef NoLock (s : S3) : Prop :=\n  (∀ a ∈ List.range s.A.length, ¬ SelfLock s a) ∧ BlocksAcyclic s\n\ninstance (s : S3) : Decidable (NoLock s) := by unfold NoLock; infer_instance\n\n/-! ## Decisions along the runs -/\n\n/-- Option 2 on an operation from the extended state `ps` (`true`: accepted by the rule). Only\n`transfer` and `issue` are checked; `store` is left to O8.3. -/\ndef opt2 (ps : PS) : Op → Bool\n  | .transfer src dst => decide (Opt2Transfer ps.s src dst)\n  | .issue i _ region dst =>\n    match ps.s.arenas[i]? with\n    | some ar => decide (Opt2Issue ps.s ar region dst)\n    | none => true\n  | _ => true\n\n/-- Option 3 on an operation from `ps` (`true`: accepted by the rule): `NoLock` of the arrival\nstate of `transfer`, `issue` and `store`. -/\ndef opt3 (ps : PS) : Op → Bool\n  | .transfer src dst => decide (NoLock (transferEff ps.s src dst))\n  | .issue i _ region dst =>\n    match ps.s.arenas[i]? with\n    | some ar => decide (NoLock (arenaSet (issueEff ps.s ar region dst).1 i\n        (issueEff ps.s ar region dst).2))\n    | none => true\n  | .store a p => decide (NoLock (storeEff ps.s a p))\n  | _ => true\n\n/-- The operations checked by the options: `transfer`, `issue`, `store`. -/\ndef checked : Op → Bool\n  | .transfer .. => true\n  | .issue .. => true\n  | .store .. => true\n  | _ => false\n\n/-- The decisions of the option `D` on the checked steps of a run of `K0` from `ps`, each on the\nstate where the step runs, in order, as long as the steps are `ok` in the kernel. -/\ndef decisions (D : PS → Op → Bool) (ps : PS) : List Op → List Bool\n  | [] => []\n  | o :: os =>\n    match pexec K0 ps o with\n    | some ps' => (if checked o then [D ps o] else []) ++ decisions D ps' os\n    | none => []\n\n/-- The run from `S3.init []` of a case. -/\ndef dec2 (os : List Op) : List Bool := decisions opt2 (PS.init []) os\ndef dec3 (os : List Op) : List Bool := decisions opt3 (PS.init []) os\n\n/-! ## Cases that must be accepted (material §5) -/\n\n/-- The runs of the cases that must be accepted, with their names: each is a run of\n`Ern.MM03.Horrors` reached under `K0`, except H21's arena which is not on the list. -/\ndef mustAccept : List (String × List Op) :=\n  [(\"H11\", h11p ++ [.endUse 3, .endUse 6, .reset 0 0]),\n   (\"H19\", h19p ++ [.endUse 2, .reset 0 0]),\n   (\"H29b\", h29bo), (\"H35\", h35o), (\"H36\", h36o), (\"H37\", h37o), (\"H44\", h44o),\n   (\"H45\", h45o), (\"H46\", h46o), (\"H47\", h47o), (\"W1\", w1o),\n   (\"W2\", w2o ++ [.release 12, .release 11, .release 10, .transfer 9 16, .transfer 12 19]),\n   (\"W3\", w3o ++ [.endUse 5, .endUse 2, .endUse 3, .endUse 4, .reset 0 0, .issue 0 0 [10] 2]),\n   (\"W3v\", w3vo ++ [.endUse 2, .reset 0 0, .issue 0 0 [7] 3])]\n\n/-- Every run of the list is `ok` in the kernel at each step, so the decisions cover all its\nchecked steps. -/\ntheorem mustAccept_runs : mustAccept.all (fun c => (prun K0 (PS.init []) c.2).isSome) = true := by\n  decide\n\n/-- The decisions of option 2 on the checked steps of each case. -/\ntheorem opt2_decisions : mustAccept.map (fun c => (c.1, dec2 c.2)) =\n    [(\"H11\", [true, true, true, true]), (\"H19\", [true]), (\"H29b\", [true]), (\"H35\", []),\n     (\"H36\", []), (\"H37\", [true]), (\"H44\", [true]), (\"H45\", [true, true, true, true]),\n     (\"H46\", [true]), (\"H47\", [true]), (\"W1\", []), (\"W2\", [true, true]),\n     (\"W3\", [true, true, true, true, true, true, true]), (\"W3v\", [true, true, true, true])] := by\n  decide\n\n/-- The decisions of option 3 on the checked steps of each case. -/\ntheorem opt3_decisions : mustAccept.map (fun c => (c.1, dec3 c.2)) =\n    [(\"H11\", [true, true, true, true]), (\"H19\", [true]), (\"H29b\", [true]), (\"H35\", []),\n     (\"H36\", []), (\"H37\", [true]), (\"H44\", [true]), (\"H45\", [true, true, true, true]),\n     (\"H46\", [true]), (\"H47\", [true]), (\"W1\", []), (\"W2\", [true, true]),\n     (\"W3\", [true, true, true, true, true, true, true]), (\"W3v\", [true, true, true, true])] := by\n  decide\n\n/-- No false rejection (material §5, criterion): neither option rejects a checked step of a case that\nmust be accepted. -/\ntheorem no_false_rejection : mustAccept.all (fun c => (dec2 c.2).all id && (dec3 c.2).all id) =\n    true := by\n  decide\n\n/-! ## Residual blockings (H49 to H51) -/\n\n/-- H49 (the cycle closed through a helper then its `release`): option 2 accepts every checked step,\nso the blocking of H49 remains; option 3 rejects the `store` that closes the cycle (the 7th checked\nstep), the helper notwithstanding. -/\ntheorem H49_options : dec2 h49o = [true, true, true, true] ∧\n    dec3 h49o = [true, true, true, false] := by\n  decide\n\n/-- The state and the step of H49 where option 3 rejects: `store 8 6` with the helper 9 active; in\nits arrival state, 7 and 8 block each other. -/\ntheorem H49_cycle : Blocks (storeEff (run K0 [] (h48o ++ [.derive 7 6 .modify])).s 8 6) 7 8 ∧\n    Blocks (storeEff (run K0 [] (h48o ++ [.derive 7 6 .modify])).s 8 6) 8 7 :=\n  by decide\n\n/-- H50 (an authority transferred or issued into the place it covers): both options reject the\n`transfer` and the `issue`, by the self-lock. -/\ntheorem H50_options : dec2 h50ao = [true, false] ∧ dec3 h50ao = [true, false] ∧\n    dec2 h50bo = [false] ∧ dec3 h50bo = [false] := by\n  decide\n\n/-- H51 (an element of a storage owned by `v` holds a view on `v`): option 2 does not check `store`,\nso the blocking remains; option 3 rejects the `store`: in its arrival state, the root of the storage,\nheld by `v`, and the view, held by the element, block each other. -/\ntheorem H51_options : dec2 h51o = [true] ∧ dec3 h51o = [false] ∧\n    Blocks (storeEff (run K0 [] (h51o.take 6)).s 4 3) 2 4 ∧\n    Blocks (storeEff (run K0 [] (h51o.take 6)).s 4 3) 4 2 := by\n  decide\n\n/-! ## Cost of the check -/\n\n/-- Locality of option 2 on `transfer`: the decision depends on the state only through the places and\nthe authorities held within the source, the ones the transfer moves. Two states with the same places\nand the same such authorities, at the same identities, get the same decision. -/\ntheorem opt2_transfer_local {s s' : S3} {src dst : Nat} (hP : s'.P = s.P)\n    (hA : ∀ j y, (s.A[j]? = some y ∨ s'.A[j]? = some y) → heldIn s.P src y.holder →\n      s'.A[j]? = s.A[j]?) :\n    Opt2Transfer s' src dst ↔ Opt2Transfer s src dst := by\n  have key : ∀ (t t' : S3), t'.P = t.P →\n      (∀ j y, (t.A[j]? = some y ∨ t'.A[j]? = some y) → heldIn t.P src y.holder →\n        t'.A[j]? = t.A[j]?) → Opt2Transfer t src dst → Opt2Transfer t' src dst := by\n    intro t t' hP hA h j hj hheld hsl\n    obtain ⟨y, hy, hh⟩ := optP_false_iff.1 hheld\n    rw [hP] at hh\n    have e := hA j y (.inr hy) hh\n    have hj' : j < t.A.length := lt_of_getElem? (e ▸ hy)\n    refine h j (List.mem_range.2 hj') (optP_false_iff.2 ⟨y, e ▸ hy, hh⟩) ?_\n    have ga : (transferEff t' src dst).A[j]? = (transferEff t src dst).A[j]? := by\n      rw [transfer_A_get, transfer_A_get, e, hP]\n    unfold SelfLock at hsl ⊢\n    rw [ga] at hsl\n    have gp : (transferEff t' src dst).P = (transferEff t src dst).P := by\n      simp only [transferEff, hP, ← e]\n      congr 1\n    rw [gp] at hsl\n    exact hsl\n  refine ⟨key s' s ?_ ?_, key s s' hP hA⟩\n  · exact hP.symm\n  · intro j y hy hh\n    rw [hP] at hh ⊢\n    exact (hA j y hy.symm (hP ▸ hh)).symm\n\n/-- Option 2 on `issue` reads only the region and the destination: the block is self-locked exactly\nwhen the destination's footprint meets the region. -/\ntheorem opt2_issue_local (s : S3) (ar : Arena) (region : List Nat) (dst : Nat) :\n    Opt2Issue s ar region dst ↔ ¬ ∃ l ∈ region, l ∈ footprint s.P dst := by\n  unfold Opt2Issue SelfLock\n  simp only [issueEff, S3.addAuth, List.getElem?_append_right (Nat.le_refl _), Nat.sub_self,\n    List.getElem?_cons_zero, OptP, true_and]\n\n/-- Option 3 is not local: from two reached states that agree on the authority stored, 8 (same\nentry), on the target 6 (same footprint) and on the number of authorities, the `store 8 6` gets\ndifferent decisions. They differ on the authority 7, which the step does not touch: stored into the\nnode 5 in the first (H48), held by the frame in the second (its twin). -/\ntheorem opt3_not_local :\n    PReach K0 [] h48 ∧ PReach K0 [] h48t ∧ h48.s.A[8]? = h48t.s.A[8]? ∧\n    footprint h48.s.P 6 = footprint h48t.s.P 6 ∧ h48.s.A.length = h48t.s.A.length ∧\n    h48.s.A[7]? ≠ h48t.s.A[7]? ∧\n    ¬ NoLock (storeEff h48.s 8 6) ∧ NoLock (storeEff h48t.s 8 6) :=\n  ⟨H48.1, H48.2.2.1, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide⟩\n\nend Ern.MM03.LockOptions\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"d514f7b9-1a72-4324-978d-b4782324a6b1","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgcfZrAkpot3T5Qhx8JLs","requestRef":"fc7ca6f0-66ae-4a2f-80ae-13662e071546","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"265265f2-e66d-4e96-8f25-cc293c8a8735","timestamp":"2026-11-01T18:17:13.201Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/validation_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
{"type":"file-history-delta","messageId":"265265f2-e66d-4e96-8f25-cc293c8a8735","snapshotMessageId":"7eafe96c-3b3c-4b36-b770-1b007ce8e182","trackingPath":"formal/Ern/MM03/LockOptions.lean","backup":{"backupFileName":null,"version":1,"backupTime":"2026-11-01T18:17:13.237Z","realParentDir":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/MM03"},"timestamp":"2026-11-01T18:17:13.242Z"}
{"parentUuid":"265265f2-e66d-4e96-8f25-cc293c8a8735","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d8867bcf-fa69-4463-9401-ce9d6d53950a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DysUHts8rb1EjgbRyjBvL8","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/MM03/LockOptions.lean (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"30c263e8-e0ad-49de-9c98-fba186b1d747","timestamp":"2026-11-01T18:17:13.248Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/MM03/LockOptions.lean","content":"import Ern.MM03.Horrors\n\n/-!\n# Measure of the `NoLock` options (jalon 3, step 4)\n\nThe options of the jalon-3 material (`ERN_Jalon3_materiel.md` v2, §5), measured on the kernel as it\nis (option 1, no rule), without modifying it:\n\n* option 2, a local rule: an operation does not place an authority into a place it covers\n  (`SelfLock`); `store` already rejects it (O8.3), so the rule is measured on `transfer` and\n  `issue` (`opt2`);\n* option 3, `NoLock`: no self-lock, as a separate clause, and the relation \"`b` blocks `a`\"\n  (`Blocks`) acyclic, checked on the arrival state of `transfer`, `issue` and `store` (`opt3`).\n\nFor each case of the list \"doit être accepté\" of §5 (H11, H19, H29b, H35 to H37, H44 to H47, W1\nto W3) and for H49 to H51, `decisions` gives the decision of an option on each `transfer`, `issue`\nand `store` of the run of the case (`Ern.MM03.Horrors`), decided on the state where the step runs;\n`true` is acceptance. The cost: option 2 is decided from the authorities the operation moves and the\nplaces that receive them (`opt2_transfer_local`); option 3 is not, the decision depends on\nauthorities the operation does not touch (`opt3_not_local`). No option is adopted (material §5:\n\"la décision revient à l'arbitrage\").\n-/\n\nnamespace Ern.MM03.LockOptions\n\nopen Ern.MM03 Ern.HandlePool Ern.MM03.Horrors\n\n/-! ## Option 2: self-lock -/\n\n/-- Self-lock of the authority `a` (material §5, options 2 and 3): `a` is active and held by a place\none of whose leaves it covers. -/\ndef SelfLock (s : S3) (a : Nat) : Prop :=\n  OptP (s.A[a]?) (fun y => y.active = true ∧ match y.holder with\n    | .place p => ∃ l ∈ y.footprint, l ∈ footprint s.P p\n    | .frame _ => False) False\n\ninstance (s : S3) (a : Nat) : Decidable (SelfLock s a) := by\n  unfold SelfLock OptP; split\n  · rename_i y _; cases y.holder <;> infer_instance\n  · infer_instance\n\n/-- Option 2 on `transfer src dst` (material §5): no authority moved by the transfer, one held within\nthe source, is self-locked in the arrival state. -/\ndef Opt2Transfer (s : S3) (src dst : Nat) : Prop :=\n  ∀ j ∈ List.range s.A.length, OptP (s.A[j]?) (fun y => heldIn s.P src y.holder) False →\n    ¬ SelfLock (transferEff s src dst) j\n\ninstance (s : S3) (src dst : Nat) : Decidable (Opt2Transfer s src dst) := by\n  unfold Opt2Transfer; infer_instance\n\n/-- Option 2 on `issue` of `region` to `dst` (material §5): the block, the new authority, is not\nself-locked in the arrival state. -/\ndef Opt2Issue (s : S3) (ar : Arena) (region : List Nat) (dst : Nat) : Prop :=\n  ¬ SelfLock (issueEff s ar region dst).1 s.A.length\n\ninstance (s : S3) (ar : Arena) (region : List Nat) (dst : Nat) :\n    Decidable (Opt2Issue s ar region dst) := by\n  unfold Opt2Issue; infer_instance\n\n/-! ## Option 3: `NoLock` -/\n\n/-- \"`b` bloque `a`\" (material §5, option 3): `b ≠ a`, both active, and the footprint of `b` contains\na leaf of the holder of `a`. -/\ndef Blocks (s : S3) (b a : Nat) : Prop :=\n  b ≠ a ∧ s.Active b ∧ s.Active a ∧ OptP (s.A[a]?) (fun y => match y.holder with\n    | .place p => ∃ l ∈ s.afp b, l ∈ footprint s.P p\n    | .frame _ => False) False\n\ninstance (s : S3) (b a : Nat) : Decidable (Blocks s b a) := by\n  unfold Blocks OptP; split\n  · rename_i y _; cases y.holder <;> infer_instance\n  · infer_instance\n\n/-- The authorities blocked by one of `xs`. -/\ndef blockedBy (s : S3) (xs : List Nat) : List Nat :=\n  (List.range s.A.length).filter fun a => decide (∃ b ∈ xs, Blocks s b a)\n\n/-- The authorities reached from `xs` by at most `n` steps of `Blocks`, `xs` included. -/\ndef blockReach (s : S3) : Nat → List Nat → List Nat\n  | 0, xs => xs\n  | n + 1, xs => blockReach s n (xs ++ blockedBy s xs)\n\n/-- Acyclicity of `Blocks` (material §5, option 3): no authority is reached from itself by one or\nmore steps. Every step leads to an authority of `A`, so a cycle has at most `A.length` steps and the\nsearch with that bound is complete (report, (f)). -/\ndef BlocksAcyclic (s : S3) : Prop :=\n  ∀ a ∈ List.range s.A.length, a ∉ blockReach s s.A.length (blockedBy s [a])\n\ninstance (s : S3) : Decidable (BlocksAcyclic s) := by unfold BlocksAcyclic; infer_instance\n\n/-- `NoLock` (material §5, option 3): no self-lock (separate clause) and `Blocks` acyclic. -/\ndef NoLock (s : S3) : Prop :=\n  (∀ a ∈ List.range s.A.length, ¬ SelfLock s a) ∧ BlocksAcyclic s\n\ninstance (s : S3) : Decidable (NoLock s) := by unfold NoLock; infer_instance\n\n/-! ## Decisions along the runs -/\n\n/-- Option 2 on an operation from the extended state `ps` (`true`: accepted by the rule). Only\n`transfer` and `issue` are checked; `store` is left to O8.3. -/\ndef opt2 (ps : PS) : Op → Bool\n  | .transfer src dst => decide (Opt2Transfer ps.s src dst)\n  | .issue i _ region dst =>\n    match ps.s.arenas[i]? with\n    | some ar => decide (Opt2Issue ps.s ar region dst)\n    | none => true\n  | _ => true\n\n/-- Option 3 on an operation from `ps` (`true`: accepted by the rule): `NoLock` of the arrival\nstate of `transfer`, `issue` and `store`. -/\ndef opt3 (ps : PS) : Op → Bool\n  | .transfer src dst => decide (NoLock (transferEff ps.s src dst))\n  | .issue i _ region dst =>\n    match ps.s.arenas[i]? with\n    | some ar => decide (NoLock (arenaSet (issueEff ps.s ar region dst).1 i\n        (issueEff ps.s ar region dst).2))\n    | none => true\n  | .store a p => decide (NoLock (storeEff ps.s a p))\n  | _ => true\n\n/-- The operations checked by the options: `transfer`, `issue`, `store`. -/\ndef checked : Op → Bool\n  | .transfer .. => true\n  | .issue .. => true\n  | .store .. => true\n  | _ => false\n\n/-- The decisions of the option `D` on the checked steps of a run of `K0` from `ps`, each on the\nstate where the step runs, in order, as long as the steps are `ok` in the kernel. -/\ndef decisions (D : PS → Op → Bool) (ps : PS) : List Op → List Bool\n  | [] => []\n  | o :: os =>\n    match pexec K0 ps o with\n    | some ps' => (if checked o then [D ps o] else []) ++ decisions D ps' os\n    | none => []\n\n/-- The run from `S3.init []` of a case. -/\ndef dec2 (os : List Op) : List Bool := decisions opt2 (PS.init []) os\ndef dec3 (os : List Op) : List Bool := decisions opt3 (PS.init []) os\n\n/-! ## Cases that must be accepted (material §5) -/\n\n/-- The runs of the cases that must be accepted, with their names: each is a run of\n`Ern.MM03.Horrors` reached under `K0`, except H21's arena which is not on the list. -/\ndef mustAccept : List (String × List Op) :=\n  [(\"H11\", h11p ++ [.endUse 3, .endUse 6, .reset 0 0]),\n   (\"H19\", h19p ++ [.endUse 2, .reset 0 0]),\n   (\"H29b\", h29bo), (\"H35\", h35o), (\"H36\", h36o), (\"H37\", h37o), (\"H44\", h44o),\n   (\"H45\", h45o), (\"H46\", h46o), (\"H47\", h47o), (\"W1\", w1o),\n   (\"W2\", w2o ++ [.release 12, .release 11, .release 10, .transfer 9 16, .transfer 12 19]),\n   (\"W3\", w3o ++ [.endUse 5, .endUse 2, .endUse 3, .endUse 4, .reset 0 0, .issue 0 0 [10] 2]),\n   (\"W3v\", w3vo ++ [.endUse 2, .reset 0 0, .issue 0 0 [7] 3])]\n\n/-- Every run of the list is `ok` in the kernel at each step, so the decisions cover all its\nchecked steps. -/\ntheorem mustAccept_runs : mustAccept.all (fun c => (prun K0 (PS.init []) c.2).isSome) = true := by\n  decide\n\n/-- The decisions of option 2 on the checked steps of each case. -/\ntheorem opt2_decisions : mustAccept.map (fun c => (c.1, dec2 c.2)) =\n    [(\"H11\", [true, true, true, true]), (\"H19\", [true]), (\"H29b\", [true]), (\"H35\", []),\n     (\"H36\", []), (\"H37\", [true]), (\"H44\", [true]), (\"H45\", [true, true, true, true]),\n     (\"H46\", [true]), (\"H47\", [true]), (\"W1\", []), (\"W2\", [true, true]),\n     (\"W3\", [true, true, true, true, true, true, true]), (\"W3v\", [true, true, true, true])] := by\n  decide\n\n/-- The decisions of option 3 on the checked steps of each case. -/\ntheorem opt3_decisions : mustAccept.map (fun c => (c.1, dec3 c.2)) =\n    [(\"H11\", [true, true, true, true]), (\"H19\", [true]), (\"H29b\", [true]), (\"H35\", []),\n     (\"H36\", []), (\"H37\", [true]), (\"H44\", [true]), (\"H45\", [true, true, true, true]),\n     (\"H46\", [true]), (\"H47\", [true]), (\"W1\", []), (\"W2\", [true, true]),\n     (\"W3\", [true, true, true, true, true, true, true]), (\"W3v\", [true, true, true, true])] := by\n  decide\n\n/-- No false rejection (material §5, criterion): neither option rejects a checked step of a case that\nmust be accepted. -/\ntheorem no_false_rejection : mustAccept.all (fun c => (dec2 c.2).all id && (dec3 c.2).all id) =\n    true := by\n  decide\n\n/-! ## Residual blockings (H49 to H51) -/\n\n/-- H49 (the cycle closed through a helper then its `release`): option 2 accepts every checked step,\nso the blocking of H49 remains; option 3 rejects the `store` that closes the cycle (the 7th checked\nstep), the helper notwithstanding. -/\ntheorem H49_options : dec2 h49o = [true, true, true, true] ∧\n    dec3 h49o = [true, true, true, false] := by\n  decide\n\n/-- The state and the step of H49 where option 3 rejects: `store 8 6` with the helper 9 active; in\nits arrival state, 7 and 8 block each other. -/\ntheorem H49_cycle : Blocks (storeEff (run K0 [] (h48o ++ [.derive 7 6 .modify])).s 8 6) 7 8 ∧\n    Blocks (storeEff (run K0 [] (h48o ++ [.derive 7 6 .modify])).s 8 6) 8 7 :=\n  by decide\n\n/-- H50 (an authority transferred or issued into the place it covers): both options reject the\n`transfer` and the `issue`, by the self-lock. -/\ntheorem H50_options : dec2 h50ao = [true, false] ∧ dec3 h50ao = [true, false] ∧\n    dec2 h50bo = [false] ∧ dec3 h50bo = [false] := by\n  decide\n\n/-- H51 (an element of a storage owned by `v` holds a view on `v`): option 2 does not check `store`,\nso the blocking remains; option 3 rejects the `store`: in its arrival state, the root of the storage,\nheld by `v`, and the view, held by the element, block each other. -/\ntheorem H51_options : dec2 h51o = [true] ∧ dec3 h51o = [false] ∧\n    Blocks (storeEff (run K0 [] (h51o.take 6)).s 4 3) 2 4 ∧\n    Blocks (storeEff (run K0 [] (h51o.take 6)).s 4 3) 4 2 := by\n  decide\n\n/-! ## Cost of the check -/\n\n/-- Locality of option 2 on `transfer`: the decision depends on the state only through the places and\nthe authorities held within the source, the ones the transfer moves. Two states with the same places\nand the same such authorities, at the same identities, get the same decision. -/\ntheorem opt2_transfer_local {s s' : S3} {src dst : Nat} (hP : s'.P = s.P)\n    (hA : ∀ j y, (s.A[j]? = some y ∨ s'.A[j]? = some y) → heldIn s.P src y.holder →\n      s'.A[j]? = s.A[j]?) :\n    Opt2Transfer s' src dst ↔ Opt2Transfer s src dst := by\n  have key : ∀ (t t' : S3), t'.P = t.P →\n      (∀ j y, (t.A[j]? = some y ∨ t'.A[j]? = some y) → heldIn t.P src y.holder →\n        t'.A[j]? = t.A[j]?) → Opt2Transfer t src dst → Opt2Transfer t' src dst := by\n    intro t t' hP hA h j hj hheld hsl\n    obtain ⟨y, hy, hh⟩ := optP_false_iff.1 hheld\n    rw [hP] at hh\n    have e := hA j y (.inr hy) hh\n    have hj' : j < t.A.length := lt_of_getElem? (e ▸ hy)\n    refine h j (List.mem_range.2 hj') (optP_false_iff.2 ⟨y, e ▸ hy, hh⟩) ?_\n    have ga : (transferEff t' src dst).A[j]? = (transferEff t src dst).A[j]? := by\n      rw [transfer_A_get, transfer_A_get, e, hP]\n    unfold SelfLock at hsl ⊢\n    rw [ga] at hsl\n    have gp : (transferEff t' src dst).P = (transferEff t src dst).P := by\n      simp only [transferEff, hP, ← e]\n      congr 1\n    rw [gp] at hsl\n    exact hsl\n  refine ⟨key s' s ?_ ?_, key s s' hP hA⟩\n  · exact hP.symm\n  · intro j y hy hh\n    rw [hP] at hh ⊢\n    exact (hA j y hy.symm (hP ▸ hh)).symm\n\n/-- Option 2 on `issue` reads only the region and the destination: the block is self-locked exactly\nwhen the destination's footprint meets the region. -/\ntheorem opt2_issue_local (s : S3) (ar : Arena) (region : List Nat) (dst : Nat) :\n    Opt2Issue s ar region dst ↔ ¬ ∃ l ∈ region, l ∈ footprint s.P dst := by\n  unfold Opt2Issue SelfLock\n  simp only [issueEff, S3.addAuth, List.getElem?_append_right (Nat.le_refl _), Nat.sub_self,\n    List.getElem?_cons_zero, OptP, true_and]\n\n/-- Option 3 is not local: from two reached states that agree on the authority stored, 8 (same\nentry), on the target 6 (same footprint) and on the number of authorities, the `store 8 6` gets\ndifferent decisions. They differ on the authority 7, which the step does not touch: stored into the\nnode 5 in the first (H48), held by the frame in the second (its twin). -/\ntheorem opt3_not_local :\n    PReach K0 [] h48 ∧ PReach K0 [] h48t ∧ h48.s.A[8]? = h48t.s.A[8]? ∧\n    footprint h48.s.P 6 = footprint h48t.s.P 6 ∧ h48.s.A.length = h48t.s.A.length ∧\n    h48.s.A[7]? ≠ h48t.s.A[7]? ∧\n    ¬ NoLock (storeEff h48.s 8 6) ∧ NoLock (storeEff h48t.s 8 6) :=\n  ⟨H48.1, H48.2.2.1, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide⟩\n\nend Ern.MM03.LockOptions\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"265265f2-e66d-4e96-8f25-cc293c8a8735","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/validation_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
