{"parentUuid":"0dea590b-05b7-4b70-80f0-4dd0e3df70f2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgcfsmzyXAzj6N8DZf76Q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Step 4 is committed, completing all four steps. Now launching four independent read-only reviewers to check exclusivity bypass/pool fidelity, MM3-H twins/verdict sources, NoLock measurement triviality, and MM23-H, while I draft the report in parallel.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1006,"cache_read_input_tokens":727528,"output_tokens":6060,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1400},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1006,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6060,"cache_read_input_tokens":727528,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1006,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1006},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":2,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"23272fd6-e72b-4103-8523-12ac0b70d360","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgcfsmQ1vJEAd6HYDdnWR","requestRef":"01008745-0ac4-4925-99a3-518bc12978bf","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"7823108a-63c6-40e9-b7aa-957e01fbdc75","timestamp":"2026-11-01T18:20:43.483Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/validation_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
{"parentUuid":"7823108a-63c6-40e9-b7aa-957e01fbdc75","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgcfsmzyXAzj6N8DZf76Q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PmmgubaPwNuwbooCFPanBF","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Review HandlePool exclusivity and fidelity","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are an adversarial, read-only reviewer (apply the \"Review (Codex)\" section of AGENTS.md in /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern). Do not edit any file in the repository. Scratch Lean files go in a fresh temp dir of your own (e.g. `mktemp -d`), checked with `cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && ~/.elan/bin/lake env lean /path/to/scratch.lean` (start scratch files with `import Ern.HandlePool` then `open Ern.MM03 Ern.HandlePool`; `lake` is at ~/.elan/bin/lake). The modules are already built.\n\nContext: jalon 3, step 1 of an ERN formalization. The normative source for this module is §4 of `/Users/guygouri/Downloads/ERN_Jalon3_materiel.md` (contract of the handle pool: entry state, compound borrow, operations newPool, allocSlot, resolve, resolveMany, unresolve, freeSlot, PoolInv, expected theorems). The kernel is `formal/Ern/MM03.lean` (spec: `/Users/guygouri/Downloads/ERN_MM-03.3_v0.3_revisee.md`). The module under review is `formal/Ern/HandlePool.lean`.\n\nLens 1 (main): try to BYPASS `pool_resolve_modify_exclusive`. The material requires: on every reached state, at most one active Modify companion per pool, and then no active Observe companion, whatever the sequence of resolve, resolveMany, release, store, transfer and unresolve. Look for (a) a reachable sequence (PReach, which includes every kernel step) where two active companions of the same pool coexist with one Modify — build it with the executable runner `prun` and `decide` if you think one exists; (b) ways the statement is weaker than the material: e.g. companions not all recorded in `ps.res`, a resolution path that creates an exclusive access to the pool storage without being recorded as a companion, two pools with the same internal/storage, newPool reading only arena entries (`NewArenaPre` clause 4), the theorem quantifying over records rather than authorities, `DDSound` hypothesis, etc. A theorem that holds because a definition is too permissive is blocking.\n\nLens 2: fidelity of each pool operation to §4, clause by clause (check order of reject/fail, \"fail leaves state unchanged\", which kernel ops are used, what is recorded). Note anything that is stronger or weaker than the material. The module docstrings say design choices are reported elsewhere (slots = children of the storage; first free entry; right check = companion's DerivePre; HandleOK out-of-range slot = fail; resolveMany Observe rejected by split); you may judge whether each is dictated by the material or is a silent interpretation that changes verdicts.\n\nLens 3: the literal `PoolInv` and its counterexamples (`pool_inv_not_preserved`, `pool_inv_cex_entry`): check that `PoolInvDisj`/`PoolInvGen`/`PoolInvDesc` say what §4's three clauses say (not stronger, not weaker), and that the counterexamples are genuine (reached states, PoolInv holding before).\n\nEvery finding needs evidence: a quote of the material/spec, a counterexample (Lean, decided), or command output. No evidence, no finding. Do not ask for additions beyond the task. Return: verdict (block / changes / ok), then each finding with severity (blocking/major/minor), location (file:line), cause (formalization error, missing coverage or spec defect) and evidence. Be concise; under 900 words.","run_in_background":"true"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1006,"cache_read_input_tokens":727528,"output_tokens":6060,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1400},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"servic