` and `open Ern.MM03 Ern.HandlePool Ern.MM03.Horrors`; modules are built; `#eval (prun K0 (PS.init []) ops).isSome` and `#eval decide (SomePre ...)` help locate which step/clause fails).\n\nContext: jalon 3, step 2 of an ERN formalization: the MM3-H corpus in `formal/Ern/MM03/Horrors.lean`. Source of the cases and expected verdicts: `/Users/guygouri/Downloads/ERN_Jalon3_materiel.md` §1 (sections A–I), §5b (W1–W3) and §0 (rules: independent oracle, positive twin = same sequence without the faulty element, states reached from the initial state, no silent correction, classification). Kernel: `formal/Ern/MM03.lean`; handle pool: `formal/Ern/HandlePool.lean` (runner `prun`, `PReach`). Spec: `/Users/guygouri/Downloads/ERN_MM-03.3_v0.3_revisee.md`.\n\nLens (main): the twins. For every rejection in the module, check (1) the rejection is caused by the clause the docstring names (and that this matches the material's source), not by an unrelated construction error (wrong index, missing write, a different clause failing) — evaluate the individual precondition clauses on the state to see which ones fail; (2) the twin is really \"the same sequence without the faulty element\" and its acceptance is not obtained by also changing something else; (3) the rejection is absent in the twin (rule 2). Also check: each expected verdict in docstrings matches the material's \"Attendu\" column; each case is encoded (no row of A–I or W1–W3 missing); the cases reported as deviating (H16 not expressible, H07 rebuilt, W2 reading of \"vue de colonne\", W3 literal reading vs variant, H01 reborrow) are described faithfully and the claimed cause is the true cause; classes (N3/Lib/spec 3) match the material.\n\nEvery finding needs evidence: a quote, a decided Lean statement, or command output. No evidence, no finding. Do not ask for additions beyond the task. Return: verdict (block / changes / ok), then each finding with severity, location (file:line), cause (formalization error, missing coverage or spec defect) and evidence. Be concise; under 900 words.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/tasks/a9fabe986081cfffc.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"23272fd6-e72b-4103-8523-12ac0b70d360","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/validation_0.1","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"603d834f-9e5f-43d0-9980-b1c44d9c98c5","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/validation_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
