ckOptions` and `open Ern.MM03 Ern.HandlePool Ern.MM03.Horrors Ern.MM03.LockOptions`; modules are built).\n\nContext: jalon 3, step 4: measure of the `NoLock` options in `formal/Ern/MM03/LockOptions.lean`, on runs defined in `formal/Ern/MM03/Horrors.lean`. Source: `/Users/guygouri/Downloads/ERN_Jalon3_materiel.md` §5 (options 1–3, measures: false rejections on H11, H19, H29b, H35–H37, H44–H47, W1–W3; residual blockings on H49–H51; cost: local vs global) and the brief's step 4: option 2 = self-lock predicate for transfer and issue (an authority placed in a location it covers); option 3 = relation \"b blocks a\" (b ≠ a, both active, the footprint of b contains a leaf of the holder of a), self-lock as a separate clause, acyclicity predicate; for each case the decision of each option by decide on the state and step concerned; cost: a locality lemma if local, a counterexample otherwise. No option is to be adopted.\n\nLens (main): is any decision made trivial by a badly built state or measure? E.g. a case whose run has no checked step (or fewer than its scenario implies), a run that stops early so later steps are not measured (`decisions` stops at the first non-ok kernel step — check `mustAccept_runs`), states where no authority is held by a place so the predicates are vacuously true, the option checked on the wrong state (before vs arrival), arena issue arrival state, the bounded reachability in `BlocksAcyclic` missing cycles, the definitions of `SelfLock`/`Blocks`/`NoLock`/`Opt2Transfer` being weaker or stronger than §5/the brief, `opt2_transfer_local` being vacuous or too weak to support \"local\", `opt3_not_local` not really showing non-locality. Also check the \"residual blocking\" claims for H49–H51 (Horrors docstrings and theorems) are true and that options are not credited with preventing a blocking they do not prevent.\n\nEvery finding needs evidence: a quote, a decided Lean statement, or command output. No evidence, no finding. Do not ask for additions beyond the task. Return: verdict (block / changes / ok), then each finding with severity, location (file:line), cause (formalization error, missing coverage or spec defect) and evidence. Be concise; under 900 words.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/tasks/acf11e06dc56d1479.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"23272fd6-e72b-4103-8523-12ac0b70d360","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/validation_0.1","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b3eedfc7-fd25-4c2e-a21c-61e873044e38","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/validation_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
