 and `open Ern Ern.MM03 Ern.MM23 Ern.MM23.Horrors`; modules are built).\n\nContext: jalon 3, step 3: the MM23-H corpus in `formal/Ern/MM23/Horrors.lean`, each case \"comme exécution traduite par simulation\" (theorem `simulation` of `formal/Ern/MM23.lean`). Source: `/Users/guygouri/Downloads/ERN_Jalon3_materiel.md` §3 (cases H01–H17, expected verdicts) and §0 rule 8 (H15, H16 encoded with the obtained verdict and marked \"écart connu\", never presented as passed; H14 and H17 not encoded, classified). The module computes the layout from the final places of the run (`autoL`, `autoG`, `piOf`) and runs translated steps with an executable `srun` proved sound (`srun_sound`, `sim_of`).\n\nCheck: (1) each case statement says what the material's \"Attendu\" says for that case — not weaker (e.g. a property proved on a state where it holds trivially, a conclusion that restates a hypothesis), not about a different step; (2) each case is really an execution translated by `simulation` (is `sim_of`/`simulation` actually applied to the run that contains the step under test, or only to some other run?); (3) the soundness of the runner (`step3exec_sound`, `srun_sound`, `simRun_of`, `sim_of`) — any gap would make every case unsound; (4) the auto-layout respects the obligations it must (`NewLayout` is checked per step by decide inside `Oblig` — confirm), and does not make a case vacuous (e.g. H03 pinned leaf, H16 offsets); (5) H15/H16 marked \"écart connu\" in docstrings and not presented as passed; (6) whether H02's \"aucun programme sûr n'y parvient\" is covered by more than the inactivity of one block (see `reset_kills_blocks`).\n\nEvery finding needs evidence: a quote, a decided Lean statement, or command output. No evidence, no finding. Do not ask for additions beyond the task. Return: verdict (block / changes / ok), then each finding with severity, location (file:line), cause (formalization error, missing coverage or spec defect) and evidence. Be concise; under 900 words.","outpu