them and stored into the fields 6, 7, 8. -/"," def w3vo : List Op := [.enter [] [lf, lf, lf, (some 2, none, 0), (some 2, none, 0),","-    (some 2, none, 0)], .write 1 [1],","-  .alloc 1 0 [lf, (some 6, none, 0), (some 6, none, 0), (some 6, none, 0)], .write 0 [0],","-  .newArena 6 3, .issue 0 0 [7] 3, .issue 0 0 [8] 4, .issue 0 0 [9] 5]","+    (some 2, none, 0), (some 2, none, 0), (some 2, none, 0), (some 2, none, 0)], .write 1 [1],","+  .alloc 1 0 [lf, (some 9, none, 0), (some 9, none, 0), (some 9, none, 0)], .write 0 [0],","+  .newArena 9 3, .issue 0 0 [10] 3, .issue 0 0 [11] 4, .issue 0 0 [12] 5,","+  .derive 4 10 .observe, .derive 5 11 .observe, .derive 6 12 .observe, .store 7 6, .store 8 7,","+  .store 9 8]"," "," /-- **W3** (§5b, frame arena; Lib). Expected: `reset` while the views live: reject; after `endUse`"," of the structure: `ok`; reissue `ok`. Obtained, literal reading (report, (b)): reject while the"," views live; after `endUse` of the structure, `reset` is still rejected, the three blocks being held"," by the values 2, 3, 4 (MM-03.3 §6, O19.2); after their end, `reset` and the reissue are accepted.","-With the blocks issued into the fields of the structure, the expected verdicts are obtained. -/","+With the blocks issued into fields of the structure and the views stored into others, the expected","+verdicts are obtained. -/"," theorem W3 : PReach K0 [] w3 ∧ ResetAtStep K0 0 0 w3.s .reject ∧ PReach K0 [] w3e ∧","     ResetAtStep K0 0 0 w3e.s .reject ∧","     PReach K0 [] (run K0 [] (w3o ++ [.endUse 5, .endUse 2, .endUse 3, .endUse 4, .reset 0 0,","       .issue 0 0 [10] 2])) ∧","     PReach K0 [] (run K0 [] w3vo) ∧ ResetAtStep K0 0 0 (run K0 [] w3vo).s .reject ∧","-    PReach K0 [] (run K0 [] (w3vo ++ [.endUse 2, .reset 0 0, .issue 0 0 [7] 3])) :=","+    PReach K0 [] (run K0 [] (w3vo ++ [.endUse 2, .reset 0 0, .issue 0 0 [10] 3])) :=","   ⟨run_reach (by decide) (by decide), .reject (by decide), run_reach (by decide) (by decide),","     .reject (by decide), run_reach (by decide) (by decide), run_reach (by decide) (by decide),","     .reject (by decide), run_reach (by decide) (by decide)⟩"," ","+/-! ## Observations on the contract of the pool (report, (g))","+","+Reached runs that bear on the reading of material §4, kept as witnesses. -/","+","+/-- The prefix of H44: a pool on an arena block, both entries allocated, nothing resolved, nothing","+pinned. -/","+def ob1 : PS := run K0 [] (h44o.take 9)","+","+/-- `freeSlot` on a pool whose `internal` is derived (here the block 6) is rejected by the","+preconditions of `endUse` (material §4: \"reject si une précondition d'`endUse` échoue\"):","+`internal` itself is an active derived authority on the entry, held outside it (`EndUseAccessOK`,","+A6). -/","+theorem pool_freeSlot_derived_internal : PReach K0 [] ob1 ∧ ob1.res = [] ∧","+    FreeSlotStep K0 0 0 ⟨0, 0, 0⟩ ob1 .reject ∧ ¬ EndUseAccessOK ob1.s 7 6 ∧ ob1.s.org 6 = some 5 :=","+  ⟨run_reach (by decide) (by decide), by decide,","+    .endUse (pl := ⟨0, 6, 6, [⟨7, 0, true⟩, ⟨10, 0, true⟩]⟩) (sl := ⟨7, 0, true⟩) (by decide)","+      (by decide) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide), by decide, by decide⟩","+","+/-- Contracts with the leaf 1 (the pool value of `pb`) `SharedMutable`. -/","+abbrev KSh : K := KT [1] [] [] [] []","+/-- A callee with an `Observe` parameter (5) on the pool value of `pb`, entry 0 allocated. -/","+def ob2 : PS := run KSh [] (pb ++ [.allocSlot 0 0 2, .derive 1 1 .observe, .enter [5] [lf]])","+","+/-- With the right to update the pool value by `writeShared` on its `SharedMutable` metadata","+(material §4), `allocSlot` is accepted while `freeSlot` is rejected: `endUse` asks `Modify` on the","+entry (A2). -/","+theorem pool_freeSlot_shared_right : PReach KSh [] ob2 ∧ ¬ HasRight ob2.s .modify 1 ∧","+    PoolRight KSh ob2.s ⟨0, 4, 4, [⟨5, 0, true⟩, ⟨6, 0, false⟩]⟩ 5 ∧","+    (pexec KSh ob2 (.allocSlot 0 5 7)).isSome = true ∧","+    FreeSlotStep KSh 0 5 ⟨0, 0, 0⟩ ob2 .reject ∧ ¬ HasRight ob2.s .modify 5 :=","+  ⟨run_reach (by decide) (by decide), by decide, by decide, by decide,","+    .endUse (pl := ⟨0, 4, 4, [⟨5, 0, true⟩, ⟨6, 0, false⟩]⟩) (sl := ⟨5, 0, true⟩) (by decide)","+      (by decide) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide), by decide⟩","+","+/-- Two pools on the same storage and `internal` 5 (`newPool` reads the arenas only, O17.4): pool 0","+frees its entry 0 and allocates it again; the handle of pool 1 on the same place still resolves. -/","+def ob3o : List Op := [.enter [] [lf, lf, lf, lf, lf], .write 0 [0], .write 1 [1],","+  .alloc 0 1 [lf, (some 5, none, 0), (some 5, none, 0)], .newPool 5 5, .newPool 5 5,","+  .allocSlot 0 0 2, .allocSlot 1 0 3, .freeSlot 0 0 ⟨0, 0, 0⟩, .allocSlot 0 0 4]","+","+theorem pool_two_on_one_internal : PReach K0 [] (run K0 [] ob3o) ∧","+    (run K0 [] ob3o).pools = [⟨0, 5, 5, [⟨6, 1, true⟩, ⟨7, 0, false⟩]⟩,","+      ⟨1, 5, 5, [⟨6, 0, true⟩, ⟨7, 0, false⟩]⟩] ∧","+    PReach K0 [] (run K0 [] (ob3o ++ [.resolve 1 ⟨1, 0, 0⟩ .modify])) :=","+  ⟨run_reach (by decide) (by decide), by decide, run_reach (by decide) (by decide)⟩","+","+/-- Two pools on the same `internal`: the `freeSlot` of pool 1 ends the content of the entry 0 of","+pool 0, written and live. -/","+def ob3b : List Op := pb ++ [.newPool 4 4, .allocSlot 0 0 2, .allocSlot 1 0 3, .write 4 [5],","+  .freeSlot 1 0 ⟨1, 0, 0⟩]","+","+theorem pool_two_freeSlot_cross : PReach K0 [] (run K0 [] ob3b) ∧","+    (run K0 [] (ob3b.take 9)).s.I 5 = .init ∧ (run K0 [] ob3b).s.I 5 = .uninit ∧","+    (run K0 [] ob3b).pools.map (fun pl => pl.slots.map (·.live)) = [[true, false], [false, false]] :=","+  ⟨run_reach (by decide) (by decide), by decide, by decide, by decide⟩","+","+/-- The mirror: `newArena` on the `internal` of a live pool is accepted (O17.4 reads arenas). -/","+theorem arena_on_pool_internal :","+    PReach K0 [] (run K0 [] (pb ++ [.allocSlot 0 0 2, .newArena 4 4])) :=","+  run_reach (by decide) (by decide)","+","+/-- \"Périmé\" read twice (report, (f)): on a fresh pool, `resolveMany` of the handle of a free entry at","+its current generation fails (the entry is free), while `freeSlot` of the same handle is accepted","+(only the identity and the generation are read). -/","+theorem pool_free_entry_handle : PReach K0 [] (run K0 [] pb) ∧","+    ResolveManyStep K0 0 [⟨0, 0, 0⟩] .modify (run K0 [] pb) (.fail (run K0 [] pb)) ∧","+    (pexec K0 (run K0 [] pb) (.freeSlot 0 0 ⟨0, 0, 0⟩)).isSome = true :=","+  ⟨run_reach (by decide) (by decide),","+    .fail (pl := ⟨0, 4, 4, [⟨5, 0, false⟩, ⟨6, 0, false⟩]⟩) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide),","+    by decide⟩","+","+/-- `allocSlot` leaves the content of the entry as it is (material §4: \"son contenu reste","+`Uninit`\"): a storage written before `newPool` gives a live entry whose content is `Init`. -/","+theorem pool_allocSlot_content_init : PReach K0 [] (run K0 [] [.enter [] [lf, lf, lf, lf],","+      .write 0 [0], .write 1 [1], .alloc 0 1 [lf, (some 4, none, 0), (some 4, none, 0)],","+      .write 4 [5], .newPool 4 4, .allocSlot 0 0 2]) ∧","+    (run K0 [] [.enter [] [lf, lf, lf, lf], .write 0 [0], .write 1 [1],","+      .alloc 0 1 [lf, (some 4, none, 0), (some 4, none, 0)], .write 4 [5], .newPool 4 4,","+      .allocSlot 0 0 2]).s.I 5 = .init :=","+  ⟨run_reach (by decide) (by decide), by decide⟩","+"," /-! ## J. Out of kernel (material §1 J): the one expressible expansion -/"," "," /-- Contracts with the place 3 deallocable by the authority 7. -/"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/MM03/Horrors.lean"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"6ec94361-b1ef-4917-a827-e932d4c2a310","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/validation_0.1","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3b4061b8-722e-4a18-8070-578b1d695890","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/validation_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","hash":"e311a6b6721a1e76a4a1cd4b36e57df955d585e5c3cbc74b78e1a07bc2eb463f","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0194nUhE2y4DhNZL2kHpAGK4","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && SP=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad && cat > $SP/j3/fix03.py <<'PYEOF'\np='Ern/MM03/Horrors.lean'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:90]\n    s=s.replace(a,b,1)\nrep(\"\"\"/-- H01, reading where the `Observe` parameter is derived from the `Modify` one (report, (b)): the\ncall with both is accepted. G1 constrains the origin of a `Modify` parameter only, and the two\nauthorities are related by derivation (I1). -/\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- H01, reading where the `Observe` parameter is derived from the `Modify` one (report, (b)): the\nonly construction that reaches `enterFrame` with both parameters. Expected (H01 row): reject;\nobtained: the call is accepted. G1 constrains the direct origin of a `Modify` parameter only (O6.3),\nand the two authorities are related by derivation (I1). -/\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"obtained: reject. Twin without the stored authority: accepted. -/\ntheorem H03\"\"\",\"\"\"obtained: reject. Twin without the stored authority: accepted. The `store` is not what makes the\nwrite fail: after the `derive` alone, the write is already rejected (I1, effective mode), so the case\ndoes not exercise F4 itself. -/\ntheorem H03\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"at the `transfer`; obtained: reject. Twin without the anchor: accepted. The material speaks of a\nvalue received as a parameter; the callee cannot transfer out of a parameter (H16), so the value is\na local of the callee (report, (b)). -/\"\"\",\"\"\"at the `transfer`; obtained: reject. Twin without the anchor: accepted. The stored value is a local\nof the callee, which the material leaves open. -/\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"def h17t : PS := run KF4 [] h17p\n\n/-- **H17** (C; A6, `Deallocable`; Lib; covered pass 2). `free` of the block on `[5]`: rejected,\nthe region is a part of the storage, neither an owned root nor deallocable. Expected: reject;\nobtained: reject. Twin: `free` of the allocated storage 4 itself, with nothing issued, accepted. -/\ntheorem H17 : PReach KF4 [] h17 ∧ FreeStep KF4 5 7 h17.s .reject ∧ PReach KF4 [] h17t ∧\n    FreeStep KF4 4 7 h17t.s (.ok (freeEff h17t.s 4)) :=\n  ⟨run_reach (by decide) (by decide), .reject (by decide), run_reach (by decide) (by decide),\n    .ok (by decide)⟩\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- Twin of H17: the same run, the block ended with its value 2. -/\ndef h17t : PS := run KF4 [] (h17p ++ [.issue 0 0 [5] 2, .endUse 2])\n/-- Contracts declaring deallocable, with the authority 7, both the storage 4 and the region 5. -/\nabbrev KF45 : K := KT [] [] [] [4, 5] [(4, 7), (5, 7)]\ndef h17d : PS := run KF45 [] (h17p ++ [.issue 0 0 [5] 2])\n\n/-- **H17** (C; A6, `Deallocable`; Lib; covered pass 2). `free` of the block on `[5]`: rejected,\nthe region is a part of the storage, not an owned root, nor deallocable under `KF4`; with the region\ndeclared deallocable (`KF45`), the `free` is still rejected (`OwnedRoot`). Expected: reject;\nobtained: reject. Twin: in the same run, the block ended, the `free` of the allocated storage 4 is\naccepted. -/\ntheorem H17 : PReach KF4 [] h17 ∧ FreeStep KF4 5 7 h17.s .reject ∧\n    PReach KF45 [] h17d ∧ ¬ OwnedRoot h17d.s 5 ∧ FreeStep KF45 5 7 h17d.s .reject ∧\n    PReach KF4 [] h17t ∧ FreeStep KF4 4 7 h17t.s (.ok (freeEff h17t.s 4)) :=\n  ⟨run_reach (by decide) (by decide), .reject (by decide), run_reach (by decide) (by decide),\n    by decide, .reject (by decide), run_reach (by decide) (by decide), .ok (by decide)⟩\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"theorem H22 : PReach K0 [] h22 ∧ TransferStep K0 0 1 h22.s .reject ∧\n    TransferStep K0 0 1 h22t.s (.ok (transferEff h22t.s 0 1)) ∧\"\"\",\"\"\"theorem H22 : PReach K0 [] h22 ∧ TransferStep K0 0 1 h22.s .reject ∧ PReach K0 [] h22t ∧\n    TransferStep K0 0 1 h22t.s (.ok (transferEff h22t.s 0 1)) ∧\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  ⟨run_reach (by decide) (by decide), .reject (by decide), .ok (by decide),\n    run_reach (by decide) (by decide)⟩\n\n/-- H23\"\"\",\"\"\"  ⟨run_reach (by decide) (by decide), .reject (by decide), run_reach (by decide) (by decide),\n    .ok (by decide), run_reach (by decide) (by decide)⟩\n\n/-- H23\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"/-- **H51** (I; §5; N3). An element of a storage owned by `v` holds a view on `v`. The direct `store`\nis rejected by its arrival clause (G2); with a helper on the storage, then its `release`, it is\nreached.\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- **H51** (I; §5; N3). An element of a storage owned by `v` holds a view on `v`. The direct `store`\nis rejected: the view already takes away the frame's `Modify` on `v`, hence on the storage `v` owns\n(`HasRight` before the step, B2), and the arrival clause of G2 fails too; with a helper on the\nstorage, then its `release`, the configuration is reached.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"/-- **W2** (§5b, ECS archetype and sparse set; Lib). Disjoint reads and writes `ok`;\n`resolveMany` `ok`; the move of a field of the row while the column view is active: rejected; after\nthe release of the views: `ok`. Expected: the same. Obtained: the same, reading \"the view of the\ncolumn\" as the column authority given by `split` (report, (f)): after the release of the read view\n12 alone, the move is still rejected by the column authority 11 (O4.4); after its release, and that\nof the first column authority, both fields of the row move. -/\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- **W2** (§5b, ECS archetype and sparse set; Lib). Expected: disjoint reads and writes `ok`;\n`resolveMany` `ok`; the move of a field of the row while the column view is active: reject; after\nits release: `ok`. Obtained: disjoint accesses, `resolveMany` and the rejection during the view as\nexpected. After the release: if \"the view of the column\" is the read view 12, the move is still\nrejected, by the column authority 11 given by `split` (O4.4; report, (b)); if it is the column\nauthority itself, the move is accepted after its release (and that of the first column authority,\nwhich covers the other field of the row). -/\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"/-- W3, reading where the blocks are issued into the fields of the structure 2 (fields 3, 4, 5;\nstorage 6 with the leaves 7, 8, 9, `internal` 3). -/\ndef w3vo : List Op := [.enter [] [lf, lf, lf, (some 2, none, 0), (some 2, none, 0),\n    (some 2, none, 0)], .write 1 [1],\n  .alloc 1 0 [lf, (some 6, none, 0), (some 6, none, 0), (some 6, none, 0)], .write 0 [0],\n  .newArena 6 3, .issue 0 0 [7] 3, .issue 0 0 [8] 4, .issue 0 0 [9] 5]\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- W3, reading where the blocks are issued into fields of the structure: structure 2 with the\nfields 3 to 8; storage 9 (leaves 10, 11, 12), `internal` 3; the blocks 4, 5, 6 issued into the\nfields 3, 4, 5; the views 7, 8, 9 derived from them and stored into the fields 6, 7, 8. -/\ndef w3vo : List Op := [.enter [] [lf, lf, lf, (some 2, none, 0), (some 2, none, 0),\n    (some 2, none, 0), (some 2, none, 0), (some 2, none, 0), (some 2, none, 0)], .write 1 [1],\n  .alloc 1 0 [lf, (some 9, none, 0), (some 9, none, 0), (some 9, none, 0)], .write 0 [0],\n  .newArena 9 3, .issue 0 0 [10] 3, .issue 0 0 [11] 4, .issue 0 0 [12] 5,\n  .derive 4 10 .observe, .derive 5 11 .observe, .derive 6 12 .observe, .store 7 6, .store 8 7,\n  .store 9 8]\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"With the blocks issued into the fields of the structure, the expected verdicts are obtained. -/\"\"\",\"\"\"With the blocks issued into fields of the structure and the views stored into others, the expected\nverdicts are obtained. -/\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"    PReach K0 [] (run K0 [] (w3vo ++ [.endUse 2, .reset 0 0, .issue 0 0 [7] 3])) :=\"\"\",\"\"\"    PReach K0 [] (run K0 [] (w3vo ++ [.endUse 2, .reset 0 0, .issue 0 0 [10] 3])) :=\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"/-! ## J. Out of kernel (material §1 J): the one expressible expansion -/\"\"\",\"\"\"/-! ## Observations on the contract of the pool (report, (g))\n\nReached runs that bear on the reading of material §4, kept as witnesses. -/\n\n/-- The prefix of H44: a pool on an arena block, both entries allocated, nothing resolved, nothing\npinned. -/\ndef ob1 : PS := run K0 [] (h44o.take 9)\n\n/-- `freeSlot` on a pool whose `internal` is derived (here the block 6) is rejected by the\npreconditions of `endUse` (material §4: \"reject si une précondition d'`endUse` échoue\"):\n`internal` itself is an active derived authority on the entry, held outside it (`EndUseAccessOK`,\nA6). -/\ntheorem pool_freeSlot_derived_internal : PReach K0 [] ob1 ∧ ob1.res = [] ∧\n    FreeSlotStep K0 0 0 ⟨0, 0, 0⟩ ob1 .reject ∧ ¬ EndUseAccessOK ob1.s 7 6 ∧ ob1.s.org 6 = some 5 :=\n  ⟨run_reach (by decide) (by decide), by decide,\n    .endUse (pl := ⟨0, 6, 6, [⟨7, 0, true⟩, ⟨10, 0, true⟩]⟩) (sl := ⟨7, 0, true⟩) (by decide)\n      (by decide) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide), by decide, by decide⟩\n\n/-- Contracts with the leaf 1 (the pool value of `pb`) `SharedMutable`. -/\nabbrev KSh : K := KT [1] [] [] [] []\n/-- A callee with an `Observe` parameter (5) on the pool value of `pb`, entry 0 allocated. -/\ndef ob2 : PS := run KSh [] (pb ++ [.allocSlot 0 0 2, .derive 1 1 .observe, .enter [5] [lf]])\n\n/-- With the right to update the pool value by `writeShared` on its `SharedMutable` metadata\n(material §4), `allocSlot` is accepted while `freeSlot` is rejected: `endUse` asks `Modify` on the\nentry (A2). -/\ntheorem pool_freeSlot_shared_right : PReach KSh [] ob2 ∧ ¬ HasRight ob2.s .modify 1 ∧\n    PoolRight KSh ob2.s ⟨0, 4, 4, [⟨5, 0, true⟩, ⟨6, 0, false⟩]⟩ 5 ∧\n    (pexec KSh ob2 (.allocSlot 0 5 7)).isSome = true ∧\n    FreeSlotStep KSh 0 5 ⟨0, 0, 0⟩ ob2 .reject ∧ ¬ HasRight ob2.s .modify 5 :=\n  ⟨run_reach (by decide) (by decide), by decide, by decide, by decide,\n    .endUse (pl := ⟨0, 4, 4, [⟨5, 0, true⟩, ⟨6, 0, false⟩]⟩) (sl := ⟨5, 0, true⟩) (by decide)\n      (by decide) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide), by decide⟩\n\n/-- Two pools on the same storage and `internal` 5 (`newPool` reads the arenas only, O17.4): pool 0\nfrees its entry 0 and allocates it again; the handle of pool 1 on the same place still resolves. -/\ndef ob3o : List Op := [.enter [] [lf, lf, lf, lf, lf], .write 0 [0], .write 1 [1],\n  .alloc 0 1 [lf, (some 5, none, 0), (some 5, none, 0)], .newPool 5 5, .newPool 5 5,\n  .allocSlot 0 0 2, .allocSlot 1 0 3, .freeSlot 0 0 ⟨0, 0, 0⟩, .allocSlot 0 0 4]\n\ntheorem pool_two_on_one_internal : PReach K0 [] (run K0 [] ob3o) ∧\n    (run K0 [] ob3o).pools = [⟨0, 5, 5, [⟨6, 1, true⟩, ⟨7, 0, false⟩]⟩,\n      ⟨1, 5, 5, [⟨6, 0, true⟩, ⟨7, 0, false⟩]⟩] ∧\n    PReach K0 [] (run K0 [] (ob3o ++ [.resolve 1 ⟨1, 0, 0⟩ .modify])) :=\n  ⟨run_reach (by decide) (by decide), by decide, run_reach (by decide) (by decide)⟩\n\n/-- Two pools on the same `internal`: the `freeSlot` of pool 1 ends the content of the entry 0 of\npool 0, written and live. -/\ndef ob3b : List Op := pb ++ [.newPool 4 4, .allocSlot 0 0 2, .allocSlot 1 0 3, .write 4 [5],\n  .freeSlot 1 0 ⟨1, 0, 0⟩]\n\ntheorem pool_two_freeSlot_cross : PReach K0 [] (run K0 [] ob3b) ∧\n    (run K0 [] (ob3b.take 9)).s.I 5 = .init ∧ (run K0 [] ob3b).s.I 5 = .uninit ∧\n    (run K0 [] ob3b).pools.map (fun pl => pl.slots.map (·.live)) = [[true, false], [false, false]] :=\n  ⟨run_reach (by decide) (by decide), by decide, by decide, by decide⟩\n\n/-- The mirror: `newArena` on the `internal` of a live pool is accepted (O17.4 reads arenas). -/\ntheorem arena_on_pool_internal :\n    PReach K0 [] (run K0 [] (pb ++ [.allocSlot 0 0 2, .newArena 4 4])) :=\n  run_reach (by decide) (by decide)\n\n/-- \"Périmé\" read twice (report, (f)): on a fresh pool, `resolveMany` of the handle of a free entry at\nits current generation fails (the entry is free), while `freeSlot` of the same handle is accepted\n(only the identity and the generation are read). -/\ntheorem pool_free_entry_handle : PReach K0 [] (run K0 [] pb) ∧\n    ResolveManyStep K0 0 [⟨0, 0, 0⟩] .modify (run K0 [] pb) (.fail (run K0 [] pb)) ∧\n    (pexec K0 (run K0 [] pb) (.freeSlot 0 0 ⟨0, 0, 0⟩)).isSome = true :=\n  ⟨run_reach (by decide) (by decide),\n    .fail (pl := ⟨0, 4, 4, [⟨5, 0, false⟩, ⟨6, 0, false⟩]⟩) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide),\n    by decide⟩\n\n/-- `allocSlot` leaves the content of the entry as it is (material §4: \"son contenu reste\n`Uninit`\"): a storage written before `newPool` gives a live entry whose content is `Init`. -/\ntheorem pool_allocSlot_content_init : PReach K0 [] (run K0 [] [.enter [] [lf, lf, lf, lf],\n      .write 0 [0], .write 1 [1], .alloc 0 1 [lf, (some 4, none, 0), (some 4, none, 0)],\n      .write 4 [5], .newPool 4 4, .allocSlot 0 0 2]) ∧\n    (run K0 [] [.enter [] [lf, lf, lf, lf], .write 0 [0], .write 1 [1],\n      .alloc 0 1 [lf, (some 4, none, 0), (some 4, none, 0)], .write 4 [5], .newPool 4 4,\n      .allocSlot 0 0 2]).s.I 5 = .init :=\n  ⟨run_reach (by decide) (by decide), by decide⟩\n\n/-! ## J. Out of kernel (material §1 J): the one expressible expansion -/\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\npython3 $SP/j3/fix03.py && time ~/.elan/bin/lake build Ern.MM03.Horrors 2>&1 | grep -E '^error|warning' -A10 | head -50","description":"Apply MM3-H fixes and pool observations, rebuild","timeout":900000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
