epts every checked step,","-so the blocking of H49 remains; option 3 rejects the `store` that closes the cycle (the 7th checked","+so the blocking of H49 remains; option 3 rejects the `store` that closes the cycle (the fourth checked"," step), the helper notwithstanding. -/"," theorem H49_options : dec2 h49o = [true, true, true, true] ∧","     dec3 h49o = [true, true, true, false] := by"]},{"oldStart":195,"oldLines":10,"newStart":198,"newLines":13,"lines":["     dec2 h50bo = [false] ∧ dec3 h50bo = [false] := by","   decide"," ","-/-- H51 (an element of a storage owned by `v` holds a view on `v`): option 2 does not check `store`,","-so the blocking remains; option 3 rejects the `store`: in its arrival state, the root of the storage,","-held by `v`, and the view, held by the element, block each other. -/","+/-- H51 (an element of a storage owned by `v` holds a view on `v`): option 2 accepts the `store`, and","+would even if it checked `store`: the view is not self-locked, the configuration being a cycle of","+two authorities, which option 2 does not cover (material §5); the blocking remains. Option 3 rejects","+the `store`: in its arrival state, the root of the storage, held by `v`, and the view, held by the","+element, block each other. -/"," theorem H51_options : dec2 h51o = [true] ∧ dec3 h51o = [false] ∧","+    ¬ SelfLock (storeEff (run K0 [] (h51o.take 6)).s 4 3) 4 ∧","     Blocks (storeEff (run K0 [] (h51o.take 6)).s 4 3) 2 4 ∧","     Blocks (storeEff (run K0 [] (h51o.take 6)).s 4 3) 4 2 := by","   decide"]},{"oldStart":244,"oldLines":15,"newStart":250,"newLines":23,"lines":["   simp only [issueEff, S3.addAuth, List.getElem?_append_right (Nat.le_refl _), Nat.sub_self,","     List.getElem?_cons_zero, OptP, true_and, holderLeaves]"," ","-/-- Option 3 is not local: from two reached states that agree on the authority stored, 8 (same","-entry), on the target 6 (same footprint) and on the number of authorities, the `store 8 6` gets","-different decisions. They differ on the authority 7, which the step does not touch: stored into the","-node 5 in the first (H48), held by the frame in the second (its twin). -/","+/-- The states of `opt3_not_local`: the state of H48 with the helper 9 (`Modify` on the node 6,","+derived from 7), and the same run without the `store` of 7, which stays held by the frame. -/","+def nl1 : PS := run K0 [] (h48o ++ [.derive 7 6 .modify])","+def nl2 : PS := run K0 [] (fao ++ [.derive 6 6 .modify, .derive 5 5 .modify, .derive 7 6 .modify])","+","+/-- Option 3 is not local to the operation: in two reached states where the kernel accepts","+`store 8 6`, with the same places, the same stored authority 8 and as many authorities, the decisions","+differ. The states differ by the authority 7, which the step does not touch (stored into the node 5","+in the first, held by the frame in the second), and by the initialisation and anchors of the node 5,","+which option 3 does not read. Both states are in one frame (report, (g)). -/"," theorem opt3_not_local :","-    PReach K0 [] h48 ∧ PReach K0 [] h48t ∧ h48.s.A[8]? = h48t.s.A[8]? ∧","-    footprint h48.s.P 6 = footprint h48t.s.P 6 ∧ h48.s.A.length = h48t.s.A.length ∧","-    h48.s.A[7]? ≠ h48t.s.A[7]? ∧","-    ¬ NoLock (storeEff h48.s 8 6) ∧ NoLock (storeEff h48t.s 8 6) :=","-  ⟨H48.1, H48.2.2.1, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide⟩","+    PReach K0 [] nl1 ∧ PReach K0 [] nl2 ∧","+    StoreStep 8 6 nl1.s (.ok (storeEff nl1.s 8 6)) ∧ StoreStep 8 6 nl2.s (.ok (storeEff nl2.s 8 6)) ∧","+    nl1.s.P = nl2.s.P ∧ nl1.s.A[8]? = nl2.s.A[8]? ∧ nl1.s.A.length = nl2.s.A.length ∧","+    nl1.s.A[7]? ≠ nl2.s.A[7]? ∧ nl1.s.F = nl2.s.F ∧","+    ¬ NoLock (storeEff nl1.s 8 6) ∧ NoLock (storeEff nl2.s 8 6) :=","+  ⟨run_reach (by decide) (by decide), run_reach (by decide) (by decide), .ok (by decide),","+    .ok (by decide), by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide⟩"," "," end Ern.MM03.LockOptions"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/MM03/LockOptions.lean"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"9d97183f-91b6-4eb2-b5c9-cec13d29b13f","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/validation_0.1","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":2,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9851a3de-1a5b-4c33-bb1d-d4674dd7a69b","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/validation_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","hash":"1ba26f87b6389f54975ad66b31550d1f779a778b7738ccad7b3900d0cf68c6f2","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016CJSrjNqetLLdo9shGVz1D","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && SP=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad && cat > $SP/j3/fixlo.py <<'PYEOF'\np='Ern/MM03/LockOptions.lean'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:90]\n    s=s.replace(a,b,1)\nrep(\"\"\"`true` is acceptance. The cost: option 2 is decided from the authorities the operation moves and the\nplaces that receive them (`opt2_transfer_local`); option 3 is not, the decision depends on\nauthorities the operation does not touch (`opt3_not_local`). No option is adopted (material §5:\n\"la décision revient à l'arbitrage\").\"\"\",\"\"\"`true` is acceptance. The cost, measured as the brief asks (from the authorities and places the\noperation touches, or the whole state): option 2 on `transfer` depends on the state only through the\nplaces and the authorities the transfer moves (`opt2_transfer_local`), on `issue` only through the\nregion and the destination (`opt2_issue_local`); option 3 depends on authorities the operation does\nnot touch (`opt3_not_local`). Whether option 3 needs more than the function where the operation runs\n(material §5, \"locale à une fonction\") is not settled here (report, (g)). No option is adopted\n(material §5: \"la décision revient à l'arbitrage\").\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"   (\"W3v\", w3vo ++ [.endUse 2, .reset 0 0, .issue 0 0 [7] 3])]\"\"\",\"\"\"   (\"W3v\", w3vo ++ [.endUse 2, .reset 0 0, .issue 0 0 [10] 3])]\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"so the blocking of H49 remains; option 3 rejects the `store` that closes the cycle (the 7th checked\nstep), the helper notwithstanding. -/\"\"\",\"\"\"so the blocking of H49 remains; option 3 rejects the `store` that closes the cycle (the fourth checked\nstep), the helper notwithstanding. -/\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"/-- H51 (an element of a storage owned by `v` holds a view on `v`): option 2 does not check `store`,\nso the blocking remains; option 3 rejects the `store`: in its arrival state, the root of the storage,\nheld by `v`, and the view, held by the element, block each other. -/\ntheorem H51_options : dec2 h51o = [true] ∧ dec3 h51o = [false] ∧\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- H51 (an element of a storage owned by `v` holds a view on `v`): option 2 accepts the `store`, and\nwould even if it checked `store`: the view is not self-locked, the configuration being a cycle of\ntwo authorities, which option 2 does not cover (material §5); the blocking remains. Option 3 rejects\nthe `store`: in its arrival state, the root of the storage, held by `v`, and the view, held by the\nelement, block each other. -/\ntheorem H51_options : dec2 h51o = [true] ∧ dec3 h51o = [false] ∧\n    ¬ SelfLock (storeEff (run K0 [] (h51o.take 6)).s 4 3) 4 ∧\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"/-- Option 3 is not local: from two reached states that agree on the authority stored, 8 (same\nentry), on the target 6 (same footprint) and on the number of authorities, the `store 8 6` gets\ndifferent decisions. They differ on the authority 7, which the step does not touch: stored into the\nnode 5 in the first (H48), held by the frame in the second (its twin). -/\ntheorem opt3_not_local :\n    PReach K0 [] h48 ∧ PReach K0 [] h48t ∧ h48.s.A[8]? = h48t.s.A[8]? ∧\n    footprint h48.s.P 6 = footprint h48t.s.P 6 ∧ h48.s.A.length = h48t.s.A.length ∧\n    h48.s.A[7]? ≠ h48t.s.A[7]? ∧\n    ¬ NoLock (storeEff h48.s 8 6) ∧ NoLock (storeEff h48t.s 8 6) :=\n  ⟨H48.1, H48.2.2.1, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide⟩\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- The states of `opt3_not_local`: the state of H48 with the helper 9 (`Modify` on the node 6,\nderived from 7), and the same run without the `store` of 7, which stays held by the frame. -/\ndef nl1 : PS := run K0 [] (h48o ++ [.derive 7 6 .modify])\ndef nl2 : PS := run K0 [] (fao ++ [.derive 6 6 .modify, .derive 5 5 .modify, .derive 7 6 .modify])\n\n/-- Option 3 is not local to the operation: in two reached states where the kernel accepts\n`store 8 6`, with the same places, the same stored authority 8 and as many authorities, the decisions\ndiffer. The states differ by the authority 7, which the step does not touch (stored into the node 5\nin the first, held by the frame in the second), and by the initialisation and anchors of the node 5,\nwhich option 3 does not read. Both states are in one frame (report, (g)). -/\ntheorem opt3_not_local :\n    PReach K0 [] nl1 ∧ PReach K0 [] nl2 ∧\n    StoreStep 8 6 nl1.s (.ok (storeEff nl1.s 8 6)) ∧ StoreStep 8 6 nl2.s (.ok (storeEff nl2.s 8 6)) ∧\n    nl1.s.P = nl2.s.P ∧ nl1.s.A[8]? = nl2.s.A[8]? ∧ nl1.s.A.length = nl2.s.A.length ∧\n    nl1.s.A[7]? ≠ nl2.s.A[7]? ∧ nl1.s.F = nl2.s.F ∧\n    ¬ NoLock (storeEff nl1.s 8 6) ∧ NoLock (storeEff nl2.s 8 6) :=\n  ⟨run_reach (by decide) (by decide), run_reach (by decide) (by decide), .ok (by decide),\n    .ok (by decide), by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide⟩\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\npython3 $SP/j3/fixlo.py && python3 - <<'EOF'\nsrc=open('Ern/MM03/LockOptions.lean').read()\ni=src.index('/-- Every run of the list is `ok`')\nt=src[:i]+'''\n#eval mustAccept.all (fun c => (prun K0 (PS.init []) c.2).isSome)\n#eval mustAccept.map (fun c => (c.1, dec2 c.2, dec3 c.2))\nend Ern.MM03.LockOptions\n'''\nopen('/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/j3/lo.lean','w').write(t)\nEOF\n~/.elan/bin/lake env lean $SP/j3/lo.lean 2>&1 | tail -16","description":"Apply LockOptions fixes and recompute decisions","timeout":900000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
