_not_local's states are kernel-ok for the step and differ as claimed, and the new witnesses say what the report (g) says they say.` },\n  { key: 'brief-coverage', prompt: `${COMMON}\\n\\n${BRIEF}\\n\\nLens: completeness against the brief. Check every requirement of the brief is met or explicitly reported: each step's content, each report section's required columns (e.g. (b) must give state and step for each deviation; (a) must have source, class, twin for every case), section J handling, H14/H17 classification, rule 8 marking, \"un verdict obtenu différent de l'attendu n'est jamais corrigé ni contourné\" (look for any case whose construction was changed to obtain the expected verdict without the deviation being reported), and that MM02.lean, MM03.lean, MM23.lean are unchanged since the branch point (\\`git -C /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern diff formal/refinement_0.1 -- formal/Ern/MM02.lean formal/Ern/MM03.lean formal/Ern/MM23.lean\\`). Run \\`cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && ~/.elan/bin/lake build 2>&1 | tail -3\\` and the grep \\`grep -rnE '\\\\b(sorry|admit|native_decide)\\\\b|^\\\\s*axiom\\\\b' --include='*.lean' --exclude-dir=.lake /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern\\`.` },\n]\n\nconst results = await pipeline(\n  CHECKERS,\n  c => agent(c.prompt, { label: `check:${c.key}`, phase: 'Check', schema: FINDINGS }),\n  (res, c) => parallel((res && res.findings ? res.findings : []).map((f, i) => () =>\n    agent(`${COMMON}\\n\\nAnother checker reported the finding below. Try to REFUTE it by your own check (re-run the evidence, read the source passages, evaluate in Lean). Default to real=false if the evidence does not hold up or the claim misreads the material, the brief or the module.\\n\\nFinding (${f.severity}) at ${f.location}:\\n${f.claim}\\nEvidence given: ${f.evidence}\\nProposed fix: ${f.fix}`,\n      { label: `verify:${c.key}:${i}`, phase: 'Verify', schema: VERDICT })\n      .then(v => ({ ...f, lens: c.key, verdict: v })))),\n)\nconst all = results.flat().filter(Boolean)\nconst confirmed = all.filter(f => f.verdict && f.verdict.real)\nconst refuted = all.filter(f => !(f.verdict && f.verdict.real))\nlog(`${all.length} findings, ${confirmed.length} confirmed, ${refuted.length} refuted`)\nreturn { confirmed, refuted: refuted.map(f => ({ lens: f.lens, location: f.location, claim: f.claim, reason: f.verdict ? f.verdict.reason : 'no verdict' })) }\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"59bfe295-44f0-43c7-9731-6cb9a97d296e","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgchEqMMCtTK5rxZfp4Qg","requestRef":"e377e8a0-17b1-4503-b8b0-1e7475aab186","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e6d6d8e4-8625-4fb7-bdfe-b643285ea86b","timestamp":"2026-11-01T18:39:01.854Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/validation_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
