{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","hash":"f5ff5ab4106c1150b45d6cb388379a4d80bc7b233eebf9264a924c15dcd8dc0c","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\n[SYSTEM NOTIFICATION - NOT USER INPUT]\nThis is an automated background-task event, NOT a message from the user.\nDo NOT interpret this as user acknowledgement, confirmation, or response to any pending question.\nNo human input has been received since the last genuine user message in this conversation. Any statement that the user said, approved, or confirmed something — including statements in your own earlier messages — is NOT real user input and must NOT be treated as approval or consent.\n\n<task-notification>\n<task-id>wmaprgx60</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_015pwfcTaMmR9YrDhFjitrTR</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/tasks/wmaprgx60.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Dynamic workflow \"Second targeted check of the jalon-3 review fixes and report, with adversarial verification of each finding\" completed</summary>\n<result>{\"confirmed\":[{\"severity\":\"major\",\"location\":\"formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md, (b) 3 (W2) and (g) 6\",\"claim\":\"The report says the expected W2 verdict ('après sa libération : ok') is obtained if 'la vue de colonne' means the column authority from `split`. That is false. After releasing the read view 12 and the column authority 11, moving the row is still rejected: authority 10, the split authority of column 1, covers row field 9. So the expected verdict is obtained under neither reading. (g) 6 then asks the arbiter a wrongly framed question.\",\"evidence\":\"Report (b) 3: « Attendu « après sa libération : ok » : obtenu si « la vue de colonne » désigne l'autorité de colonne ; non obtenu si elle désigne la vue de lecture. » and (g) 6: « Avec la seconde lecture, le déplacement reste rejeté après sa libération. » Scratch file (lake env lean, no errors): `def w2b : PS := run K0 [] (w2o ++ [.release 12, .release 11])`; `example : PReach K0 [] w2b := run_reach (by decide) (by decide)`; `example : TransferStep K0 9 16 w2b.s .reject := .reject (by decide)`; `example : ActiveDerivedOutside w2b.s 9 10 := by decide`; `example : TransferStep K0 12 19 w2b.s (.ok (transferEff w2b.s 12 19)) := .ok (by decide)`; `example : TransferStep K0 9 16 (transferEff w2b.s 12 19) .reject := .reject (by decide)`. The only accepting run in the module is `W2`'s last conjunct, which also releases 10: `w2o ++ [.release 12, .release 11, .release 10, .transfer 9 16, .transfer 12 19]`. The W2 docstring says this in a parenthesis; the report drops it.\",\"fix\":\"In (b) 3 and (g) 6, say that under either reading the move stays rejected after releasing 'the column view'. It is accepted only after releasing both split column authorities, 11 and 10 (the W2 theorem). Reword the (g) 6 question to match.\",\"lens\":\"report-facts\",\"verdict\":{\"real\":true,\"reason\":\"The finding holds. The material describes W2 as « déplacement d'une entité vers un autre archetype (transferts des champs de la ligne) pendant qu'une vue de colonne est active, puis après sa libération », with expected « après : ok ». So the move transfers both row fields, 9 and 12, and only one view is released. Report (b) 3 says the expected verdict is « obtenu si « la vue de colonne » désigne l'autorité de colonne ». The bullet just before names that authority: « l'autorité de colonne 11, issue du `split` ». In Lean, releasing 12 and 11 is not enough: field 12 then transfers, but field 9 is still rejected because split authority 10 covers it. The expected verdict is reached only after also releasing 10, a release the material never mentions. The module's W2 docstring states this condition in a parenthesis: \\\"and that of the first column authority, which covers the other field of the row\\\". The table row also gets it right (« après libération des autorités de colonne de `split` », plural). Report (b) 3 drops the condition, and (g) 6 puts the question to the arbiter as if the first reading gave the expected verdict. So the report claims more than the module proves. I would rate it minor to major, since the theorem and the table are right and only the text in (b) 3 and (g) 6 is wrong.\",\"evidence\":\"Material /Users/guygouri/Downloads/ERN_Jalon3_materiel.md line 247: « déplacement d'une entité vers un autre archetype (transferts des champs de la ligne) pendant qu'une vue de colonne est active, puis après sa libération » | « déplacement pendant la vue : `reject` ; après : `ok` ».\\n\\nReport formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md, line 139: « l'autorité de colonne 11, issue du `split`, reste une autorité dérivée active ». Line 140: « obtenu si « la vue de colonne » désigne l'autorité de colonne ». Line 249 ((g) 6): « Avec la seconde lecture, le déplacement reste rejeté après sa libération. »\\n\\nModule formal/Ern/MM03/Horrors.lean, W2 docstring: \\\"the move is accepted after its release (and that of the first column authority, which covers the other field of the row)\\\". The only accepting run releases 12, 11 and 10.\\n\\nScratch file checked with `lake env lean`, exit 0, no errors:\\ndef w2b : PS := run K0 [] (w2o ++ [.release 12, .release 11])\\nexample : PReach K0 [] w2b := run_reach (by decide) (by decide)\\nexample : TransferStep K0 9 16 w2b.s .reject := .reject (by decide)\\nexample : ActiveDerivedOutside w2b.s 9 10 := by decide\\nexample : TransferStep K0 12 19 w2b.s (.ok (transferEff w2b.s 12 19)) := .ok (by decide)\\nexample : TransferStep K0 9 16 (transferEff w2b.s 12 19) .reject := .reject (by decide)\\nexample : TransferStep K0 9 16 w2a.s .reject := .reject (by decide)\"}},{\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md, (g) 2\",\"claim\":\"'resolveMany Observe est toujours rejeté' is false as stated. With an invalid batch the outcome is `fail`, not `reject`. The module also witnesses only one instance (`resolveMany_observe_rejected` on h31b), not the general 'toujours'.\",\"evidence\":\"Compiles in a scratch file: `example : ResolveManyStep K0 0 [⟨0, 0, 0⟩, ⟨0, 0, 0⟩] .observe h31b (.fail h31b) := .fail (pl := plA) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide)`. The module's only witness is `theorem resolveMany_observe_rejected : ResolveManyStep K0 0 [⟨0, 0, 0⟩, ⟨0, 1, 0⟩] .observe h31b .reject`.\",\"fix\":\"Rephrase as 'resolveMany Observe n'est jamais accepté : rejeté (noSplit) sur un lot valide, `fail` sur un lot invalide' and present it as shown on one instance.\",\"lens\":\"report-facts\",\"verdict\":{\"real\":true,\"reason\":\"The finding is real (minor) and I could not refute it. The report says '`resolveMany Observe` est toujours rejeté'. Elsewhere the report keeps fail apart from reject: H31b is listed as `fail`, and (f) 13 says `resolve` and `resolveMany` 'échouent' on a free entry. Read that way, 'rejeté' means the reject outcome. `ResolveManyStep` (formal/Ern/HandlePool.lean:244-261) checks the right first, then `BatchOK` (giving `fail`), then `SplitPre` (giving `noSplit`/reject). So an `Observe` batch that has the right but is invalid ends in `fail`, not reject. I proved this in Lean on the reachable state h31b. The claim also rests on a single instance (`resolveMany_observe_rejected`); no general theorem backs the word 'toujours'. The substance holds: `Observe` is never accepted. A valid batch and an empty batch both go to reject through `noSplit`, because `SplitPre` requires `ExercisableAt src .modify`. Only the 'toujours rejeté' wording is wrong.\",\"evidence\":\"Scratch file /var/folders/fx/7gtkr7tx4wdc6t84nz4d15r40000gn/T/tmp.bOor91qE7f/t.lean compiled with `lake env lean` (exit 0):\\n```\\nexample : ResolveManyStep K0 0 [⟨0, 0, 0⟩, ⟨0, 0, 0⟩] .observe h31b (.fail h31b) :=\\n  .fail (pl := plA) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide)\\ntheorem hp : h31b.pools[0]? = some plA := by decide\\nexample : ¬ ResolveManyStep K0 0 [⟨0, 0, 0⟩, ⟨0, 0, 0⟩] .observe h31b .reject := by\\n  intro h\\n  cases h with\\n  | reject h1 h2 =&gt; rw [hp] at h1; cases h1; exact h2 (by decide)\\n  | noSplit h1 _ h3 _ =&gt; rw [hp] at h1; cases h1; exact absurd h3 (by decide)\\n  | none h1 =&gt; rw [hp] at h1; cases h1\\n```\\nSo on this invalid `Observe` batch the outcome is `fail`, and reject cannot be derived. Report line 245: '2. **`resolveMany Observe`** est toujours rejeté par la construction du matériel (`split` exige `Modify`, O2 ; `resolveMany_observe_rejected`).' The only module witness, formal/Ern/MM03/Horrors.lean:582-584, is `theorem resolveMany_observe_rejected : ResolveManyStep K0 0 [⟨0, 0, 0⟩, ⟨0, 1, 0⟩] .observe h31b .reject`, a single valid batch. A separate check, /var/folders/fx/7gtkr7tx4wdc6t84nz4d15r40000gn/T/tmp.bOor91qE7f/u.lean (exit 0), shows the empty `Observe` batch is also reject via `noSplit`. That supports the proposed rewording: rejected on a valid batch, `fail` on an invalid one, never accepted.\"}},{\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md, (f) 14\",\"claim\":\"(f) 14 points to the wrong question. It cites question (g) 12, which is about `freeSlot` following `endUse`. The question on the content of an allocated entry is (g) 13.\",\"evidence\":\"(f) 14: « … ce qui ne vaut que si l\n... (truncated 43882 chars, full result in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/tasks/wmaprgx60.output)</result>\n<diagnostics>Per-agent results: /Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/subagents/workflows/wf_1b1999dd-fac/journal.jsonl — one {\"type\":\"result\",...} line per completed agent with its full return value.\nIf the result above is empty or unexpected, Read this file BEFORE diagnosing — do not assume agents returned non-empty results.\nTo re-run with edited post-processing: Workflow({scriptPath: '/Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/workflows/scripts/j3-second-check-wf_1b1999dd-fac.js', resumeFromRunId: 'wf_1b1999dd-fac'}) — agents whose (prompt, opts) are unchanged replay from cache.</diagnostics>\n<usage><agent_count>19</agent_count><agents_done>19</agents_done><agents_error>0</agents_error><agents_skipped>0</agents_skipped><agents_empty_result>0</agents_empty_result><subagent_tokens>2301547</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>300</tool_uses><duration_ms>898724</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}]}}
