loads(l) for l in open(j) if l.strip()]\nres=[r for r in rows if r.get('type')=='result']\nchecks=[r for r in res if isinstance(r['result'],dict) and 'findings' in r['result']]\nn=0\nfor c in checks:\n    for f in c['result']['findings']:\n        print(f\"F{n} [{f['severity']}] {f['location'][:110]}\\n  C: {f['claim'][:420]}\\n  FIX: {f['fix'][:300]}\")\n        n+=1\nEOF","description":"Print all second-check findings compactly"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"0b0792e5-1179-4d3e-884c-82ecff3e6830","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgciTc66hDJgJVvKqWCnb","requestRef":"9ad36039-c159-4893-aa83-9ca06ea8c9c4","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"6473be0b-aa31-4814-89fc-86459e896f0b","timestamp":"2026-11-01T18:54:26.959Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/validation_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
{"parentUuid":"6473be0b-aa31-4814-89fc-86459e896f0b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e1d83cab-fde8-4fcc-bb5d-dbd7211556dd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QVqqY62Av6sLWvRVpMagyF","type":"tool_result","content":"F0 [minor] formal/Ern/MM23/Horrors.lean:507 (r2i) and :557-559 (H06)\n  C: In H06, the `free` step runs under the contracts K2f, but the state it runs in is reached under K0. No Lean statement shows that state is reached under K2f, so the case is not one execution from the initial state under a single K (material §0 rule 3). The same commit fixed exactly this mismatch for H07 by adding `PReach KNS [] r7n`, but left H06 as it was. The verdict itself holds: restated under K2f it is decided tr\n  FIX: Define the H06 state under K2f, as `sst K2f [] π2 (r2.take 7)`, or add a conjunct that `srun K2f ... (r2.take 7)` succeeds. State `¬ OwnedRoot` and the `FreeStep K2f ... .reject` on that state.\nF1 [major] formal/Ern/MM23/Horrors.lean:638-670 (KL, H01); formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md:106\n  C: MM23-H01 is encoded with the byte instantiation of L7 (`DeclaredDisjoint := ByteDisjoint π4.L`), not the instantiation by leaf disjointness that the source names (decision 1 of jalon 2). As a result, \"régions déclarées ⇒ octets disjoints\" holds by definition, which is weaker than the source. The report still marks the case \"idem\". The substitution is not listed in (f) and is not reported as a deviation in (b) or (c).\n  FIX: Encode H01 with the leaf instantiation, which is a K parameter and needs no draft change. Prove the byte disjointness of the declared regions as a fact, by `decide` or `byteDisjoint_of_leaves`. If that is not done, report the substitution in (b) or (c) and list it in (f).\nF2 [major] formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md:137-140 ((b) 3), formal/Ern/MM03/LockOptions.lean:149, formal/Ern/MM03/Horrors.lean:\n  C: Point (b) 3 says the W2 expectation \"après sa libération : ok\" is met if \"la vue de colonne\" means the column authority. That is not true. Releasing that authority (11) and the read view (12) still leaves the move of the entity rejected, because system A's column authority 10 covers the row's other field. The run reaches `ok` only by adding `.release 10`, a step the scenario does not contain. (b) does not report this\n  FIX: In (b) 3, report the state `w2o ++ [release 12, release 11]` and the step `transfer 9 16` as rejected. State that `ok` also needs the release of authority 10. Extend question (g) 6 to cover it.\nF3 [minor] formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md:104-122 (MM23-H table); formal/Ern/MM23/Horrors.lean:553-559 (H06)\n  C: The brief requires (a) to give source, class and twin for every case. The MM23-H table has only the columns Cas, Théorème, Attendu and Obtenu, so no case has a source, class or twin; only H14 and H17 are classified. The MM23-H06 rejection (`FreeStep K2f 5 7 r2i.1 .reject`) has no accepted twin in the MM23 module (rule 2). Separately, W1–W3 are given class `Lib` in the MM3-H table, a choice the material does not make,\n  FIX: Add Source, Classe and Jumeau columns to the MM23-H table. Add an accepted twin for MM23-H06, or name an existing one. Record the class given to W1–W3 in (f).\nF4 [minor] formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md:95 (section J, H38)\n  C: For H38 the report says each branch runs in the kernel, but gives no witness. It neither confirms that H38 cannot be expressed nor flags it as expressible the way H42 is flagged with `J_H42_expansion`. The brief asks for exactly one of these.\n  FIX: Either add straight-line witnesses for the two branches and flag H38 as expressible, as for H42, or replace the claim with an explicit statement that H38 cannot be expressed.\nF5 [minor] formal/Ern/MM03/LockOptions.lean:217-220 (opt2_transfer_local); formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md:184,190\n  C: The brief asks whether the check reads only the authorities and places touched by the operation. The locality lemma for option 2 on `transfer` assumes the whole place list is equal, so it shows locality in authorities only. Locality in places is not shown, yet the (e) table records option 2 as \"locale\".\n  FIX: Weaken `hP` to equal places and footprints for the source, the destination and the holders involved. Otherwise, qualify the (e) verdict as local in authorities only.\nF6 [minor] formal/Ern/MM03/Horrors.lean:118-127 (H03)\n  C: The twin state `h03t` of H03 is never shown to be reached (rule 3). The same gap was fixed for H22 in 6cb3f1b (\"twin reached in H22\").\n  FIX: Add a `PReach K0 [] h03t` conjunct to H03, proved by `run_reach (by decide) (by decide)`.\nF7 [minor] formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md:256 ((g) 12, first bullet); formal/Ern/MM03/Horrors.lean:885 (docstring of pool_free\n  C: Two claims say more than the one witness supports. The report says a pool whose `internal` is derived \"(stockage local ou bloc d'arène, le cas de H44) ne peut jamais libérer une entrée\". The docstring says that `freeSlot` on any pool with a derived `internal` is rejected. Counterexample 1: a pool on local storage can have the root as `internal`, and then `freeSlot` is accepted. Counterexample 2: a pool with a derived\n  FIX: In both places, limit the statement to a live pool whose derived `internal` is held outside the entry. Give \"local storage owned directly by the frame\" and \"arena block (H44)\" as examples, and drop the unqualified \"stockage local\" and \"jamais\".\nF8 [minor] formal/Ern/MM03/Horrors.lean:322-327 (h17d and the H17 docstring); report (a), H17 row\n  C: The fix added the `KF45` state to show that `free` of the block is still rejected once the region is declared deallocable, and names the cause as `OwnedRoot`. In `h17d` the block 5 is still active, so a second clause also fails: `FreeAccessOK` (an active derived authority on the freed leaf, held outside it by the value 2). The witness therefore does not show that `OwnedRoot` alone rejects the step.\n  FIX: Build `h17d` on `h17p ++ [.issue 0 0 [5] 2, .endUse 2]`, where `OwnedRoot` is the only clause that fails. Alternatively, name both failing clauses (`OwnedRoot`, `FreeAccessOK`) in the docstring and in the report.\nF9 [minor] formal/Ern/MM03/LockOptions.lean:23-24 (module docstring, rewritten by 6cb3f1b)\n  C: The docstring attributes the quotation \"la décision revient à l'arbitrage\" to material §5. That phrase does not appear in the material. Material §5 states a different rule: options with a false rejection are excluded, and among the rest the cheapest to analyse wins.\n  FIX: Remove the quotation. Alternatively, cite where it actually comes from (the task brief, if that is the source) instead of material §5.\nF10 [major] formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md, (b) 3 (W2) and (g) 6\n  C: The report says the expected W2 verdict ('après sa libération : ok') is obtained if 'la vue de colonne' means the column authority from `split`. That is false. After releasing the read view 12 and the column authority 11, moving the row is still rejected: authority 10, the split authority of column 1, covers row field 9. So the expected verdict is obtained under neither reading. (g) 6 then asks the arbiter a wrongly \n  FIX: In (b) 3 and (g) 6, say that under either reading the move stays rejected after releasing 'the column view'. It is accepted only after releasing both split column authorities, 11 and 10 (the W2 theorem). Reword the (g) 6 question to match.\nF11 [minor] formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md, (g) 2\n  C: 'resolveMany Observe est toujours rejeté' is false as stated. With an invalid batch the outcome is `fail`, not `reject`. The module also witnesses only one instance (`resolveMany_observe_rejected` on h31b), not the general 'toujours'.\n  FIX: Rephrase as 'resolveMany Observe n'est jamais accepté : rejeté (noSplit) sur un lot valide, `fail` sur un lot invalide' and present it as shown on one instance.\nF12 [minor] formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md, (f) 14\n  C: (f) 14 points to the wrong question. It cites question (g) 12, which is about `freeSlot` following `endUse`. The question on the content of an allocated entry is (g) 13.\n  FIX: Replace 'question (g) 12' with 'question (g) 13' in (f) 14.\nF13 [minor] formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md, (a) rows H03, H11, H48, H51; (b) 1; (b) 3; (b) 4; (e) option 3 / H50\n  C: Several clause-level causes and verdicts in the report have no module witness. The theorems prove only the reject/ok outcome. I decided each claim true in scratch files, but none is stated in a module.\n  FIX: Either add these decided conjuncts to the corresponding theorems (H03, H11, H16, H48, H51, W2, W3, H50_options), or mark the causes in the report as not formalized.\nF14 [minor] formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md, (a) section J (H38); (b) 1; (b) 2; (g) 12\n  C: Several general or execution claims have no module witness at all, or only a single instance behind a universal statement: H38 (« chaque branche s'exécute séparément dans le noyau, sans exemple Lean »); (b) 1 (« Un appelé ne peut donc prendre une valeur de l'appelant par transfert »); (b) 2 (« La seule construction qui atteint `enterFrame` avec les deux paramètres … »); (g) 12 (« ne peut jamais libérer une entrée »).\n  FIX: State these as observations on the cited runs, not as general facts, or say they are unproven. For H38, either add the two branch runs or drop the execution claim.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"968a2adb-e1a1-4c64-8319-3f08e34d33a3","timestamp":"2026-11-01T18:54:27.244Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"F0 [minor] formal/Ern/MM23/Horrors.lean:507 (r2i) and :557-559 (H06)\n  C: In H06, the `free` step runs under the contracts K2f, but the state it runs in is reached under K0. No Lean statement shows that state is reached under K2f, so the case is not one execution from the initial state under a single K (material §0 rule 3). The same commit fixed exactly this mismatch for H07 by adding `PReach KNS [] r7n`, but left H06 as it was. The verdict itself holds: restated under K2f it is decided tr\n  FIX: Define the H06 state under K2f, as `sst K2f [] π2 (r2.take 7)`, or add a conjunct that `srun K2f ... (r2.take 7)` succeeds. State `¬ OwnedRoot` and the `FreeStep K2f ... .reject` on that state.\nF1 [major] formal/Ern/MM23/Horrors.lean:638-670 (KL, H01); formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md:106\n  C: MM23-H01 is encoded with the byte instantiation of L7 (`DeclaredDisjoint := ByteDisjoint π4.L`), not the instantiation by leaf disjointness that the source names (decision 1 of jalon 2). As a result, \"régions déclarées ⇒ octets disjoints\" holds by definition, which is weaker than the source. The report still marks the case \"idem\". The substitution is not listed in (f) and is not reported as a deviation in (b) or (c).\n  FIX: Encode H01 with the leaf instantiation, which is a K parameter and needs no draft change. Prove the byte disjointness of the declared regions as a fact, by `decide` or `byteDisjoint_of_leaves`. If that is not done, report the substitution in (b) or (c) and list it in (f).\nF2 [major] formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md:137-140 ((b) 3), formal/Ern/MM03/LockOptions.lean:149, formal/Ern/MM03/Horrors.lean:\n  C: Point (b) 3 says the W2 expectation \"après sa libération : ok\" is met if \"la vue de colonne\" means the column authority. That is not true. Releasing that authority (11) and the read view (12) still leaves the move of the entity rejected, because system A's column authority 10 covers the row's other field. The run reaches `ok` only by adding `.release 10`, a step the scenario does not contain. (b) does not report this\n  FIX: In (b) 3, report the state `w2o ++ [release 12, release 11]` and the step `transfer 9 16` as rejected. State that `ok` also needs the release of authority 10. Extend question (g) 6 to cover it.\nF3 [minor] formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md:104-122 (MM23-H table); formal/Ern/MM23/Horrors.lean:553-559 (H06)\n  C: The brief requires (a) to give source, class and twin for every case. The MM23-H table has only the columns Cas, Théorème, Attendu and Obtenu, so no case has a source, class or twin; only H14 and H17 are classified. The MM23-H06 rejection (`FreeStep K2f 5 7 r2i.1 .reject`) has no accepted twin in the MM23 module (rule 2). Separately, W1–W3 are given class `Lib` in the MM3-H table, a choice the material does not make,\n  FIX: Add Source, Classe and Jumeau columns to the MM23-H table. Add an accepted twin for MM23-H06, or name an existing one. Record the class given to W1–W3 in (f).\nF4 [minor] formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md:95 (section J, H38)\n  C: For H38 the report says each branch runs in the kernel, but gives no witness. It neither confirms that H38 cannot be expressed nor flags it as expressible the way H42 is flagged with `J_H42_expansion`. The brief asks for exactly one of these.\n  FIX: Either add straight-line witnesses for the two branches and flag H38 as expressible, as for H42, or replace the claim with an explicit statement that H38 cannot be expressed.\nF5 [minor] formal/Ern/MM03/LockOptions.lean:217-220 (opt2_transfer_local); formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md:184,190\n  C: The brief asks whether the check reads only the authorities and places touched by the operation. The locality lemma for option 2 on `transfer` assumes the whole place list is equal, so it shows locality in authorities only. Locality in places is not shown, yet the (e) table records option 2 as \"locale\".\n  FIX: Weaken `hP` to equal places and footprints for the source, the destination and the holders involved. Otherwise, qualify the (e) verdict as local in authorities only.\nF6 [minor] formal/Ern/MM03/Horrors.lean:118-127 (H03)\n  C: The twin state `h03t` of H03 is never shown to be reached (rule 3). The same gap was fixed for H22 in 6cb3f1b (\"twin reached in H22\").\n  FIX: Add a `PReach K0 [] h03t` conjunct to H03, proved by `run_reach (by decide) (by decide)`.\nF7 [minor] formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md:256 ((g) 12, first bullet); formal/Ern/MM03/Horrors.lean:885 (docstring of pool_free\n  C: Two claims say more than the one witness supports. The report says a pool whose `internal` is derived \"(stockage local ou bloc d'arène, le cas de H44) ne peut jamais libérer une entrée\". The docstring says that `freeSlot` on any pool with a derived `internal` is rejected. Counterexample 1: a pool on local storage can have the root as `internal`, and then `freeSlot` is accepted. Counterexample 2: a pool with a derived\n  FIX: In both places, limit the statement to a live pool whose derived `internal` is held outside the entry. Give \"local storage owned directly by the frame\" and \"arena block (H44)\" as examples, and drop the unqualified \"stockage local\" and \"jamais\".\nF8 [minor] formal/Ern/MM03/Horrors.lean:322-327 (h17d and the H17 docstring); report (a), H17 row\n  C: The fix added the `KF45` state to show that `free` of the block is still rejected once the region is declared deallocable, and names the cause as `OwnedRoot`. In `h17d` the block 5 is still active, so a second clause also fails: `FreeAccessOK` (an active derived authority on the freed leaf, held outside it by the value 2). The witness therefore does not show that `OwnedRoot` alone rejects the step.\n  FIX: Build `h17d` on `h17p ++ [.issue 0 0 [5] 2, .endUse 2]`, where `OwnedRoot` is the only clause that fails. Alternatively, name both failing clauses (`OwnedRoot`, `FreeAccessOK`) in the docstring and in the report.\nF9 [minor] formal/Ern/MM03/LockOptions.lean:23-24 (module docstring, rewritten by 6cb3f1b)\n  C: The docstring attributes the quotation \"la décision revient à l'arbitrage\" to material §5. That phrase does not appear in the material. Material §5 states a different rule: options with a false rejection are excluded, and among the rest the cheapest to analyse wins.\n  FIX: Remove the quotation. Alternatively, cite where it actually comes from (the task brief, if that is the source) instead of material §5.\nF10 [major] formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md, (b) 3 (W2) and (g) 6\n  C: The report says the expected W2 verdict ('après sa libération : ok') is obtained if 'la vue de colonne' means the column authority from `split`. That is false. After releasing the read view 12 and the column authority 11, moving the row is still rejected: authority 10, the split authority of column 1, covers row field 9. So the expected verdict is obtained under neither reading. (g) 6 then asks the arbiter a wrongly \n  FIX: In (b) 3 and (g) 6, say that under either reading the move stays rejected after releasing 'the column view'. It is accepted only after releasing both split column authorities, 11 and 10 (the W2 theorem). Reword the (g) 6 question to match.\nF11 [minor] formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md, (g) 2\n  C: 'resolveMany Observe est toujours rejeté' is false as stated. With an invalid batch the outcome is `fail`, not `reject`. The module also witnesses only one instance (`resolveMany_observe_rejected` on h31b), not the general 'toujours'.\n  FIX: Rephrase as 'resolveMany Observe n'est jamais accepté : rejeté (noSplit) sur un lot valide, `fail` sur un lot invalide' and present it as shown on one instance.\nF12 [minor] formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md, (f) 14\n  C: (f) 14 points to the wrong question. It cites question (g) 12, which is about `freeSlot` following `endUse`. The question on the content of an allocated entry is (g) 13.\n  FIX: Replace 'question (g) 12' with 'question (g) 13' in (f) 14.\nF13 [minor] formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md, (a) rows H03, H11, H48, H51; (b) 1; (b) 3; (b) 4; (e) option 3 / H50\n  C: Several clause-level causes and verdicts in the report have no module witness. The theorems prove only the reject/ok outcome. I decided each claim true in scratch files, but none is stated in a module.\n  FIX: Either add these decided conjuncts to the corresponding theorems (H03, H11, H16, H48, H51, W2, W3, H50_options), or mark the causes in the report as not formalized.\nF14 [minor] formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md, (a) section J (H38); (b) 1; (b) 2; (g) 12\n  C: Several general or execution claims have no module witness at all, or only a single instance behind a universal statement: H38 (« chaque branche s'exécute séparément dans le noyau, sans exemple Lean »); (b) 1 (« Un appelé ne peut donc prendre une valeur de l'appelant par transfert »); (b) 2 (« La seule construction qui atteint `enterFrame` avec les deux paramètres … »); (g) 12 (« ne peut jamais libérer une entrée »).\n  FIX: State these as observations on the cited runs, not as general facts, or say they are unproven. For H38, either add the two branch runs or drop the execution claim.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0b0792e5-1179-4d3e-884c-82ecff3e6830","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/validation_0.1","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6473be0b-aa31-4814-89fc-86459e896f0b","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/validation_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
