eePre` is a plain conjunction (formal/Ern/MM03.lean:4159-4164). So the proven `¬ OwnedRoot h17d.s 5` is enough by itself to make `FreePre` false and the step a reject, whatever the other clauses say. The witness therefore does show that `OwnedRoot` alone rejects the step. The docstring says \"still rejected (`OwnedRoot`)\". That names one sufficient cause. It does not claim `OwnedRoot` is the only failing clause, so it is not a wrong claim. The statement is not weaker than its source either: the material's H17 row (§1.C) ask \n\nREFUTED: The finding is not a defect. Every claim it lists is true, and the finder agrees. None of them is wrong or weaker than its source, and the brief does not require them to be stated in a module. The brief asks (b) to give each discrepancy \"avec l'état et le pas en cause\", and the report does: h16a with `transfer 1 4`, w2a with `transfer 12 19`, w3e with `reset 0 0`. Neither the brief nor material §0 asks for a module theorem for each failing or holding precondition clause. The proposed fix only adds conjuncts to theorems, and AGENTS.md says a review must \"Never ask for additions beyond the task\". Two of the items are also covered more than the finding allows:\n- H50, option 3, \"auto-blocage\": `","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e41defe6-d93d-4321-a75d-2f05afa73c46","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/validation_0.1","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"