{"parentUuid":"d604b86f-17c0-48d2-8b38-b3bf07755b70","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e1d83cab-fde8-4fcc-bb5d-dbd7211556dd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011M8hARNcFh7tXzHsDH4CzY","type":"tool_result","content":"631:/-! ## Run R4: declared disjointness (H01) -/\n/-! ## Run R4: declared disjointness (H01) -/\n\n/-- R4: frame 1 with the structure 0 of the parts 1 and 2. -/\ndef r4 : List Op3 := [.enter [] [lf, (some 0, none, 0), (some 0, none, 0)]]\ndef P4 : List Place := (Ern.MM03.Horrors.run K0 [] (r4.map toOp)).s.P\ndef π4 : Params := piOf P4 []\n\n/-- L7: the contracts whose `DeclaredDisjoint` is the byte disjointness of the leaves of the two\nregions under the layout of R4. -/\ndef KL : K := { K0 with DeclaredDisjoint := ByteDisjoint π4.L }\n\ninstance : ∀ r r', Decidable (KL.DeclaredDisjoint r r') := fun r r' => by\n  show Decidable (ByteDisjoint π4.L r r'); unfold ByteDisjoint; infer_instance\ninstance : DecidablePred KL.SharedMutable := fun l => inferInstanceAs (Decidable (l ∈ ([] : List Nat)))\ninstance : DecidablePred KL.Pinned := fun l => inferInstanceAs (Decidable (l ∈ ([] : List Nat)))\ninstance : DecidablePred KL.ExternalDone := fun l => inferInstanceAs (Decidable (l ∈ ([] : List Nat)))\ninstance : DecidablePred KL.Deallocable := fun l => inferInstanceAs (Decidable (l ∈ ([] : List Nat)))\ninstance : ∀ p a, Decidable (KL.FreeCompat p a) := fun p a =>\n  inferInstanceAs (Decidable ((p, a) ∈ ([] : List (Nat × Nat))))\ninstance : ∀ p ls s, Decidable (KL.Satisfiable p ls s) := fun _ _ _ => instDecidableTrue\n\n/-- `DDSound` of `KL` (L7, `ddSound_instance`): every leaf of the layout has a non-empty range. -/\ntheorem KL_dd : DDSound KL :=\n  ddSound_instance K0 (L := π4.L) fun l => by unfold π4 piOf autoL; simp\n\ndef r4s : SSt := sst KL [] π4 r4\n\n/-- **MM23-H01** (passe 2, `ddSound_of_layout`). With `DeclaredDisjoint` instantiated by the byte\ndisjointness of the leaves, two regions sharing the leaf 2 are not declared disjoint, and their\n`split` is rejected; the regions `[1]` and `[2]` are declared disjoint, with disjoint bytes, and\ntheir `split` runs in a translated execution, `DDSound` holding. Expected: rejected through\n`DDSound`, declared regions with disjoint bytes; obtained: the same. -/\ntheorem H01 : DDSound KL ∧ ¬ KL.DeclaredDisjoint [1, 2] [2] ∧ SplitStep KL 0 [[1, 2], [2]] r4s.1 .reject ∧\n    ByteDisjoint π4.L [1] [2] ∧\n    ∃ os, AllOk Ceq CaseSim.obR CaseSim.obW MM02.State.empty os ∧\n      Repr π4.tok π4.ptok (sst KL [] π4 (r4 ++ [.split 0 [[1], [2]]])).2.1 π4.L\n        (sst KL [] π4 (r4 ++ [.split 0 [[1], [2]]])).1 (sst KL [] π4 (r4 ++ [.split 0 [[1], [2]]])).2.2 :=\n  ⟨KL_dd, by decide, .reject (by decide), (show KL.DeclaredDisjoint [1] [2] by decide),\n    (sim_of (P := P4) (z := []) KL_dd (by decide) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide)).imp\n      fun _ h => ⟨h.1, h.2.2.1⟩⟩\n\n/-! ## Run R5: pointers to empty regions (H15, écart connu) -/\n\n/-- R5: frame 1 with the arena value 0, the allocator 1, the leaves 2, 3, 4; storage 5 with the\nleaf 6, owned by 0, `internal` 5; `issue []` to 2; `split` of the root of 3 into `[[]]`, then\n`store` of that empty authority 7 into 4. -/\n96:- `lwf`: `LayoutWF` (K1);\n112:  lwf : LayoutWF L s3 s2\n413:  · exact hR.lwf.sameAlloc","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"444ff364-5315-420a-ae26-2af9db002f2d","timestamp":"2026-11-01T18:55:27.296Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"631:/-! ## Run R4: declared disjointness (H01) -/\n/-! ## Run R4: declared disjointness (H01) -/\n\n/-- R4: frame 1 with the structure 0 of the parts 1 and 2. -/\ndef r4 : List Op3 := [.enter [] [lf, (some 0, none, 0), (some 0, none, 0)]]\ndef P4 : List Place := (Ern.MM03.Horrors.run K0 [] (r4.map toOp)).s.P\ndef π4 : Params := piOf P4 []\n\n/-- L7: the contracts whose `DeclaredDisjoint` is the byte disjointness of the leaves of the two\nregions under the layout of R4. -/\ndef KL : K := { K0 with DeclaredDisjoint := ByteDisjoint π4.L }\n\ninstance : ∀ r r', Decidable (KL.DeclaredDisjoint r r') := fun r r' => by\n  show Decidable (ByteDisjoint π4.L r r'); unfold ByteDisjoint; infer_instance\ninstance : DecidablePred KL.SharedMutable := fun l => inferInstanceAs (Decidable (l ∈ ([] : List Nat)))\ninstance : DecidablePred KL.Pinned := fun l => inferInstanceAs (Decidable (l ∈ ([] : List Nat)))\ninstance : DecidablePred KL.ExternalDone := fun l => inferInstanceAs (Decidable (l ∈ ([] : List Nat)))\ninstance : DecidablePred KL.Deallocable := fun l => inferInstanceAs (Decidable (l ∈ ([] : List Nat)))\ninstance : ∀ p a, Decidable (KL.FreeCompat p a) := fun p a =>\n  inferInstanceAs (Decidable ((p, a) ∈ ([] : List (Nat × Nat))))\ninstance : ∀ p ls s, Decidable (KL.Satisfiable p ls s) := fun _ _ _ => instDecidableTrue\n\n/-- `DDSound` of `KL` (L7, `ddSound_instance`): every leaf of the layout has a non-empty range. -/\ntheorem KL_dd : DDSound KL :=\n  ddSound_instance K0 (L := π4.L) fun l => by unfold π4 piOf autoL; simp\n\ndef r4s : SSt := sst KL [] π4 r4\n\n/-- **MM23-H01** (passe 2, `ddSound_of_layout`). With `DeclaredDisjoint` instantiated by the byte\ndisjointness of the leaves, two regions sharing the leaf 2 are not declared disjoint, and their\n`split` is rejected; the regions `[1]` and `[2]` are declared disjoint, with disjoint bytes, and\ntheir `split` runs in a translated execution, `DDSound` holding. Expected: rejected through\n`DDSound`, declared regions with disjoint bytes; obtained: the same. -/\ntheorem H01 : DDSound KL ∧ ¬ KL.DeclaredDisjoint [1, 2] [2] ∧ SplitStep KL 0 [[1, 2], [2]] r4s.1 .reject ∧\n    ByteDisjoint π4.L [1] [2] ∧\n    ∃ os, AllOk Ceq CaseSim.obR CaseSim.obW MM02.State.empty os ∧\n      Repr π4.tok π4.ptok (sst KL [] π4 (r4 ++ [.split 0 [[1], [2]]])).2.1 π4.L\n        (sst KL [] π4 (r4 ++ [.split 0 [[1], [2]]])).1 (sst KL [] π4 (r4 ++ [.split 0 [[1], [2]]])).2.2 :=\n  ⟨KL_dd, by decide, .reject (by decide), (show KL.DeclaredDisjoint [1] [2] by decide),\n    (sim_of (P := P4) (z := []) KL_dd (by decide) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide)).imp\n      fun _ h => ⟨h.1, h.2.2.1⟩⟩\n\n/-! ## Run R5: pointers to empty regions (H15, écart connu) -/\n\n/-- R5: frame 1 with the arena value 0, the allocator 1, the leaves 2, 3, 4; storage 5 with the\nleaf 6, owned by 0, `internal` 5; `issue []` to 2; `split` of the root of 3 into `[[]]`, then\n`store` of that empty authority 7 into 4. -/\n96:- `lwf`: `LayoutWF` (K1);\n112:  lwf : LayoutWF L s3 s2\n413:  · exact hR.lwf.sameAlloc","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"409df479-3920-49d1-a325-bc658305102e","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/validation_0.1","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d604b86f-17c0-48d2-8b38-b3bf07755b70","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/validation_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
