{"parentUuid":"bfa4c86d-d837-4509-9f3e-1d551356e3d3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgciYUwdMkYCNp4a9Q43s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Re-encoding MM23-H01 using leaf disjointness, with byte disjointness derived via `byteDisjoint_of_leaves`, while also applying the H06/H02 twins, the H06 state contract, and the MM3-H additions (H03 twin, W2 witness, general `transfer` lemma, restricted docstrings).\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2588,"cache_read_input_tokens":885349,"output_tokens":8768,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3218},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2588,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8768,"cache_read_input_tokens":885349,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2588,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2588},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":2,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"1e115655-c51e-420a-b241-fa664a5e2e84","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgciYUemNqm1SBBFmt4qN","requestRef":"f4e98646-94e2-4006-a2d7-8e4caef94be0","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c93ba93c-6bc3-4ce6-85f2-9ab8fa822689","timestamp":"2026-11-01T18:55:55.133Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/validation_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
{"parentUuid":"c93ba93c-6bc3-4ce6-85f2-9ab8fa822689","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgciYUwdMkYCNp4a9Q43s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0195KdDhG5SpKTju675ibAcr","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"SP=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad && cat > $SP/j3/fix2.py <<'PYEOF'\nimport re\np='Ern/MM23/Horrors.lean'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b,src=None):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:90]\n    s=s.replace(a,b,1)\ni=s.index(\"/-- L7: the contracts whose `DeclaredDisjoint` is the byte disjointness\")\nj=s.index(\"/-! ## Run R5\")\ns=s[:i]+'''/-- Decision 1 of jalon 2, the source of MM23-H01: the contracts whose `DeclaredDisjoint` is the\ndisjointness of the leaves of the two regions, as a parameter `K` (the draft `MM23` is unchanged). -/\ndef KLf : K := { K0 with DeclaredDisjoint := fun r r' => ∀ l ∈ r, l ∉ r' }\n\ninstance : ∀ r r', Decidable (KLf.DeclaredDisjoint r r') := fun r r' =>\n  inferInstanceAs (Decidable (∀ l ∈ r, l ∉ r'))\ninstance : DecidablePred KLf.SharedMutable := fun l =>\n  inferInstanceAs (Decidable (l ∈ ([] : List Nat)))\ninstance : DecidablePred KLf.Pinned := fun l => inferInstanceAs (Decidable (l ∈ ([] : List Nat)))\ninstance : DecidablePred KLf.ExternalDone := fun l =>\n  inferInstanceAs (Decidable (l ∈ ([] : List Nat)))\ninstance : DecidablePred KLf.Deallocable := fun l =>\n  inferInstanceAs (Decidable (l ∈ ([] : List Nat)))\ninstance : ∀ p a, Decidable (KLf.FreeCompat p a) := fun p a =>\n  inferInstanceAs (Decidable ((p, a) ∈ ([] : List (Nat × Nat))))\ninstance : ∀ p ls s, Decidable (KLf.Satisfiable p ls s) := fun _ _ _ => instDecidableTrue\n\n/-- `DDSound` of the instantiation by leaf disjointness: immediate (MM-03.3.8). -/\ntheorem KLf_dd : DDSound KLf := fun _ _ h => h\n\ndef r4s : SSt := sst KLf [] π4 r4\n/-- R4 after the `split` of the structure into the regions `[1]` and `[2]`. -/\ndef r4d : SSt := sst KLf [] π4 (r4 ++ [.split 0 [[1], [2]]])\n\n/-- **MM23-H01** (decision 1 of jalon 2; L7, `byteDisjoint_of_leaves`). With `DeclaredDisjoint`\ninstantiated by the disjointness of the leaves, two regions sharing the leaf 2 are not declared\ndisjoint and their `split` is rejected; the regions `[1]` and `[2]` are declared disjoint and their\n`split` runs in a translated execution. In its MM-02 state, every pair of declared regions of leaves\nhas disjoint bytes, through `LayoutWF` of `Repr`. Expected: rejected through `DDSound`\n(instantiation by leaves), declared regions with disjoint bytes; obtained: the same. -/\ntheorem H01 : DDSound KLf ∧ ¬ KLf.DeclaredDisjoint [1, 2] [2] ∧\n    SplitStep KLf 0 [[1, 2], [2]] r4s.1 .reject ∧ KLf.DeclaredDisjoint [1] [2] ∧\n    SplitStep KLf 0 [[1], [2]] r4s.1 (.ok (splitEff r4s.1 0 [[1], [2]])) ∧\n    (∃ os, AllOk Ceq CaseSim.obR CaseSim.obW MM02.State.empty os ∧\n      Repr π4.tok π4.ptok r4d.2.1 π4.L r4d.1 r4d.2.2) ∧\n    ∀ r r', KLf.DeclaredDisjoint r r' → (∀ l ∈ r, l < r4d.1.P.length ∧ isLeaf r4d.1.P l) →\n      (∀ l ∈ r', l < r4d.1.P.length ∧ isLeaf r4d.1.P l) → ByteDisjoint π4.L r r' := by\n  obtain ⟨os, hok, -, hR, -⟩ := sim_of (k := KLf) (statics := []) (P := P4) (z := [])\n    (ops := r4 ++ [.split 0 [[1], [2]]]) KLf_dd (by decide) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide)\n  exact ⟨KLf_dd, by decide, .reject (by decide), by decide, .ok (by decide), ⟨os, hok, hR⟩,\n    fun r r' hd hr hr' => byteDisjoint_of_leaves hR.lwf hr hr' hd⟩\n\n'''+s[j:]\n# H06 under K2f with twin; H02 twin\nrep(\"\"\"theorem H06 : K2f.Deallocable 5 ∧ K2f.FreeCompat 5 7 ∧ ¬ OwnedRoot r2i.1 5 ∧\n    FreeStep K2f 5 7 r2i.1 .reject ∧ (π2.L 5).alloc = (π2.L 4).alloc :=\n  ⟨by decide, by decide, by decide, .reject (by decide), by decide⟩\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- R2 under `K2f` before the transfer, and after the end of the block value. -/\ndef r2k : SSt := sst K2f [] π2 (r2.take 7)\ndef r2kt : SSt := sst K2f [] π2 (r2.take 10)\n\ntheorem H06 : Reachable K2f [] r2k.1 ∧ K2f.Deallocable 5 ∧ K2f.FreeCompat 5 7 ∧\n    ¬ OwnedRoot r2k.1 5 ∧ FreeStep K2f 5 7 r2k.1 .reject ∧ (π2.L 5).alloc = (π2.L 4).alloc ∧\n    Reachable K2f [] r2kt.1 ∧ FreeStep K2f 4 7 r2kt.1 (.ok (freeEff r2kt.1 4)) :=\n  ⟨(sim_of (k := K2f) (statics := []) (P := P2) (z := []) (ops := r2.take 7)\n      (KT_dd [] [] [] [4, 5] [(4, 7), (5, 7)]) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide)\n      (by decide)).2.2.2.2,\n    by decide, by decide, by decide, .reject (by decide), by decide,\n    (sim_of (k := K2f) (statics := []) (P := P2) (z := []) (ops := r2.take 10)\n      (KT_dd [] [] [] [4, 5] [(4, 7), (5, 7)]) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide)\n      (by decide)).2.2.2.2, .ok (by decide)⟩\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"allocation; obtained: the same. -/\ntheorem H06\"\"\",\"\"\"allocation; obtained: the same. Every state is reached under `K2f`. Twin: in the same run, once the\nblock value has ended, the `free` of the allocated storage 4 is accepted. -/\ntheorem H06\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"theorem H02 : ¬ r2f.1.Active 5 ∧ Read3Step 5 [5] r2f.1 .reject ∧\"\"\",\"\"\"theorem H02 : ¬ r2f.1.Active 5 ∧ Read3Step 5 [5] r2f.1 .reject ∧ Read3Step 5 [5] r2i.1 (.ok r2i.1) ∧\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  ⟨by decide, .reject (by decide), fun _ hs ha =>\"\"\",\"\"\"  ⟨by decide, .reject (by decide), .ok (by decide), fun _ hs ha =>\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"R2 the block was already released by `endUse q`, which `reset` requires (O19.2). Expected: no safe\nprogram reaches it, MM-02 would accept it; obtained: the same. -/\"\"\",\"\"\"R2 the block was already released by `endUse q`, which `reset` requires (O19.2). Twin: the same read\nthrough the block before its end is accepted. Expected: no safe program reaches it, MM-02 would\naccept it; obtained: the same. -/\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='Ern/MM03/Horrors.lean'\ns=open(p).read()\nrep(\"\"\"theorem H03 : PReach K0 [] h03 ∧ Write3Step 0 [1] h03.s .reject ∧\n    Write3Step 0 [1] h03t.s (.ok (write3Eff h03t.s [1])) :=\n  ⟨run_reach (by decide) (by decide), .reject (by decide), .ok (by decide)⟩\"\"\",\"\"\"theorem H03 : PReach K0 [] h03 ∧ Write3Step 0 [1] h03.s .reject ∧ PReach K0 [] h03t ∧\n    Write3Step 0 [1] h03t.s (.ok (write3Eff h03t.s [1])) :=\n  ⟨run_reach (by decide) (by decide), .reject (by decide), run_reach (by decide) (by decide),\n    .ok (by decide)⟩\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"/-- Contracts with the place 3 deallocable by the authority 7. -/\nabbrev KF3\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- A `transfer` is rejected while an active derived authority held by a frame covers a leaf of the\nsource (MM-03.3 §3, O4.4, `ActiveDerivedOutside`): a callee cannot transfer out of the footprint of\none of its parameters (H16, H07). -/\ntheorem transfer_rejected_by_frame_held {k : K} {s : S3} {src dst j f : Nat} {y : Authority}\n    (hy : s.A[j]? = some y) (ha : y.active = true) (ho : y.origin ≠ none)\n    (hh : y.holder = .frame f) (hl : ∃ l ∈ y.footprint, l ∈ footprint s.P src) :\n    TransferStep k src dst s .reject := by\n  have had : ActiveDerivedOutside s src j := by\n    unfold ActiveDerivedOutside; rw [hy]; exact ⟨ha, ho, by rw [hh]; exact id, hl⟩\n  exact .reject fun hpre =>\n    hpre.2.2.2.2.2.2.2.2.1 j (List.mem_range.2 (lt_of_getElem? hy)) had\n\n/-- Contracts with the place 3 deallocable by the authority 7. -/\nabbrev KF3\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"def w2a : PS := run K0 [] (w2o ++ [.release 12])\"\"\",\"\"\"def w2a : PS := run K0 [] (w2o ++ [.release 12])\n/-- W2 after the release of the read view 12 and of the column authority 11. -/\ndef w2b : PS := run K0 [] (w2o ++ [.release 12, .release 11])\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"/-- **W2** (§5b, ECS archetype and sparse set; Lib). Expected: disjoint reads and writes `ok`;\n`resolveMany` `ok`; the move of a field of the row while the column view is active: reject; after\nits release: `ok`. Obtained: disjoint accesses, `resolveMany` and the rejection during the view as\nexpected. After the release: if \"the view of the column\" is the read view 12, the move is still\nrejected, by the column authority 11 given by `split` (O4.4; report, (b)); if it is the column\nauthority itself, the move is accepted after its release (and that of the first column authority,\nwhich covers the other field of the row). -/\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- **W2** (§5b, ECS archetype and sparse set; Lib). Expected: disjoint reads and writes `ok`;\n`resolveMany` `ok`; the move of the row (transfers of its fields) while a column view is active:\nreject; after its release: `ok`. Obtained: disjoint accesses, `resolveMany` and the rejection during\nthe view as expected. After the release of one view, the move is still rejected under either\nreading of \"the view of the column\": after the read view 12 alone, by the column authority 11\n(O4.4); after the read view and the column authority 11, the field 9 of the row is still covered\nby the other column authority 10. The move is accepted after the release of both column authorities\ngiven by `split` (report, (b)). -/\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"theorem W2 : PReach K0 [] w2 ∧ TransferStep K0 12 19 w2.s .reject ∧ PReach K0 [] w2a ∧\n    TransferStep K0 12 19 w2a.s .reject ∧ ActiveDerivedOutside w2a.s 12 11 ∧\"\"\",\"\"\"theorem W2 : PReach K0 [] w2 ∧ TransferStep K0 12 19 w2.s .reject ∧ PReach K0 [] w2a ∧\n    TransferStep K0 12 19 w2a.s .reject ∧ ActiveDerivedOutside w2a.s 12 11 ∧\n    PReach K0 [] w2b ∧ TransferStep K0 9 16 w2b.s .reject ∧ ActiveDerivedOutside w2b.s 9 10 ∧\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  ⟨run_reach (by decide) (by decide), .reject (by decide), run_reach (by decide) (by decide),\n    .reject (by decide), by decide, run_reach (by decide) (by decide)⟩\n\n/-- W3\"\"\",\"\"\"  ⟨run_reach (by decide) (by decide), .reject (by decide), run_reach (by decide) (by decide),\n    .reject (by decide), by decide, run_reach (by decide) (by decide), .reject (by decide),\n    by decide, run_reach (by decide) (by decide)⟩\n\n/-- W3\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"/-- `freeSlot` on a pool whose `internal` is derived (here the block 6) is rejected by the\npreconditions of `endUse` (material §4: \"reject si une précondition d'`endUse` échoue\"):\n`internal` itself is an active derived authority on the entry, held outside it (`EndUseAccessOK`,\nA6). -/\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- `freeSlot` on this pool, whose `internal` is derived (the block 6) and held by the pool value,\noutside the entry, is rejected by the preconditions of `endUse` (material §4: \"reject si une\nprécondition d'`endUse` échoue\"): `internal` itself is an active derived authority on the entry, held\noutside it and staying live (`EndUseAccessOK`, A6). -/\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='Ern/MM03/LockOptions.lean'\ns=open(p).read()\nrep(\"\"\"not touch (`opt3_not_local`). Whether option 3 needs more than the function where the operation runs\n(material §5, \"locale à une fonction\") is not settled here (report, (g)). No option is adopted\n(material §5: \"la décision revient à l'arbitrage\").\"\"\",\"\"\"not touch (`opt3_not_local`). Whether option 3 needs more than the function where the operation runs\n(material §5, \"locale à une fonction\") is not settled here (report, (g)). No option is adopted (task\nof jalon 3, step 4: the decision is left to arbitration).\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\npython3 $SP/j3/fix2.py && time ~/.elan/bin/lake build 2>&1 | grep -E '^error|warning|Build' -A10 | head -40","description":"Apply second-check module fixes and rebuild","timeout":900000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2588,"cache_read_input_tokens":885349,"output_tokens":8768,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3218},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2588,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8768,"cache_read_input_tokens":885349,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2588,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2588},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0195KdDhG5SpKTju675ibAcr":{"command":"cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && SP=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad && cat > $SP/j3/fix2.py <<'PYEOF'\nimport re\np='Ern/MM23/Horrors.lean'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b,src=None):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:90]\n    s=s.replace(a,b,1)\ni=s.index(\"/-- L7: the contracts whose `DeclaredDisjoint` is the byte disjointness\")\nj=s.index(\"/-! ## Run R5\")\ns=s[:i]+'''/-- Decision 1 of jalon 2, the source of MM23-H01: the contracts whose `DeclaredDisjoint` is the\ndisjointness of the leaves of the two regions, as a parameter `K` (the draft `MM23` is unchanged). -/\ndef KLf : K := { K0 with DeclaredDisjoint := fun r r' => ∀ l ∈ r, l ∉ r' }\n\ninstance : ∀ r r', Decidable (KLf.DeclaredDisjoint r r') := fun r r' =>\n  inferInstanceAs (Decidable (∀ l ∈ r, l ∉ r'))\ninstance : DecidablePred KLf.SharedMutable := fun l =>\n  inferInstanceAs (Decidable (l ∈ ([] : List Nat)))\ninstance : DecidablePred KLf.Pinned := fun l => inferInstanceAs (Decidable (l ∈ ([] : List Nat)))\ninstance : DecidablePred KLf.ExternalDone := fun l =>\n  inferInstanceAs (Decidable (l ∈ ([] : List Nat)))\ninstance : DecidablePred KLf.Deallocable := fun l =>\n  inferInstanceAs (Decidable (l ∈ ([] : List Nat)))\ninstance : ∀ p a, Decidable (KLf.FreeCompat p a) := fun p a =>\n  inferInstanceAs (Decidable ((p, a) ∈ ([] : List (Nat × Nat))))\ninstance : ∀ p ls s, Decidable (KLf.Satisfiable p ls s) := fun _ _ _ => instDecidableTrue\n\n/-- `DDSound` of the instantiation by leaf disjointness: immediate (MM-03.3.8). -/\ntheorem KLf_dd : DDSound KLf := fun _ _ h => h\n\ndef r4s : SSt := sst KLf [] π4 r4\n/-- R4 after the `split` of the structure into the regions `[1]` and `[2]`. -/\ndef r4d : SSt := sst KLf [] π4 (r4 ++ [.split 0 [[1], [2]]])\n\n/-- **MM23-H01** (decision 1 of jalon 2; L7, `byteDisjoint_of_leaves`). With `DeclaredDisjoint`\ninstantiated by the disjointness of the leaves, two regions sharing the leaf 2 are not declared\ndisjoint and their `split` is rejected; the regions `[1]` and `[2]` are declared disjoint and their\n`split` runs in a translated execution. In its MM-02 state, every pair of declared regions of leaves\nhas disjoint bytes, through `LayoutWF` of `Repr`. Expected: rejected through `DDSound`\n(instantiation by leaves), declared regions with disjoint bytes; obtained: the same. -/\ntheorem H01 : DDSound KLf ∧ ¬ KLf.DeclaredDisjoint [1, 2] [2] ∧\n    SplitStep KLf 0 [[1, 2], [2]] r4s.1 .reject ∧ KLf.DeclaredDisjoint [1] [2] ∧\n    SplitStep KLf 0 [[1], [2]] r4s.1 (.ok (splitEff r4s.1 0 [[1], [2]])) ∧\n    (∃ os, AllOk Ceq CaseSim.obR CaseSim.obW MM02.State.empty os ∧\n      Repr π4.tok π4.ptok r4d.2.1 π4.L r4d.1 r4d.2.2) ∧\n    ∀ r r', KLf.DeclaredDisjoint r r' → (∀ l ∈ r, l < r4d.1.P.length ∧ isLeaf r4d.1.P l) →\n      (∀ l ∈ r', l < r4d.1.P.length ∧ isLeaf r4d.1.P l) → ByteDisjoint π4.L r r' := by\n  obtain ⟨os, hok, -, hR, -⟩ := sim_of (k := KLf) (statics := []) (P := P4) (z := [])\n    (ops := r4 ++ [.split 0 [[1], [2]]]) KLf_dd (by decide) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide)\n  exact ⟨KLf_dd, by decide, .reject (by decide), by decide, .ok (by decide), ⟨os, hok, hR⟩,\n    fun r r' hd hr hr' => byteDisjoint_of_leaves hR.lwf hr hr' hd⟩\n\n'''+s[j:]\n# H06 under K2f with twin; H02 twin\nrep(\"\"\"theorem H06 : K2f.Deallocable 5 ∧ K2f.FreeCompat 5 7 ∧ ¬ OwnedRoot r2i.1 5 ∧\n    FreeStep K2f 5 7 r2i.1 .reject ∧ (π2.L 5).alloc = (π2.L 4).alloc :=\n  ⟨by decide, by decide, by decide, .reject (by decide), by decide⟩\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- R2 under `K2f` before the transfer, and after the end of the block value. -/\ndef r2k : SSt := sst K2f [] π2 (r2.take 7)\ndef r2kt : SSt := sst K2f [] π2 (r2.take 10)\n\ntheorem H06 : Reachable K2f [] r2k.1 ∧ K2f.Deallocable 5 ∧ K2f.FreeCompat 5 7 ∧\n    ¬ OwnedRoot r2k.1 5 ∧ FreeStep K2f 5 7 r2k.1 .reject ∧ (π2.L 5).alloc = (π2.L 4).alloc ∧\n    Reachable K2f [] r2kt.1 ∧ FreeStep K2f 4 7 r2kt.1 (.ok (freeEff r2kt.1 4)) :=\n  ⟨(sim_of (k := K2f) (statics := []) (P := P2) (z := []) (ops := r2.take 7)\n      (KT_dd [] [] [] [4, 5] [(4, 7), (5, 7)]) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide)\n      (by decide)).2.2.2.2,\n    by decide, by decide, by decide, .reject (by decide), by decide,\n    (sim_of (k := K2f) (statics := []) (P := P2) (z := []) (ops := r2.take 10)\n      (KT_dd [] [] [] [4, 5] [(4, 7), (5, 7)]) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide)\n      (by decide)).2.2.2.2, .ok (by decide)⟩\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"allocation; obtained: the same. -/\ntheorem H06\"\"\",\"\"\"allocation; obtained: the same. Every state is reached under `K2f`. Twin: in the same run, once the\nblock value has ended, the `free` of the allocated storage 4 is accepted. -/\ntheorem H06\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"theorem H02 : ¬ r2f.1.Active 5 ∧ Read3Step 5 [5] r2f.1 .reject ∧\"\"\",\"\"\"theorem H02 : ¬ r2f.1.Active 5 ∧ Read3Step 5 [5] r2f.1 .reject ∧ Read3Step 5 [5] r2i.1 (.ok r2i.1) ∧\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  ⟨by decide, .reject (by decide), fun _ hs ha =>\"\"\",\"\"\"  ⟨by decide, .reject (by decide), .ok (by decide), fun _ hs ha =>\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"R2 the block was already released by `endUse q`, which `reset` requires (O19.2). Expected: no safe\nprogram reaches it, MM-02 would accept it; obtained: the same. -/\"\"\",\"\"\"R2 the block was already released by `endUse q`, which `reset` requires (O19.2). Twin: the same read\nthrough the block before its end is accepted. Expected: no safe program reaches it, MM-02 would\naccept it; obtained: the same. -/\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='Ern/MM03/Horrors.lean'\ns=open(p).read()\nrep(\"\"\"theorem H03 : PReach K0 [] h03 ∧ Write3Step 0 [1] h03.s .reject ∧\n    Write3Step 0 [1] h03t.s (.ok (write3Eff h03t.s [1])) :=\n  ⟨run_reach (by decide) (by decide), .reject (by decide), .ok (by decide)⟩\"\"\",\"\"\"theorem H03 : PReach K0 [] h03 ∧ Write3Step 0 [1] h03.s .reject ∧ PReach K0 [] h03t ∧\n    Write3Step 0 [1] h03t.s (.ok (write3Eff h03t.s [1])) :=\n  ⟨run_reach (by decide) (by decide), .reject (by decide), run_reach (by decide) (by decide),\n    .ok (by decide)⟩\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"/-- Contracts with the place 3 deallocable by the authority 7. -/\nabbrev KF3\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- A `transfer` is rejected while an active derived authority held by a frame covers a leaf of the\nsource (MM-03.3 §3, O4.4, `ActiveDerivedOutside`): a callee cannot transfer out of the footprint of\none of its parameters (H16, H07). -/\ntheorem transfer_rejected_by_frame_held {k : K} {s : S3} {src dst j f : Nat} {y : Authority}\n    (hy : s.A[j]? = some y) (ha : y.active = true) (ho : y.origin ≠ none)\n    (hh : y.holder = .frame f) (hl : ∃ l ∈ y.footprint, l ∈ footprint s.P src) :\n    TransferStep k src dst s .reject := by\n  have had : ActiveDerivedOutside s src j := by\n    unfold ActiveDerivedOutside; rw [hy]; exact ⟨ha, ho, by rw [hh]; exact id, hl⟩\n  exact .reject fun hpre =>\n    hpre.2.2.2.2.2.2.2.2.1 j (List.mem_range.2 (lt_of_getElem? hy)) had\n\n/-- Contracts with the place 3 deallocable by the authority 7. -/\nabbrev KF3\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"def w2a : PS := run K0 [] (w2o ++ [.release 12])\"\"\",\"\"\"def w2a : PS := run K0 [] (w2o ++ [.release 12])\n/-- W2 after the release of the read view 12 and of the column authority 11. -/\ndef w2b : PS := run K0 [] (w2o ++ [.release 12, .release 11])\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"/-- **W2** (§5b, ECS archetype and sparse set; Lib). Expected: disjoint reads and writes `ok`;\n`resolveMany` `ok`; the move of a field of the row while the column view is active: reject; after\nits release: `ok`. Obtained: disjoint accesses, `resolveMany` and the rejection during the view as\nexpected. After the release: if \"the view of the column\" is the read view 12, the move is still\nrejected, by the column authority 11 given by `split` (O4.4; report, (b)); if it is the column\nauthority itself, the move is accepted after its release (and that of the first column authority,\nwhich covers the other field of the row). -/\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- **W2** (§5b, ECS archetype and sparse set; Lib). Expected: disjoint reads and writes `ok`;\n`resolveMany` `ok`; the move of the row (transfers of its fields) while a column view is active:\nreject; after its release: `ok`. Obtained: disjoint accesses, `resolveMany` and the rejection during\nthe view as expected. After the release of one view, the move is still rejected under either\nreading of \"the view of the column\": after the read view 12 alone, by the column authority 11\n(O4.4); after the read view and the column authority 11, the field 9 of the row is still covered\nby the other column authority 10. The move is accepted after the release of both column authorities\ngiven by `split` (report, (b)). -/\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"theorem W2 : PReach K0 [] w2 ∧ TransferStep K0 12 19 w2.s .reject ∧ PReach K0 [] w2a ∧\n    TransferStep K0 12 19 w2a.s .reject ∧ ActiveDerivedOutside w2a.s 12 11 ∧\"\"\",\"\"\"theorem W2 : PReach K0 [] w2 ∧ TransferStep K0 12 19 w2.s .reject ∧ PReach K0 [] w2a ∧\n    TransferStep K0 12 19 w2a.s .reject ∧ ActiveDerivedOutside w2a.s 12 11 ∧\n    PReach K0 [] w2b ∧ TransferStep K0 9 16 w2b.s .reject ∧ ActiveDerivedOutside w2b.s 9 10 ∧\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  ⟨run_reach (by decide) (by decide), .reject (by decide), run_reach (by decide) (by decide),\n    .reject (by decide), by decide, run_reach (by decide) (by decide)⟩\n\n/-- W3\"\"\",\"\"\"  ⟨run_reach (by decide) (by decide), .reject (by decide), run_reach (by decide) (by decide),\n    .reject (by decide), by decide, run_reach (by decide) (by decide), .reject (by decide),\n    by decide, run_reach (by decide) (by decide)⟩\n\n/-- W3\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"/-- `freeSlot` on a pool whose `internal` is derived (here the block 6) is rejected by the\npreconditions of `endUse` (material §4: \"reject si une précondition d'`endUse` échoue\"):\n`internal` itself is an active derived authority on the entry, held outside it (`EndUseAccessOK`,\nA6). -/\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- `freeSlot` on this pool, whose `internal` is derived (the block 6) and held by the pool value,\noutside the entry, is rejected by the preconditions of `endUse` (material §4: \"reject si une\nprécondition d'`endUse` échoue\"): `internal` itself is an active derived authority on the entry, held\noutside it and staying live (`EndUseAccessOK`, A6). -/\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='Ern/MM03/LockOptions.lean'\ns=open(p).read()\nrep(\"\"\"not touch (`opt3_not_local`). Whether option 3 needs more than the function where the operation runs\n(material §5, \"locale à une fonction\") is not settled here (report, (g)). No option is adopted\n(material §5: \"la décision revient à l'arbitrage\").\"\"\",\"\"\"not touch (`opt3_not_local`). Whether option 3 needs more than the function where the operation runs\n(material §5, \"locale à une fonction\") is not settled here (report, (g)). No option is adopted (task\nof jalon 3, step 4: the decision is left to arbitration).\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\npython3 $SP/j3/fix2.py && time ~/.elan/bin/lake build 2>&1 | grep -E '^error|warning|Build' -A10 | head -40","description":"Apply second-check module fixes and rebuild","timeout":900000}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_0195KdDhG5SpKTju675ibAcr":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"1e115655-c51e-420a-b241-fa664a5e2e84","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgciYUemNqm1SBBFmt4qN","requestRef":"f4e98646-94e2-4006-a2d7-8e4caef94be0","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e2556a4b-196f-4b73-85f9-76390c677f57","timestamp":"2026-11-01T18:56:31.675Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-