{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-01T19:10:57.624Z","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>wwis3b7lx</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_012RhbgtrWauN49L9qibVGyj</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/tasks/wwis3b7lx.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Dynamic workflow \"Third check of the jalon-3 second-round fixes (commit 772778c), with a refuter per finding\" completed</summary>\n<result>{\"confirmed\":[{\"severity\":\"major\",\"location\":\"formal/Ern/MM03/Horrors.lean:839-857 (w2b, W2 docstring); same claim in formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md (b) 3 and (g) 6\",\"claim\":\"The new W2 docstring says that releasing one view is not enough \\\"under either reading\\\" (report: \\\"sous aucune lecture\\\"). That result comes from an encoding choice the material does not require: system A's column authority 10 stays active through the move, so two column views are active at the move, not one. When only one column view is active at the move, the expected verdict is obtained under the reading view = B's column authority 11 with its read view 12. This deviation was chosen silently and is reported as an obtained result.\",\"fix\":\"Restrict the W2 docstring and report (b) 3 so the deviation is stated as holding only while A's column authority 10 stays active at the move. Add the one-active-view construction (w2v, with the expected verdict obtained under the column-authority reading) as a witness, and list that reading in question (g) 6. Alternatively, encode W2 with A's view ended after its write.\"},{\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"formal/Ern/MM23/Horrors.lean:555-572 (r2k, r2kt, H06)\",\"claim\":\"The H06 twin is not minimal, and the rejected case has a second cause. At r2k, `free 5` fails both OwnedRoot and FreeAccessOK, because the live block authority is held by place 2. The same-state twin, `free 4` at r2k, is also rejected. The twin used, `free 4` at r2kt, adds three steps (transfer 2 3, read 3 [3], endUse 3) where a single `endUse 2` is enough. A minimal pair exists at r2kt, where `free 5` fails only on OwnedRoot.\",\"fix\":\"State the rejection and the twin on the same state where the block value has ended: `free 5` rejected and `free 4` ok at r2kt, or at `r2.take 7 ++ [.endUse 2]`. Alternatively, record that the r2k rejection is also caused by FreeAccessOK.\"},{\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"formal/Ern/MM23/Horrors.lean:536-548 (H02 twin on r2i)\",\"claim\":\"The new H02 twin reads through the block at r2.take 7, which also removes `transfer 2 3` and `read 3 [3]`. Those steps play no part in the rejection. The minimal twin, the same sequence without the block's end (`endUse 3`, `reset`), is r2.take 9, and the read there is accepted.\",\"fix\":\"Use `sst K0 [] π2 (r2.take 9)` as the H02 twin state: the read just before `endUse 3`.\"},{\"severity\":\"major\",\"location\":\"formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md:139-142 ((b) 3), :253 ((g) 6), :297 (second-check summary); same claim in the W2 docstring, formal/Ern/MM03/Horrors.lean:840-848\",\"claim\":\"The new claim that releasing one view is not enough \\\"sous aucune lecture de « la vue de colonne »\\\", and the (g) 6 premise that a move needs both split column authorities released, come from how this run was built, not from the scenario. The construction keeps system A's column authority 10 active through the move. If A's column is released after its write, leaving only one column view active as the material describes, the expected verdict holds under the column-authority reading.\",\"fix\":\"Rewrite (b) 3, (g) 6 and the summary line. The result depends on the reading and on whether system A's column authority is still active at the move. Under the column-authority reading with A's column released first, the expected verdict is obtained (add that witness). Under the read-view reading, it is not. Ask the arbitration question on that basis.\"},{\"severity\":\"major\",\"location\":\"formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md:104 (MM23-H table header), against rows H14 and H17 (lines 121, 124)\",\"claim\":\"\\\"Classe : R (raffinement) pour tous les cas\\\" is false for H17, and for H14. The report's own H17 row contradicts it, and so does the material. Under rule 5, a case from another spec does not block the closure of jalon 3, so labelling two unencoded cases R misstates what blocks closure.\",\"fix\":\"Class R for H01–H13, H15 and H16; spec 4 and spec 11 for H17; spec 3 (with MM-02.G) for H14. Or add a Classe column per row.\"},{\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md:115 (MM23-H table, H08, Source column)\",\"claim\":\"H08's source is given as \\\"L5 (`leaked`)\\\", but L5 is about `free` and frame exit. H08 is an `endUse` with no free and before the exit. That case is K3 (with K4 for \\\"no step\\\"). Neither the module nor the earlier reports support L5 here.\",\"fix\":\"Change the H08 source to K3 (`leaked`), K4.\"},{\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md:104 (header sentence) and Source column rows H02, H11, H12 (lines 109, 118, 119)\",\"claim\":\"The header says the sources are \\\"arbitrages du jalon 2 (K1–K5, L1–L8) et décisions du jalon 2, comme les cite le module\\\". The column also cites R1, R2 and R4, which are MM-03.3 §9.2 refinement rules, plus O19.2, A6, O7, MM-02.G and spec 3. The H14 and H17 sources come from the material, since the module does not encode those cases. Worse, R1, R2 and R4 clash with the run names R1–R7 defined just above in the same subsection.\",\"fix\":\"Write \\\"MM-03.3 §9.2 R1/R2/R4\\\" in the Source column, and correct the header so it covers spec clauses and the material.\"},{\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md:108 (MM23-H table, H01, Obtenu) and :296 (summary)\",\"claim\":\"\\\"dans l'état traduit, toute paire de régions déclarées a des octets disjoints\\\" says more than `H01` proves. The theorem only concludes `ByteDisjoint` when both regions consist of leaves of the state. Under `KLf`, a declared pair with a non-leaf region overlaps in bytes.\",\"fix\":\"Write \\\"toute paire de régions de feuilles déclarées\\\".\"},{\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"formal/Ern/MM03/Horrors.lean:286-288 (docstring of `transfer_rejected_by_frame_held`, the lemma behind report (b) 1)\",\"claim\":\"The new lemma's docstring gives MM3-H07 as an instance. It is not. H07's rejected transfer has no active, derived, frame-held authority covering its source. It is rejected by C1 (`EffAnchorOK`), as its own docstring and the report table say.\",\"fix\":\"Remove H07 from the docstring's parenthesis (keep H16).\"}],\"refuted\":[]}</result>\n<diagnostics>Per-agent results: /Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/subagents/workflows/wf_0389f812-2f0/journal.jsonl — one {\"type\":\"result\",...} line per completed agent with its full return value.\nIf the result above is empty or unexpected, Read this file BEFORE diagnosing — do not assume agents returned non-empty results.\nTo re-run with edited post-processing: Workflow({scriptPath: '/Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/workflows/scripts/j3-third-check-wf_0389f812-2f0.js', resumeFromRunId: 'wf_0389f812-2f0'}) — agents whose (prompt, opts) are unchanged replay from cache.</diagnostics>\n<usage><agent_count>11</agent_count><agents_done>11</agents_done><agents_error>0</agents_error><agents_skipped>0</agents_skipped><agents_empty_result>0</agents_empty_result><subagent_tokens>1158172</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>156</tool_uses><duration_ms>697335</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
