{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-01T19:21:07.517Z","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>wdkj6v53y</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01CckuKPMiy9rF8F7UDNdvNT</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/tasks/wdkj6v53y.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Dynamic workflow \"Narrow check of the jalon-3 third-round fixes (commit 64e5809), with a refuter per finding\" completed</summary>\n<result>{\"confirmed\":[{\"severity\":\"major\",\"location\":\"formal/Ern/MM03/Horrors.lean:841-857 (W2 docstring and theorem `W2`, last conjunct)\",\"claim\":\"The W2 theorem does not prove the two claims this commit adds to its docstring. First, after system B's column authority 11 is released, \\\"the move is accepted\\\". Second, \\\"one column view ... is active at the move\\\" (A's authority 10 is released). Only `TransferStep K0 12 19 w2b.s (.ok _)` is non-vacuous. The conjunct meant to show the whole move, `PReach K0 [] (run K0 [] (w2o ++ [.release 12, .release 11, .transfer 9 16, .transfer 12 19]))`, holds even when a step is rejected. When a step is not ok, `run` falls back to `PS.init`, and `PReach.init` reaches that state.\",\"fix\":\"Replace the last conjunct with a non-vacuous one, either `(prun K0 (PS.init []) (w2o ++ [.release 12, .release 11, .transfer 9 16, .transfer 12 19])).isSome = true` or `TransferStep K0 9 16 w2b.s (.ok (transferEff w2b.s 9 16)) ∧ TransferStep K0 12 19 (run K0 [] (w2o ++ [.release 12, .release 11, .transfer 9 16])).s (.ok _)`. To back the docstring's \\\"one column view is active at the move\\\", also add that authority 10 is inactive in `w2.s` (for example `OptP (w2.s.A[10]?) (·.active = false) False`). All of these hold by `decide`: evaluation gives authority 10 `active = false` in `w2.s`, and `TransferPre K0 w2b.s 9 16` is `true`.\"},{\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md:109 (MM23-H table, H02 row, Jumeau column) and :304 (third-check summary 'MM23-H02 (même run sans la fin du bloc)')\",\"claim\":\"The commit says the H02 twin is 'the same run without the end of the block', but that run is not an accepted run. The Lean twin is the prefix that drops both `endUse q` and the `reset`, the step H02 is about. The wording it replaced, 'lecture par le bloc avant sa fin : ok', was accurate.\",\"fix\":\"Describe the twin as the prefix of R2 before `endUse q`, without the `reset` (which O19.2 forbids while the block is active). Use this wording in the H02 row and in the third-check bullet, or restore 'lecture par le bloc avant sa fin : ok'.\"},{\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md:296 (second-check summary, W2 bullet) vs :303 (third-check summary)\",\"claim\":\"The commit rewrote the second-check bullet to describe the third round's result. The report now gives two different accounts of what the second check concluded about W2.\",\"fix\":\"Restore the original second-check bullet ('la libération d'une seule vue ne suffit sous aucune lecture, témoin `w2b`'). Line 303 already says that the third check superseded it.\"},{\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md:104 (MM23-H header sentence) with :115 (H08 Source 'K3 (`leaked`), K4')\",\"claim\":\"The rewritten header sentence still says the Source column gives the sources 'comme les cite le module'. The module does not cite the source this commit gave H08, nor several other sources in the column.\",\"fix\":\"Change the header to say the sources are those cited by the module or by the jalon-2 reports (reports/MM23_v0.1*.md). Alternatively, cite the arbitrage K3 and K4 in the H08 docstring, and also add the missing L5 and O7 citations to H05 and H09.\"}],\"refuted\":[{\"location\":\"formal/Ern/MM23/Horrors.lean:557-570 (MM23-H06 docstring and theorem `H06`)\",\"claim\":\"The docstring's new claim \\\"the block value ended, so the other clauses of `free` hold\\\" is not in the statement. The commit message says \\\"OwnedRoot alone fails\\\", but the theorem gives only `¬ OwnedRoot\",\"reason\":\"The claim in the docstring is true, and the finding says so too. Its reason is also right: the block value had to end first. The theorem does not prove the remark, but the remark is not a formal claim. It only explains why the commit picked state r2kt (after `endUse q`) over the old r2k. No spec quo\"}]}</result>\n<diagnostics>Per-agent results: /Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/subagents/workflows/wf_6bfbde39-90c/journal.jsonl — one {\"type\":\"result\",...} line per completed agent with its full return value.\nIf the result above is empty or unexpected, Read this file BEFORE diagnosing — do not assume agents returned non-empty results.\nTo re-run with edited post-processing: Workflow({scriptPath: '/Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/workflows/scripts/j3-fourth-check-wf_6bfbde39-90c.js', resumeFromRunId: 'wf_6bfbde39-90c'}) — agents whose (prompt, opts) are unchanged replay from cache.</diagnostics>\n<usage><agent_count>7</agent_count><agents_done>7</agents_done><agents_error>0</agents_error><agents_skipped>0</agents_skipped><agents_empty_result>0</agents_empty_result><subagent_tokens>701284</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>86</tool_uses><duration_ms>433818</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
