{"parentUuid":"b8ddb593-2751-4f25-9a0f-53a91b69f772","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgckatsqWwj9z6wvDUKU4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FGHB9AGeXYVm3DSkBiKjzT","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"SP=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad && cat > $SP/j3/fix4.py <<'PYEOF'\ndef edit(p, reps):\n    s=open(p).read()\n    for a,b in reps:\n        assert a in s, (p, a[:90])\n        s=s.replace(a,b,1)\n    open(p,'w').write(s)\nedit('Ern/MM03/Horrors.lean',[\n(\"\"\"section Run\nvariable (k : K)\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- The state given for a run whose steps are not all `ok`: it has no frame, so no run reaches it\n(`run_ok_of_reach`). -/\ndef stuckPS : PS := ⟨{ S3.init [] with F := [] }, [], 0, []⟩\n\nsection Run\nvariable (k : K)\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"/-- The state reached by the operations `os` from `S3.init statics`, or that initial state when a\nstep is not `ok` (then `run_reach` cannot be used). -/\ndef run (statics : Statics) (os : List Op) : PS :=\n  (prun k (PS.init statics) os).getD (PS.init statics)\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- The state reached by the operations `os` from `S3.init statics`; `stuckPS` when a step is not\n`ok`. So a statement `PReach k statics (run k statics os)` says that every step is `ok`\n(`run_ok_of_reach`). -/\ndef run (statics : Statics) (os : List Op) : PS :=\n  (prun k (PS.init statics) os).getD stuckPS\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"  prun_init hsh (some_getD h)\n\nend RunSound\"\"\",\"\"\"  prun_init hsh (some_getD h)\n\n/-- Under `DDSound`, a reached `run` is a run whose every step is `ok`: the state given for a failed\nrun has no frame, which `WF3` excludes on reached states (MM-03.3 §2.1). -/\ntheorem run_ok_of_reach (hdd : DDSound k) {statics : Statics} {os : List Op}\n    (h : PReach k statics (run k statics os)) : (prun k (PS.init statics) os).isSome = true := by\n  cases hp : prun k (PS.init statics) os with\n  | some _ => rfl\n  | none =>\n    have hr := pReach_reachable hdd h\n    simp only [run, hp, Option.getD_none] at hr\n    exact absurd rfl (reachable_invariants hdd hr).1.2.2.1\n\nend RunSound\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"theorem W2 : PReach K0 [] w2 ∧ TransferStep K0 12 19 w2.s .reject ∧ PReach K0 [] w2a ∧\"\"\",\"\"\"theorem W2 : PReach K0 [] w2 ∧ ¬ w2.s.Active 10 ∧ TransferStep K0 12 19 w2.s .reject ∧\n    PReach K0 [] w2a ∧\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"  ⟨run_reach (by decide) (by decide), .reject (by decide), run_reach (by decide) (by decide),\n    .reject (by decide), by decide, run_reach (by decide) (by decide), .ok (by decide),\n    run_reach (by decide) (by decide)⟩\"\"\",\"\"\"  ⟨run_reach (by decide) (by decide), by decide, .reject (by decide),\n    run_reach (by decide) (by decide), .reject (by decide), by decide,\n    run_reach (by decide) (by decide), .ok (by decide), run_reach (by decide) (by decide)⟩\"\"\"),\n])\nedit('Ern/MM23/Horrors.lean',[\n(\"\"\"section Cases\nvariable (k : K)\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- The state given for a translated run whose steps are not all `ok`: it has no frame, so it is not\nreached (`sst_ok_of_reachable`). -/\ndef sstuck : SSt := ({ S3.init [] with F := [] }, fun _ => none, MM02.State.empty)\n\nsection Cases\nvariable (k : K)\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"/-- The state reached by the translated run of `ops` (or the initial state if it fails). -/\ndef sst (statics : Statics) (π : Params) (ops : List Op3) : SSt :=\n  (srun k Ceq CaseSim.obR CaseSim.obW π (sinit statics π) ops).getD (sinit statics π)\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- The state reached by the translated run of `ops`; `sstuck` if a step is not `ok`, so a statement\nthat its MM-03 state is reached says that every step is `ok` (`sst_ok_of_reachable`). -/\ndef sst (statics : Statics) (π : Params) (ops : List Op3) : SSt :=\n  (srun k Ceq CaseSim.obR CaseSim.obW π (sinit statics π) ops).getD sstuck\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"    (Ern.HandlePool.some_getD (d := sinit statics (piOf P z)) h)\"\"\",\"\"\"    (Ern.HandlePool.some_getD (d := sstuck) h)\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"end Sim\n\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- Under `DDSound`, a translated run whose MM-03 state is reached is a run whose every step is `ok`:\nthe state given for a failed run has no frame, which `WF3` excludes (MM-03.3 §2.1). -/\ntheorem sst_ok_of_reachable (hdd : DDSound k) {statics : Statics} {π : Params} {ops : List Op3}\n    (h : Reachable k statics (sst k statics π ops).1) :\n    (srun k Ceq CaseSim.obR CaseSim.obW π (sinit statics π) ops).isSome = true := by\n  cases hp : srun k Ceq CaseSim.obR CaseSim.obW π (sinit statics π) ops with\n  | some _ => rfl\n  | none =>\n    simp only [sst, hp, Option.getD_none, sstuck] at h\n    exact absurd rfl (reachable_invariants hdd h).1.2.2.1\n\nend Sim\n\"\"\"),\n])\np='reports/J3_v0.1.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:90]\n    s=s.replace(a,b,1)\nrep(\"| même run sans la fin du bloc : lecture par le bloc ok |\",\"| préfixe de R2 avant `endUse q`, sans `reset` : lecture par le bloc ok |\")\nrep(\"- jumeaux minimaux de MM23-H06 (même état) et de MM23-H02 (même run sans la fin du bloc) ;\",\"- jumeaux minimaux de MM23-H06 (même état) et de MM23-H02 (préfixe de R2 avant `endUse q`, sans `reset`) ;\")\nrep(\"- W2 : écart selon la lecture de « la vue de colonne » ((b) 3, (g) 6) ;\",\"- W2 : la libération d'une seule vue ne suffit sous aucune lecture, témoin `w2b` d'alors ((b) 3, (g) 6 ; conclusion remplacée par la troisième vérification) ;\")\nrep(\"Sources : arbitrages du jalon 2 (K1–K5, L1–L8), décisions du jalon 2, obligations de MM-03.3 §9.2 et clauses de MM-03.3, comme les cite le module ; pour H14 et H17, non encodés, le matériel.\",\n    \"Sources : arbitrages du jalon 2 (K1–K5, L1–L8), décisions du jalon 2, obligations de MM-03.3 §9.2 et clauses de MM-03.3, cités par le module ou par les rapports du jalon 2 (`MM23_v0.1.md`, `MM23_v0.1_p2.md`) ; pour H14 et H17, non encodés, le matériel.\")\nrep(\"**Méthode.** Chaque cas est une exécution depuis l'état initial (règle 3).\",\"\"\"**Méthode.** Chaque cas est une exécution depuis l'état initial (règle 3). Un énoncé « l'état de l'exécution est atteint » (`PReach k statics (run k statics os)`, `Reachable k statics (sst …).1`) dit que chaque pas est `ok` : une exécution qui échoue donne un état sans cadre, qu'aucune exécution n'atteint (`run_ok_of_reach`, `sst_ok_of_reachable`).\"\"\")\ns=s.rstrip('\\n')+\"\"\"\n\nQuatrième vérification, ciblée sur les corrections précédentes : 5 constats, 4 confirmés, 1 réfuté. Le principal : un énoncé « l'état de l'exécution est atteint » tenait aussi pour une exécution en échec, l'état de repli étant l'état initial, atteint ; les preuves établissaient bien le succès de chaque exécution, mais les énoncés ne le disaient pas. Correction pour tous les cas : l'état de repli est un état sans cadre, et `run_ok_of_reach` et `sst_ok_of_reachable` déduisent le succès de l'énoncé d'atteinte. Autres corrections : W2 énonce l'inactivité de l'autorité de colonne de A au déplacement ; jumeau de MM23-H02 décrit comme préfixe ; résumé de la seconde vérification rétabli ; provenance des sources de la table MM23-H précisée.\n\"\"\"\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\npython3 $SP/j3/fix4.py && time ~/.elan/bin/lake build 2>&1 | grep -E '^error|warning|Build' -A10 | head -30","description":"Make run fallbacks unreachable, fix wording, rebuild","timeout":900000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1998,"cache_read_input_tokens":944391,"output_tokens":4373,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":968},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1998,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4373,"cache_read_input_tokens":944391,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1998,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5