{"parentUuid":"d5785aa4-594e-4312-bb13-bfac1ac5e24d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01LXbo5phedidotB7yNXbcmx","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"e28a47ca-1575-41f7-9fe8-1b63c6298b18","timestamp":"2026-11-01T19:23:46.395Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/validation_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
{"parentUuid":"e28a47ca-1575-41f7-9fe8-1b63c6298b18","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgckhCasFj9Up1CXGxDyD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UZhYdCVnNB2n6HHa3JkVrj","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nfor a,b in [(\"  - `MM03.Horrors` : 177 constantes, dont 68 théorèmes ;\",\"  - `MM03.Horrors` : 180 constantes, dont 70 théorèmes ;\"),\n            (\"  - `MM23.Horrors` : 226 constantes, dont 120 théorèmes ;\",\"  - `MM23.Horrors` : 229 constantes, dont 122 théorèmes ;\")]:\n    assert a in s, a\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit checkout formal/Ern/.gitkeep 2>/dev/null; git add formal/Ern/MM03/Horrors.lean formal/Ern/MM23/Horrors.lean formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nJ3: fourth check fixes\n\nWhy: a fourth check found that a statement \"the state of the run is\nreached\" also held for a failed run, whose fallback state was the\ninitial state, itself reached. Every proof established the success of\nits run, but the statements did not say so.\n\nWhat:\n- MM03/Horrors: a failed run now gives stuckPS, a state without frame;\n  run_ok_of_reach derives from PReach of a run that every step is ok.\n- MM23/Horrors: same for translated runs (sstuck, sst_ok_of_reachable).\n- W2 states that system A's column authority is inactive at the move.\n- Report: method paragraph on the meaning of the reachability\n  statements; MM23-H02 twin described as a prefix; second-check summary\n  restored; provenance of the MM23-H sources; fourth check summarized;\n  constant counts.\n\nProof: lake build succeeds without warnings; every constant of the four\nnew modules depends only on propext and Quot.sound; MM02, MM03 and MM23\nunchanged since formal/refinement_0.1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -10; git status --short","description":"Commit fourth-check fixes","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":962,"cache_read_input_tokens":950896,"output_tokens":844,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":962,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":844,"cache_read_input_tokens":950896,"cache_creation_input_tokens":962,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":962},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01UZhYdCVnNB2n6HHa3JkVrj":{"command":"cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nfor a,b in [(\"  - `MM03.Horrors` : 177 constantes, dont 68 théorèmes ;\",\"  - `MM03.Horrors` : 180 constantes, dont 70 théorèmes ;\"),\n            (\"  - `MM23.Horrors` : 226 constantes, dont 120 théorèmes ;\",\"  - `MM23.Horrors` : 229 constantes, dont 122 théorèmes ;\")]:\n    assert a in s, a\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit checkout formal/Ern/.gitkeep 2>/dev/null; git add formal/Ern/MM03/Horrors.lean formal/Ern/MM23/Horrors.lean formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nJ3: fourth check fixes\n\nWhy: a fourth check found that a statement \"the state of the run is\nreached\" also held for a failed run, whose fallback state was the\ninitial state, itself reached. Every proof established the success of\nits run, but the statements did not say so.\n\nWhat:\n- MM03/Horrors: a failed run now gives stuckPS, a state without frame;\n  run_ok_of_reach derives from PReach of a run that every step is ok.\n- MM23/Horrors: same for translated runs (