{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","id":"4b2ed6ba-3055-4c03-9d3c-1bbac6176f6b","timestamp":"2026-11-01T19:24:07.008Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"d1aa6c2254c890b11835611a868b353c28b0e75545aafd34fb8d8155d691dfb1","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"xhigh"}},"base":"4b35d59e-5b7c-4a96-94e3-ad7944893f04","keep":451,"tail":["b3f308168cd6d37f77057d867b797b71314f22f4d454ad7f385371877599b66e","cff572633d43566b177de5ea6abd9a570ee04bc529a2d6c233f495ad642f7b19"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",452,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"237f7d3c936bd3e7c22aeca221d9e0fbaebcc3cad91ca25a37b84db435a6d986"}
{"parentUuid":"428d0a33-e657-408a-9dcc-17bb72b95743","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgckjFHtYBzMcdAacnHb2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Jalon 3 is done on branch `formal/validation_0.1`. Following \"pas de merge, pas de PR\", nothing was pushed, merged or opened as a PR. `lake build` succeeds without warnings. Every constant of the four new modules uses only `propext` and `Quot.sound`. `MM02.lean`, `MM03.lean` and `MM23.lean` are unchanged. The report is [J3_v0.1.md](formal/reports/J3_v0.1.md).\n\n**Pool of handles (step 1)**\n- **Exclusivity holds.** `pool_resolve_modify_exclusive` is proved for any sequence of kernel and pool steps, not only the six listed. The proof rests on I1 and on the effective mode of `internal` when each companion is created. No reviewer found a way around it.\n- **No stale access.** `pool_no_stale_access` is proved, as are the stale, other-pool, atomicity, distinctness and `freeSlot` theorems. The pool plugs into `Reachable` without changing the kernel.\n- **`PoolInv`, read literally, is not preserved.** `pool_inv_preserved` is false, with counterexamples kept: a kernel `derive` from the companion onto a free entry, a `derive` from an entry authority, and the re-anchoring done by `exitFrame`. The first clause and the no-stale-access part are proved.\n- **`freeSlot` as the material defines it is unusable in two cases.** It applies all of `endUse`'s preconditions, so it is always rejected when `internal` is derived (the arena-block pool of H44). It is also rejected when the right comes from `writeShared`.\n\n**MM3-H (step 2)**\n- All 54 cases (51 rows A–I plus W1–W3) are built from the initial state, each with its expected verdict, its twin and its class.\n- **Deviations reported in (b):**\n  - **H16:** the callee can never receive a value by transfer, because its own parameter blocks the `transfer`.\n  - **H01:** an `Observe` parameter derived from the `Modify` parameter is accepted.\n  - **W2:** the expected verdict depends on what \"la vue de colonne\" means.\n  - **W3:** read literally, `reset` stays rejected after `endUse` of the structure.\n- In section J, only H42 can be expressed in the kernel, as a straight-line expansion, and the kernel accepts it.\n\n**MM23-H (step 3)**\n- Every case is an execution translated by `simulation`.\n- H15 and H16 are marked \"écart connu\": empty-region pointers get address 0, and a region's pointer takes its head leaf's address, 8 bytes above the lowest leaf.\n- H14 and H17 are classed, not encoded.\n\n**`NoLock` (step 4)**\n\n| Option | False rejections | H49 | H50 | H51 | Check |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2 (self-lock on `transfer`/`issue`) | none | still blocks | prevented | still blocks | local to the operation |\n| 3 (acyclic \"b blocks a\") | none | prevented | prevented | prevented | needs authorities the operation does not touch |\n\nNo option is adopted. Whether option 3 can be checked within one function, as the material asks, is not settled.\n\n**Review:** four independent reviewers, then three narrower rounds, each finding re-checked by a refuter. The confirmed counts were 13 of 15, then 9, then 4. The last round found that statements of the form \"this run's state is reached\" also held when a run failed. That is fixed for all cases with lemmas `run_ok_of_reach` and `sst_ok_of_reachable`. The fixes from that round were not re-checked by a fifth round.\n\n**Decisions for you:** report section (g) lists 13 questions. The main ones:\n- how to restate `PoolInv`;\n- whether `freeSlot` keeps all of `endUse`'s preconditions;\n- two pools, or a pool and an arena, sharing one `internal`;\n- passing a value by transfer into a callee;\n- the readings of W2 and W3;\n- whether option 3 is local to a function.\n\n**ub-mode log:**\n1. Created the branch; read MM-03.3 v0.3, the jalon-3 material and the kernel API.\n2. Designed the pool beside `S3` and built it only from kernel steps.\n3. Step 1 (6d79960). Added an executable runner with a soundness proof, so `decide` builds reached states in seconds.\n4. Step 2 (ee78e35). Found H16 inexpressible, and the W2 and W3 deviations.\n5. Step 3 (22c8b99). Added a translated runner and a layout computed from each run's final places.\n6. Step 4 (f13f3fd).\n7. Reviews, fixes and the report: 6cb3f1b, 772778c, 64e5809, 7d24495.\n\nLessons I saved to memory:\n- A runner's fallback state must be unreachable, or \"reached\" statements say nothing.\n- Projecting a component out of an existential passes the elaborator but fails in the kernel.\n- When a fix concludes \"fails under every reading\", check whether the construction itself forces the failure."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":226,"cache_read_input_tokens":953760,"output_tokens":1714,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":226,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1714,"cache_read_input_tokens":953760,"cache_creation_input_tokens":226,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":226},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"0a5c62db-b9c8-4659-be06-0c4fca03db93","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgckjEyYB3pavjUtMtdFN","requestRef":"4b2ed6ba-3055-4c03-9d3c-1bbac6176f6b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"e58de35d-f5ad-4b96-badd-6125984dd529","timestamp":"2026-11-01T19:24:23.244Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-de