rnlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/validation_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
{"parentUuid":"c03303fd-69ea-4d84-bf99-b550f468e797","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fcfe6e6f-a978-46ba-b770-f92b3a29d346","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012gB9B2a9aLVYiDX9FbGHhF","type":"tool_result","content":"import Ern.MM03.Horrors\n\n/-!\n# Measure of the `NoLock` options (jalon 3, step 4)\n\nThe options of the jalon-3 material (`ERN_Jalon3_materiel.md` v2, §5), measured on the kernel as it\nis (option 1, no rule), without modifying it:\n\n* option 2, a local rule: an operation does not place an authority into a place it covers\n  (`SelfLock`); `store` already rejects it (O8.3), so the rule is measured on `transfer` and\n  `issue` (`opt2`);\n* option 3, `NoLock`: no self-lock, as a separate clause, and the relation \"`b` blocks `a`\"\n  (`Blocks`) acyclic, checked on the arrival state of `transfer`, `issue` and `store` (`opt3`).\n\nFor each case of the list \"doit être accepté\" of §5 (H11, H19, H29b, H35 to H37, H44 to H47, W1\nto W3) and for H49 to H51, `decisions` gives the decision of an option on each `transfer`, `issue`\nand `store` of the run of the case (`Ern.MM03.Horrors`), decided on the state where the step runs;\n`true` is acceptance. The cost, measured as the brief asks (from the authorities and places the\noperation touches, or the whole state): option 2 on `transfer` depends on the state only through the\nplaces and the authorities the transfer moves (`opt2_transfer_local`), on `issue` only through the\nregion and the destination (`opt2_issue_local`); option 3 depends on authorities the operation does\nnot touch (`opt3_not_local`). Whether option 3 needs more than the function where the operation runs\n(material §5, \"locale à une fonction\") is not settled here (report, (g)). No option is adopted (task\nof jalon 3, step 4: the decision is left to arbitration).\n-/\n\nnamespace Ern.MM03.LockOptions\n\nopen Ern.MM03 Ern.HandlePool Ern.MM03.Horrors\n\n/-! ## Option 2: self-lock -/\n\n/-- The leaves of a holder (MM-03.3.4): those of a place, none for a frame. -/\ndef holderLeaves (s : S3) : Holder → List Nat\n  | .place p => footprint s.P p\n  | .frame _ => []\n\n/-- Self-lock of the authority `a` (material §5, options 2 and 3): `a` is active and held by a place\none of whose leaves it covers. -/\ndef SelfLock (s : S3) (a : Nat) : Prop :=\n  OptP (s.A[a]?) (fun y => y.active = true ∧ ∃ l ∈ y.footprint, l ∈ holderLeaves s y.holder) False\n\ninstance (s : S3) (a : Nat) : Decidable (SelfLock s a) := by unfold SelfLock; infer_instance\n\n/-- Option 2 on `transfer src dst` (material §5): no authority moved by the transfer, one held within\nthe source, is self-locked in the arrival state. -/\ndef Opt2Transfer (s : S3) (src dst : Nat) : Prop :=\n  ∀ j ∈ List.range s.A.length, OptP (s.A[j]?) (fun y => heldIn s.P src y.holder) False →\n    ¬ SelfLock (transferEff s src dst) j\n\ninstance (s : S3) (src dst : Nat) : Decidable (Opt2Transfer s src dst) := by\n  unfold Opt2Transfer; infer_instance\n\n/-- Option 2 on `issue` of `region` to `dst` (material §5): the block, the new authority, is not\nself-locked in the arrival state. -/\ndef Opt2Issue (s : S3) (ar : Arena) (region : List Nat) (dst : Nat) : Prop :=\n  ¬ SelfLock (issueEff s ar region dst).1 s.A.length\n\ninstance (s : S3) (ar : Arena) (region : List Nat) (dst : Nat) :\n    Decidable (Opt2Issue s ar region dst) := by\n  unfold Opt2Issue; infer_instance\n\n/-! ## Option 3: `NoLock` -/\n\n/-- \"`b` bloque `a`\" (material §5, option 3): `b ≠ a`, both active, and the footprint of `b` contains\na leaf of the holder of `a`. -/\ndef Blocks (s : S3) (b a : Nat) : Prop :=\n  b ≠ a ∧ s.Active b ∧ s.Active a ∧\n    OptP (s.A[a]?) (fun y => ∃ l ∈ s.afp b, l ∈ holderLeaves s y.holder) False\n\ninstance (s : S3) (b a : Nat) : Decidable (Blocks s b a) := by unfold Blocks; infer_instance\n\n/-- The authorities blocked by one of `xs`. -/\ndef blockedBy (s : S3) (xs : List Nat) : List Nat :=\n  (List.range s.A.length).filter fun a => decide (∃ b ∈ xs, Blocks s b a)\n\n/-- The authorities reached from `xs` by at most `n` steps of `Blocks`, `xs` included. -/\ndef blockReach (s : S3) : Nat → List Nat → List Nat\n  | 0, xs => xs\n  | n + 1, xs => blockReach s n (xs ++ blockedBy s xs)\n34:def holderLeaves (s : S3) : Holder → List Nat\n40:def SelfLock (s : S3) (a : Nat) : Prop :=\n47:def Opt2Transfer (s : S3) (src dst : Nat) : Prop :=\n56:def Opt2Issue (s : S3) (ar : Arena) (region : List Nat) (dst : Nat) : Prop :=\n67:def Blocks (s : S3) (b a : Nat) : Prop :=\n74:def blockedBy (s : S3) (xs : List Nat) : List Nat :=\n78:def blockReach (s : S3) : Nat → List Nat → List Nat\n85:def BlocksAcyclic (s : S3) : Prop :=\n91:def NoLock (s : S3) : Prop :=\n100:def opt2 (ps : PS) : Op → Bool\n110:def opt3 (ps : PS) : Op → Bool\n121:def checked : Op → Bool\n129:def decisions (D : PS → Op → Bool) (ps : PS) : List Op → List Bool\n137:def dec2 (os : List Op) : List Bool := decisions opt2 (PS.init []) os\n138:def dec3 (os : List Op) : List Bool := decisions opt3 (PS.init []) os\n144:def mustAccept : List (String × List Op) :=\n155:theorem mustAccept_runs : mustAccept.all (fun c => (prun K0 (PS.init []) c.2).isSome) = true := by\n159:theorem opt2_decisions : mustAccept.map (fun c => (c.1, dec2 c.2)) =\n167:theorem opt3_decisions : mustAccept.map (fun c => (c.1, dec3 c.2)) =\n176:theorem no_false_rejection : mustAccept.all (fun c => (dec2 c.2).all id && (dec3 c.2).all id) =\n185:theorem H49_options : dec2 h49o = [true, true, true, true] ∧\n191:theorem H49_cycle : Blocks (storeEff (run K0 [] (h48o ++ [.derive 7 6 .modify])).s 8 6) 7 8 ∧\n197:theorem H50_options : dec2 h50ao = [true, false] ∧ dec3 h50ao = [true, false] ∧\n206:theorem H51_options : dec2 h51o = [true] ∧ dec3 h51o = [false] ∧\n217:theorem opt2_transfer_local {s s' : S3} {src dst : Nat} (hP : s'.P = s.P)\n247:theorem opt2_issue_local (s : S3) (ar : Arena) (region : List Nat) (dst : Nat) :\n255:def nl1 : PS := run K0 [] (h48o ++ [.derive 7 6 .modify])\n256:def nl2 : PS := run K0 [] (fao ++ [.derive 6 6 .modify, .derive 5 5 .modify, .derive 7 6 .modify])\n263:theorem opt3_not_local :","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"1f018540-fb25-4b3d-801a-d9844921d037","timestamp":"2026-11-03T13:35:42.291Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"import Ern.MM03.Horrors\n\n/-!\n# Measure of the `NoLock` options (jalon 3, step 4)\n\nThe options of the jalon-3 material (`ERN_Jalon3_materiel.md` v2, §5), measured on the kernel as it\nis (option 1, no rule), without modifying it:\n\n* option 2, a local rule: an operation does not place an authority into a place it covers\n  (`SelfLock`); `store` already rejects it (O8.3), so the rule is measured on `transfer` and\n  `issue` (`opt2`);\n* option 3, `NoLock`: no self-lock, as a separate clause, and the relation \"`b` blocks `a`\"\n  (`Blocks`) acyclic, checked on the arrival state of `transfer`, `issue` and `store` (`opt3`).\n\nFor each case of the list \"doit être accepté\" of §5 (H11, H19, H29b, H35 to H37, H44 to H47, W1\nto W3) and for H49 to H51, `decisions` gives the decision of an option on each `transfer`, `issue`\nand `store` of the run of the case (`Ern.MM03.Horrors`), decided on the state where the step runs;\n`true` is acceptance. The cost, measured as the brief asks (from the authorities and places the\noperation touches, or the whole state): option 2 on `transfer` depends on the state only through the\nplaces and the authorities the transfer moves (`opt2_transfer_local`), on `issue` only through the\nregion and the destination (`opt2_issue_local`); option 3 depends on authorities the operation does\nnot touch (`opt3_not_local`). Whether option 3 needs more than the function where the operation runs\n(material §5, \"locale à une fonction\") is not settled here (report, (g)). No option is adopted (task\nof jalon 3, step 4: the decision is left to arbitration).\n-/\n\nnamespace Ern.MM03.LockOptions\n\nopen Ern.MM03 Ern.HandlePool Ern.MM03.Horrors\n\n/-! ## Option 2: self-lock -/\n\n/-- The leaves of a holder (MM-03.3.4): those of a place, none for a frame. -/\ndef holderLeaves (s : S3) : Holder → List Nat\n  | .place p => footprint s.P p\n  | .frame _ => []\n\n/-- Self-lock of the authority `a` (material §5, options 2 and 3): `a` is active and held by a place\none of whose leaves it covers. -/\ndef SelfLock (s : S3) (a : Nat) : Prop :=\n  OptP (s.A[a]?) (fun y => y.active = true ∧ ∃ l ∈ y.footprint, l ∈ holderLeaves s y.holder) False\n\ninstance (s : S3) (a : Nat) : Decidable (SelfLock s a) := by unfold SelfLock; infer_instance\n\n/-- Option 2 on `transfer src dst` (material §5): no authority moved by the transfer, one held within\nthe source, is self-locked in the arrival state. -/\ndef Opt2Transfer (s : S3) (src dst : Nat) : Prop :=\n  ∀ j ∈ List.range s.A.length, OptP (s.A[j]?) (fun y => heldIn s.P src y.holder) False →\n    ¬ SelfLock (transferEff s src dst) j\n\ninstance (s : S3) (src dst : Nat) : Decidable (Opt2Transfer s src dst) := by\n  unfold Opt2Transfer; infer_instance\n\n/-- Option 2 on `issue` of `region` to `dst` (material §5): the block, the new authority, is not\nself-locked in the arrival state. -/\ndef Opt2Issue (s : S3) (ar : Arena) (region : List Nat) (dst : Nat) : Prop :=\n  ¬ SelfLock (issueEff s ar region dst).1 s.A.length\n\ninstance (s : S3) (ar : Arena) (region : List Nat) (dst : Nat) :\n    Decidable (Opt2Issue s ar region dst) := by\n  unfold Opt2Issue; infer_instance\n\n/-! ## Option 3: `NoLock` -/\n\n/-- \"`b` bloque `a`\" (material §5, option 3): `b ≠ a`, both active, and the footprint of `b` contains\na leaf of the holder of `a`. -/\ndef Blocks (s : S3) (b a : Nat) : Prop :=\n  b ≠ a ∧ s.Active b ∧ s.Active a ∧\n    OptP (s.A[a]?) (fun y => ∃ l ∈ s.afp b, l ∈ holderLeaves s y.holder) False\n\ninstance (s : S3) (b a : Nat) : Decidable (Blocks s b a) := by unfold Blocks; infer_instance\n\n/-- The authorities blocked by one of `xs`. -/\ndef blockedBy (s : S3) (xs : List Nat) : List Nat :=\n  (List.range s.A.length).filter fun a => decide (∃ b ∈ xs, Blocks s b a)\n\n/-- The authorities reached from `xs` by at most `n` steps of `Blocks`, `xs` included. -/\ndef blockReach (s : S3) : Nat → List Nat → List Nat\n  | 0, xs => xs\n  | n + 1, xs => blockReach s n (xs ++ blockedBy s xs)\n34:def holderLeaves (s : S3) : Holder → List Nat\n40:def SelfLock (s : S3) (a : Nat) : Prop :=\n47:def Opt2Transfer (s : S3) (src dst : Nat) : Prop :=\n56:def Opt2Issue (s : S3) (ar : Arena) (region : List Nat) (dst : Nat) : Prop :=\n67:def Blocks (s : S3) (b a : Nat) : Prop :=\n74:def blockedBy (s : S3) (xs : List Nat) : List Nat :=\n78:def blockReach (s : S3) : Nat → List Nat → List Nat\n85:def BlocksAcyclic (s : S3) : Prop :=\n91:def NoLock (s : S3) : Prop :=\n100:def opt2 (ps : PS) : Op → Bool\n110:def opt3 (ps : PS) : Op → Bool\n121:def checked : Op → Bool\n129:def decisions (D : PS → Op → Bool) (ps : PS) : List Op → List Bool\n137:def dec2 (os : List Op) : List Bool := decisions opt2 (PS.init []) os\n138:def dec3 (os : List Op) : List Bool := decisions opt3 (PS.init []) os\n144:def mustAccept : List (String × List Op) :=\n155:theorem mustAccept_runs : mustAccept.all (fun c => (prun K0 (PS.init []) c.2).isSome) = true := by\n159:theorem opt2_decisions : mustAccept.map (fun c => (c.1, dec2 c.2)) =\n167:theorem opt3_decisions : mustAccept.map (fun c => (c.1, dec3 c.2)) =\n176:theorem no_false_rejection : mustAccept.all (fun c => (dec2 c.2).all id && (dec3 c.2).all id) =\n185:theorem H49_options : dec2 h49o = [true, true, true, true] ∧\n191:theorem H49_cycle : Blocks (storeEff (run K0 [] (h48o ++ [.derive 7 6 .modify])).s 8 6) 7 8 ∧\n197:theorem H50_options : dec2 h50ao = [true, false] ∧ dec3 h50ao = [true, false] ∧\n206:theorem H51_options : dec2 h51o = [true] ∧ dec3 h51o = [false] ∧\n217:theorem opt2_transfer_local {s s' : S3} {src dst : Nat} (hP : s'.P = s.P)\n247:theorem opt2_issue_local (s : S3) (ar : Arena) (region : List Nat) (dst : Nat) :\n255:def nl1 : PS := run K0 [] (h48o ++ [.derive 7 6 .modify])\n256:def nl2 : PS := run K0 [] (fao ++ [.derive 6 6 .modify, .derive 5 5 .modify, .derive 7 6 .modify])\n263:theorem opt3_not_local :","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"ca63c733-abcc-490a-bbf8-694925b8f51a","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/validation_0.1","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c03303fd-69ea-4d84-bf99-b550f468e797","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/validation_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
