ide)\nexample : EnterStep [4, 5] [(none, none, 0)] (deriveEff (deriveEff a3 0 0 .observe) 2 2 .modify)\n    (.ok a6) := .ok (by decide)\nexample : IssueAt KA 0 4 [4] 6 a6 (.ok a7) := .ok (ar := ar7) (by decide) (.ok (by decide) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide))\nexample : TransferStep KA 6 2 a7 (.ok a8) := .ok (by decide)\nexample : ExitStep KA a8 (.ok a9) := .ok (by decide)\nexample : ResetAtStep KA 0 0 a9 .reject := .reject (by decide)\nexample : EndUseStep KA 2 a9 (.ok a10) := .ok (by decide)\nexample : ResetAtStep KA 0 0 a10 (.ok a11) := .ok (by decide)\n\n/-- The run of case 16 and n4 is an execution of `Reachable` from `S3.init []`, and the list of\narenas is not empty from `newArena` on. -/\ntheorem case16_reachable :\nErn/HandlePool.lean:461:  | reset hs =>\nErn/HandlePool.lean:463:    unfold resetAtEff; split <;> exact .same rfl\nErn/HandlePool.lean:525:  | reset hs =>\nErn/HandlePool.lean:527:    unfold resetAtEff; split <;> exact .same rfl\nErn/HandlePool.lean:553:  | reset hs => exact .reset hr hs\nErn/HandlePool.lean:1554:  | reset (i via : Nat)\nErn/HandlePool.lean:1595:  | .reset i via => if ResetAtPre k s i via then some (resetAtEff s i) else none\nErn/HandlePool.lean:1688:           | exact .reset (Guarded.ok hp)\nErn/MM03/Horrors.lean:249:`transfer` is accepted, `reset` is rejected while a block lives. Expected: `transfer` `ok`, `reset`\nErn/MM03/Horrors.lean:251:6), `reset` is accepted. -/\nErn/MM03/Horrors.lean:253:    PReach K0 [] (run K0 [] (h11p ++ [.endUse 3, .endUse 6, .reset 0 0])) :=\nErn/MM03/Horrors.lean:383:/-- **H19** (D; F1; Lib; covered pass 6). `reset` of the parent while the child lives: rejected;\nErn/MM03/Horrors.lean:386:    PReach K0 [] (run K0 [] (h19p ++ [.endUse 2, .reset 0 0])) :=\nErn/MM03/Horrors.lean:389:/-- **H20** (D; A10, `arena_reuse_safe`; Lib). `alloc`, `newArena`, `issue`, `endUse`, `reset`, then\nErn/MM03/Horrors.lean:393:    .reset 0 0, .issue 0 0 [4] 2]) :=\nErn/MM03/Horrors.lean:662:  .resolve 0 ⟨0, 1, 0⟩ .modify, .write 10 [11, 12], .unresolve 9, .endUse 2, .reset 0 0]\nErn/MM03/Horrors.lean:668:unresolved; `endUse` of the pool value; `reset` of the arena, without reading the links. Expected:\nErn/MM03/Horrors.lean:702:/-- H45: the run of the pass-6 witness `fb`, then `reset`. -/\nErn/MM03/Horrors.lean:707:  .derive 5 6 .modify, .store 8 10, .release 7, .release 8, .endUse 2, .endUse 3, .reset 0 0]\nErn/MM03/Horrors.lean:711:`endUse` of both node values), then `reset`. Expected: `ok` throughout; obtained: `ok`. -/\nErn/MM03/Horrors.lean:758:`release`: accepted; the authorities 7 and 8 are then exercisable at no mode and `reset` is\nErn/MM03/Horrors.lean:897:/-- **W3** (§5b, frame arena; Lib). Expected: `reset` while the views live: reject; after `endUse`\nErn/MM03/Horrors.lean:899:views live; after `endUse` of the structure, `reset` is still rejected, the three blocks being held\nErn/MM03/Horrors.lean:900:by the values 2, 3, 4 (MM-03.3 §6, O19.2); after their end, `reset` and the reissue are accepted.\nErn/MM03/Horrors.lean:905:    PReach K0 [] (run K0 [] (w3o ++ [.endUse 5, .endUse 2, .endUse 3, .endUse 4, .reset 0 0,\nErn/MM03/Horrors.lean:908:    PReach K0 [] (run K0 [] (w3vo ++ [.endUse 2, .reset 0 0, .issue 0 0 [10] 3])) :=","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"fc49edf1-bf5f-4954-af16-6bb3fc0c6714","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/validation_0.1","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}