{"parentUuid":"2751b977-36b7-42ed-b02b-a1db6368b316","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fcfe6e6f-a978-46ba-b770-f92b3a29d346","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015rWQmiUxzsCPrBJcfks137","type":"tool_result","content":"namespace Ern.MM03.Horrors\n\nopen Ern.MM03 Ern.HandlePool\n\n/-- The state given for a run whose steps are not all `ok`: it has no frame, so no run reaches it\n(`run_ok_of_reach`). -/\ndef stuckPS : PS := ⟨{ S3.init [] with F := [] }, [], 0, []⟩\n\nsection Run\nvariable (k : K) [∀ r r', Decidable (k.DeclaredDisjoint r r')] [DecidablePred k.SharedMutable]\n  [DecidablePred k.Pinned] [DecidablePred k.ExternalDone] [DecidablePred k.Deallocable]\n  [∀ p a, Decidable (k.FreeCompat p a)] [∀ p ls s, Decidable (k.Satisfiable p ls s)]\n\n/-- The state reached by the operations `os` from `S3.init statics`; `stuckPS` when a step is not\n`ok`. So a statement `PReach k statics (run k statics os)` says that every step is `ok`\n(`run_ok_of_reach`). -/\ndef run (statics : Statics) (os : List Op) : PS :=\n  (prun k (PS.init statics) os).getD stuckPS\n\nend Run\n\nsection RunSound\nvariable {k : K} [∀ r r', Decidable (k.DeclaredDisjoint r r')] [DecidablePred k.SharedMutable]\n  [DecidablePred k.Pinned] [DecidablePred k.ExternalDone] [DecidablePred k.Deallocable]\n  [∀ p a, Decidable (k.FreeCompat p a)] [∀ p ls s, Decidable (k.Satisfiable p ls s)]\n\n/-- A run whose steps are all `ok` reaches its final state (material §0, rule 3). -/\ntheorem run_reach {statics : Statics} {os : List Op} (hsh : ShapeOK 0 (statics.map (·.1)))\n    (h : (prun k (PS.init statics) os).isSome = true) : PReach k statics (run k statics os) :=\n  prun_init hsh (some_getD h)\n\n/-- Under `DDSound`, a reached `run` is a run whose every step is `ok`: the state given for a failed\nrun has no frame, which `WF3` excludes on reached states (MM-03.3 §2.1). -/\ntheorem run_ok_of_reach (hdd : DDSound k) {statics : Statics} {os : List Op}\n    (h : PReach k statics (run k statics os)) : (prun k (PS.init statics) os).isSome = true := by\n  cases hp : prun k (PS.init statics) os with\n  | some _ => rfl\n  | none =>\n    have hr := pReach_reachable hdd h\n    simp only [run, hp, Option.getD_none] at hr\n    exact absurd rfl (reachable_invariants hdd hr).1.2.2.1\n\nend RunSound\n\n/-- A read rejected for every authority of the state is rejected for every authority (MM-03.3 §5,\n`canRead3`: the reading authority exists). -/\ntheorem read_rejected {s : S3} {ls : List Nat} (h : ∀ a ∈ List.range s.A.length, ¬ canRead3 s a ls)\n    (a : Nat) : Read3Step a ls s .reject :=\n  .reject fun hc => by\n    by_cases ha : a < s.A.length\n    · exact h a (List.mem_range.2 ha) hc\n    · cases hc.1 with\n      | base hy => exact ha (lt_of_getElem? hy)\n      | held hy => exact ha (lt_of_getElem? hy)\n\nEach verdict is obtained by `decide` on the precondition of the operation concerned. States are\nbuilt from `S3.init` by the effects of operations. Classification of each case (kernel,\nabstraction with `K` instantiated, out of kernel) is given in the report. -/\n\n/-- Test contracts: `SharedMutable`, `Pinned`, `ExternalDone`, `Deallocable` given by lists of\nleaves or places, `FreeCompat` by a list of pairs; no declared disjointness; every allocation\nsatisfiable. -/\ndef KT (sh pinned done dealloc : List Nat) (compat : List (Nat × Nat)) : K :=\n  ⟨fun _ _ => False, (· ∈ sh), (· ∈ pinned), (· ∈ done), (· ∈ dealloc),\n    fun p a => (p, a) ∈ compat, fun _ _ _ => True⟩\n\nsection TestContracts\nvariable (sh pinned done dealloc : List Nat) (compat : List (Nat × Nat))\ninstance : ∀ r r', Decidable ((KT sh pinned done dealloc compat).DeclaredDisjoint r r') :=\n  fun _ _ => instDecidableFalse\ninstance : DecidablePred (KT sh pinned done dealloc compat).SharedMutable :=\n  fun l => inferInstanceAs (Decidable (l ∈ sh))\ninstance : DecidablePred (KT sh pinned done dealloc compat).Pinned :=\n  fun l => inferInstanceAs (Decidable (l ∈ pinned))\ninstance : DecidablePred (KT sh pinned done dealloc compat).ExternalDone :=\n  fun l => inferInstanceAs (Decidable (l ∈ done))\ninstance : DecidablePred (KT sh pinned done dealloc compat).Deallocable :=\n  fun p => inferInstanceAs (Decidable (p ∈ dealloc))\ninstance : ∀ p a, Decidable ((KT sh pinned done dealloc compat).FreeCompat p a) :=\n  fun p a => inferInstanceAs (Decidable ((p, a) ∈ compat))\ninstance : ∀ p ls s, Decidable ((KT sh pinned done dealloc compat).Satisfiable p ls s) :=\n  fun _ _ _ => instDecidableTrue\nend TestContracts\n\n/-- Empty contracts. -/\nabbrev K0 : K := KT [] [] [] [] []\n\ntheorem KT_dd (sh pinned done dealloc : List Nat) (compat : List (Nat × Nat)) :\n    DDSound (KT sh pinned done dealloc compat) := fun _ _ h => h.elim\n\n/-- Entering frame 1 from the initial frame with locals `ls`. -/\ndef enter1 (ls : List (Option Nat × Option Nat × Nat)) : S3 := enterEff (S3.init []) [] ls\n\n/-! ### Case 1: two observations of a leaf (expected: allowed) -/\n\ndef c1a : S3 := write3Eff (enter1 [(none, none, 0)]) [0]\nErn/MM03.lean:8755:abbrev K0 : K := KT [] [] [] [] []\nErn/MM03.lean:8810:abbrev KA : K := KT [0] [] [] [] []\ndef PS.init (statics : Statics) : PS := ⟨S3.init statics, [], 0, []⟩\n\n/-- States reached from the initial state by kernel, arena and pool steps (material §4, extension of\n`Reachable`, MM-03.3 §10). -/\ninductive PReach (k : K) (statics : Statics) : PS → Prop where\n  | init : ShapeOK 0 (statics.map (·.1)) → PReach k statics (PS.init statics)\n  | step {ps ps' : PS} : PReach k statics ps → PStep k ps ps' → PReach k statics ps'\n\n/-! ## Kernel steps keep authorities and footprints (MM-03.3 §3–6) -/\n\n/-- The authorities of `s` remain in `s'` with their mode and footprint; one active in `s'` was\nactive in `s` and, if it was derived, is still derived. -/\ndef KeepsAuth (s s' : S3) : Prop :=\n  s.A.length ≤ s'.A.length ∧ ∀ (j : Nat) (y' : Authority), s'.A[j]? = some y' → j < s.A.length →\n    ∃ y, s.A[j]? = some y ∧ y'.mode = y.mode ∧ y'.footprint = y.footprint ∧\n      (y'.active = true → y.active = true ∧ (y.origin ≠ none → y'.origin ≠ none))\n\ntheorem KeepsAuth.refl (s : S3) : KeepsAuth s s :=\n  ⟨Nat.le_refl _, fun _ y' hy' _ => ⟨y', hy', rfl, rfl, fun ha => ⟨ha, id⟩⟩⟩\n\ntheorem KeepsAuth.trans {s s₁ s₂ : S3} (h₁ : KeepsAuth s s₁) (h₂ : KeepsAuth s₁ s₂) :\n    KeepsAuth s s₂ := by\n  refine ⟨Nat.le_trans h₁.1 h₂.1, fun j y₂ hy₂ hj => ?_⟩\n  obtain ⟨y₁, hy₁, m₁, f₁, a₁⟩ := h₂.2 j y₂ hy₂ (Nat.lt_of_lt_of_le hj h₁.1)\n  obtain ⟨y, hy, m, f, a⟩ := h₁.2 j y₁ hy₁ hj\n  exact ⟨y, hy, m₁.trans m, f₁.trans f, fun ha =>\n    ⟨(a (a₁ ha).1).1, fun ho => (a₁ ha).2 ((a (a₁ ha).1).2 ho)⟩⟩\n\ntheorem KeepsAuth.of_releases {s s₁ : S3} (h : OnlyReleases s s₁) : KeepsAuth s s₁ :=\n  ⟨Nat.le_of_eq h.1.symm, fun j z hz _ => by\n    obtain ⟨y, hy, m, o, f, -, a⟩ := h.2 j z hz\n530:theorem reachable_step {k : K} {statics : Statics} {s s' : S3} (hr : Reachable k statics s)\n570:theorem reachable_steps {k : K} {statics : Statics} {s s' : S3} (hr : Reachable k statics s)\n678:theorem pReach_reachable {k : K} (hdd : DDSound k) {statics : Statics} {ps : PS}","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a7d85c19-dc89-4250-adf4-2134e5019c0f","timestamp":"2026-11-03T13:42:43.193Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"namespace Ern.MM03.Horrors\n\nopen Ern.MM03 Ern.HandlePool\n\n/-- The state given for a run whose steps are not all `ok`: it has no frame, so no run reaches it\n(`run_ok_of_reach`). -/\ndef stuckPS : PS := ⟨{ S3.init [] with F := [] }, [], 0, []⟩\n\nsection Run\nvariable (k : K) [∀ r r', Decidable (k.DeclaredDisjoint r r')] [DecidablePred k.SharedMutable]\n  [DecidablePred k.Pinned] [DecidablePred k.ExternalDone] [DecidablePred k.Deallocable]\n  [∀ p a, Decidable (k.FreeCompat p a)] [∀ p ls s, Decidable (k.Satisfiable p ls s)]\n\n/-- The state reached by the operations `os` from `S3.init statics`; `stuckPS` when a step is not\n`ok`. So a statement `PReach k statics (run k statics os)` says that every step is `ok`\n(`run_ok_of_reach`). -/\ndef run (statics : Statics) (os : List Op) : PS :=\n  (prun k (PS.init statics) os).getD stuckPS\n\nend Run\n\nsection RunSound\nvariable {k : K} [∀ r r', Decidable (k.DeclaredDisjoint r r')] [DecidablePred k.SharedMutable]\n  [DecidablePred k.Pinned] [DecidablePred k.ExternalDone] [DecidablePred k.Deallocable]\n  [∀ p a, Decidable (k.FreeCompat p a)] [∀ p ls s, Decidable (k.Satisfiable p ls s)]\n\n/-- A run whose steps are all `ok` reaches its final state (material §0, rule 3). -/\ntheorem run_reach {statics : Statics} {os : List Op} (hsh : ShapeOK 0 (statics.map (·.1)))\n    (h : (prun k (PS.init statics) os).isSome = true) : PReach k statics (run k statics os) :=\n  prun_init hsh (some_getD h)\n\n/-- Under `DDSound`, a reached `run` is a run whose every step is `ok`: the state given for a failed\nrun has no frame, which `WF3` excludes on reached states (MM-03.3 §2.1). -/\ntheorem run_ok_of_reach (hdd : DDSound k) {statics : Statics} {os : List Op}\n    (h : PReach k statics (run k statics os)) : (prun k (PS.init statics) os).isSome = true := by\n  cases hp : prun k (PS.init statics) os with\n  | some _ => rfl\n  | none =>\n    have hr := pReach_reachable hdd h\n    simp only [run, hp, Option.getD_none] at hr\n    exact absurd rfl (reachable_invariants hdd hr).1.2.2.1\n\nend RunSound\n\n/-- A read rejected for every authority of the state is rejected for every authority (MM-03.3 §5,\n`canRead3`: the reading authority exists). -/\ntheorem read_rejected {s : S3} {ls : List Nat} (h : ∀ a ∈ List.range s.A.length, ¬ canRead3 s a ls)\n    (a : Nat) : Read3Step a ls s .reject :=\n  .reject fun hc => by\n    by_cases ha : a < s.A.length\n    · exact h a (List.mem_range.2 ha) hc\n    · cases hc.1 with\n      | base hy => exact ha (lt_of_getElem? hy)\n      | held hy => exact ha (lt_of_getElem? hy)\n\nEach verdict is obtained by `decide` on the precondition of the operation concerned. States are\nbuilt from `S3.init` by the effects of operations. Classification of each case (kernel,\nabstraction with `K` instantiated, out of kernel) is given in the report. -/\n\n/-- Test contracts: `SharedMutable`, `Pinned`, `ExternalDone`, `Deallocable` given by lists of\nleaves or places, `FreeCompat` by a list of pairs; no declared disjointness; every allocation\nsatisfiable. -/\ndef KT (sh pinned done dealloc : List Nat) (compat : List (Nat × Nat)) : K :=\n  ⟨fun _ _ => False, (· ∈ sh), (· ∈ pinned), (· ∈ done), (· ∈ dealloc),\n    fun p a => (p, a) ∈ compat, fun _ _ _ => True⟩\n\nsection TestContracts\nvariable (sh pinned done dealloc : List Nat) (compat : List (Nat × Nat))\ninstance : ∀ r r', Decidable ((KT sh pinned done dealloc compat).DeclaredDisjoint r r') :=\n  fun _ _ => instDecidableFalse\ninstance : DecidablePred (KT sh pinned done dealloc compat).SharedMutable :=\n  fun l => inferInstanceAs (Decidable (l ∈ sh))\ninstance : DecidablePred (KT sh pinned done dealloc compat).Pinned :=\n  fun l => inferInstanceAs (Decidable (l ∈ pinned))\ninstance : DecidablePred (KT sh pinned done dealloc compat).ExternalDone :=\n  fun l => inferInstanceAs (Decidable (l ∈ done))\ninstance : DecidablePred (KT sh pinned done dealloc compat).Deallocable :=\n  fun p => inferInstanceAs (Decidable (p ∈ dealloc))\ninstance : ∀ p a, Decidable ((KT sh pinned done dealloc compat).FreeCompat p a) :=\n  fun p a => inferInstanceAs (Decidable ((p, a) ∈ compat))\ninstance : ∀ p ls s, Decidable ((KT sh pinned done dealloc compat).Satisfiable p ls s) :=\n  fun _ _ _ => instDecidableTrue\nend TestContracts\n\n/-- Empty contracts. -/\nabbrev K0 : K := KT [] [] [] [] []\n\ntheorem KT_dd (sh pinned done dealloc : List Nat) (compat : List (Nat × Nat)) :\n    DDSound (KT sh pinned done dealloc compat) := fun _ _ h => h.elim\n\n/-- Entering frame 1 from the initial frame with locals `ls`. -/\ndef enter1 (ls : List (Option Nat × Option Nat × Nat)) : S3 := enterEff (S3.init []) [] ls\n\n/-! ### Case 1: two observations of a leaf (expected: allowed) -/\n\ndef c1a : S3 := write3Eff (enter1 [(none, none, 0)]) [0]\nErn/MM03.lean:8755:abbrev K0 : K := KT [] [] [] [] []\nErn/MM03.lean:8810:abbrev KA : K := KT [0] [] [] [] []\ndef PS.init (statics : Statics) : PS := ⟨S3.init statics, [], 0, []⟩\n\n/-- States reached from the initial state by kernel, arena and pool steps (material §4, extension of\n`Reachable`, MM-03.3 §10). -/\ninductive PReach (k : K) (statics : Statics) : PS → Prop where\n  | init : ShapeOK 0 (statics.map (·.1)) → PReach k statics (PS.init statics)\n  | step {ps ps' : PS} : PReach k statics ps → PStep k ps ps' → PReach k statics ps'\n\n/-! ## Kernel steps keep authorities and footprints (MM-03.3 §3–6) -/\n\n/-- The authorities of `s` remain in `s'` with their mode and footprint; one active in `s'` was\nactive in `s` and, if it was derived, is still derived. -/\ndef KeepsAuth (s s' : S3) : Prop :=\n  s.A.length ≤ s'.A.length ∧ ∀ (j : Nat) (y' : Authority), s'.A[j]? = some y' → j < s.A.length →\n    ∃ y, s.A[j]? = some y ∧ y'.mode = y.mode ∧ y'.footprint = y.footprint ∧\n      (y'.active = true → y.active = true ∧ (y.origin ≠ none → y'.origin ≠ none))\n\ntheorem KeepsAuth.refl (s : S3) : KeepsAuth s s :=\n  ⟨Nat.le_refl _, fun _ y' hy' _ => ⟨y', hy', rfl, rfl, fun ha => ⟨ha, id⟩⟩⟩\n\ntheorem KeepsAuth.trans {s s₁ s₂ : S3} (h₁ : KeepsAuth s s₁) (h₂ : KeepsAuth s₁ s₂) :\n    KeepsAuth s s₂ := by\n  refine ⟨Nat.le_trans h₁.1 h₂.1, fun j y₂ hy₂ hj => ?_⟩\n  obtain ⟨y₁, hy₁, m₁, f₁, a₁⟩ := h₂.2 j y₂ hy₂ (Nat.lt_of_lt_of_le hj h₁.1)\n  obtain ⟨y, hy, m, f, a⟩ := h₁.2 j y₁ hy₁ hj\n  exact ⟨y, hy, m₁.trans m, f₁.trans f, fun ha =>\n    ⟨(a (a₁ ha).1).1, fun ho => (a₁ ha).2 ((a (a₁ ha).1).2 ho)⟩⟩\n\ntheorem KeepsAuth.of_releases {s s₁ : S3} (h : OnlyReleases s s₁) : KeepsAuth s s₁ :=\n  ⟨Nat.le_of_eq h.1.symm, fun j z hz _ => by\n    obtain ⟨y, hy, m, o, f, -, a⟩ := h.2 j z hz\n530:theorem reachable_step {k : K} {statics : Statics} {s s' : S3} (hr : Reachable k statics s)\n570:theorem reachable_steps {k : K} {statics : Statics} {s s' : S3} (hr : Reachable k statics s)\n678:theorem pReach_reachable {k : K} (hdd : DDSound k) {statics : Statics} {ps : PS}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"19e0f7c9-aa96-45f3-9e63-58dc6fc9981f","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/validation_0.1","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2751b977-36b7-42ed-b02b-a1db6368b316","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/validation_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
