{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","id":"cdd72c1d-0dd5-40a1-9d5e-a5241c34495a","timestamp":"2026-11-03T13:52:19.736Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"d1aa6c2254c890b11835611a868b353c28b0e75545aafd34fb8d8155d691dfb1","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"xhigh"}},"base":"710894d5-8958-4908-9d43-0c0b9f2b535b","keep":77,"tail":["334e33d93e3418879ca029eff256724eb06efd5f99929825269ff92aa6ba8a63","651d0b075a4a62aaa775eba4f9883306c0d6c22d0dbf06ae7866a5011d618c48"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",78,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"fbb3309e6821747989ada81c5350f8a6eb798ac8aad1954530921fdc433dabbd"}
{"parentUuid":"a15c1126-bad3-4532-9845-72b97796c4cd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgg73dPFzSSDrixhotjpP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GQ95VApJSwbNq3X5nyZ6U1","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='Ern/Derived/Arena.lean'\ns=open(p).read()\nadd = r'''\n/-- An active `Modify` descendant of `a` covering `p` takes the effective `Modify` of `a` on `p`\naway (§43, case 3). -/\ntheorem effective_ne_modify_of_desc {s : S3} {a j p : Nat} {y : Authority} (hy : s.A[j]? = some y)\n    (ya : y.active = true) (hp : p ∈ y.footprint) (hj : a ∈ s.ancs j) (hm : y.mode = .modify) :\n    effective s a p ≠ some .modify := by\n  intro he\n  obtain ⟨x, -, -, -, hx⟩ := effective_some he\n  have hmem : Mode.modify ∈ descModes s a p := mem_descModes.2 ⟨j, y, hy, ya, hp, hj, hm⟩\n  rcases effOf_cases hx with ⟨h0, -⟩ | ⟨-, h1, -⟩\n  · rw [h0] at hmem; simp at hmem\n  · exact h1 hmem\n\n/-- The restricted right is exactly the exercise of `internal` at `Modify` (§43), the first\nprecondition of `derive` and `split` on `internal` (O1.1, O2.1): `internal` is a `Modify` authority\nheld by the arena value (`ArenaInv`, §55). -/\ntheorem metaRightM_iff {s : S3} {ar : Arena} (hai : ArenaInv s ar) (hact : s.Active ar.internal) :\n    MetaRightM s ar ↔ s.ExercisableAt ar.internal .modify := by\n  obtain ⟨y, v, hy, hm, hv⟩ := hai.2.2.2.2.2.2.1\n  have hav : arenaValue s ar = some v := by simp [arenaValue, hy, hv]\n  obtain ⟨y', hy', ya⟩ := hact\n  rw [hy] at hy'; cases hy'\n  unfold MetaRightM; rw [hav]; simp only [OptP]\n  constructor\n  · rintro ⟨b, -, hb, hall⟩\n    exact .held hy ya (.inr hm) hv hb hall\n  · intro h\n    cases h with\n    | base hy₂ _ _ hf => rw [hy] at hy₂; cases hy₂; rw [hv] at hf; cases hf\n    | held hy₂ _ _ hp hb hc =>\n      rw [hy] at hy₂; cases hy₂; rw [hv] at hp; cases hp\n      exact ⟨_, List.mem_range.2 hb.lt, hb, hc⟩\n\n/-- The effective anchor of an authority with an origin is strictly older than it. -/\ntheorem effAnchor_lt {s : S3} {x o : Nat} (ho : s.org x = some o) (hlt : o < x) :\n    s.effAnchor x < x := by\n  unfold S3.effAnchor S3.ancs\n  rw [chain_cons ho hlt]\n  exact chain_lt (by rw [chain_cons ho hlt]; exact List.getLastD_mem_cons)\n\n/-- `store` changes no `EffAnchorOK` whose effective anchor is not the stored authority. -/\ntheorem effAnchorOK_store {s : S3} {a p x : Nat} {y : Authority} (hy : s.A[a]? = some y)\n    (hne : s.effAnchor x ≠ a) (fd : Option Nat) :\n    EffAnchorOK (storeEff s a p) x fd ↔ EffAnchorOK s x fd := by\n  have he : (storeEff s a p).effAnchor x = s.effAnchor x := by\n    unfold S3.effAnchor; rw [(store_skel s a p).ancs]\n  have hP : (storeEff s a p).P = s.P := by rw [storeEff_eq hy]\n  have hF : (storeEff s a p).F = s.F := by rw [storeEff_eq hy]\n  have hA : (storeEff s a p).A[s.effAnchor x]? = s.A[s.effAnchor x]? := by\n    rw [storeEff_eq hy]; exact List.getElem?_set_ne (Ne.symm hne)\n  unfold EffAnchorOK\n  rw [he, hA, hF]\n  simp only [S3.hframe_congr hP]\n\n/-! ## `issue` as `split` (or `derive`) then `store` -/\n\nsection IssueAsKernel\n\nvariable {k : K} (hdd : DDSound k) {statics : Statics} {s : S3} (hr : Reachable k statics s)\n  {ar : Arena} (har : ar ∈ s.arenas) {region : List Nat} {dst : Nat}\ninclude hdd hr har\n\n/-- Direction `issue` → sequence (brief, question 1): an `ok` of the restricted `issue` whose\ndestination is still exercisable at `Modify` in the arrival state is the `ok` of `split` of\n`internal` on the region, then of `store` of the block into the destination, with the same\narrival state. The extra hypothesis is clause 5 of `store` (O8.5, `store_keeps_target_reachable`),\nwhich the restricted `issue` does not check: `ce_g2` shows it is needed. Clause 3 of `store` on the\nstorage owned by the destination (O8.3) follows from clause 2 of `issue` (no active authority held\nby the destination) in reached states (`ownedIn_holds`). -/\ntheorem issue_to_seq {s' : S3} {ar' : Arena} (h : IssueR ar region dst s (.ok s' ar'))\n    (hg2 : HasRight s' .modify dst) :\n    SplitStep k ar.internal [region] s (.ok (s.addAuth (blockOf s ar region))) ∧\n      StoreStep s.A.length dst (s.addAuth (blockOf s ar region)) (.ok s') := by\n  obtain ⟨hwf, hinv, -, hais⟩ := reachable_invariants hdd hr\n  have hrl := reachable_rootLive hdd hr\n  obtain ⟨hst, -, hright, harr, he⟩ := issueR_ok_iff.1 h\n  have hs' : s' = storeEff (s.addAuth (blockOf s ar region)) s.A.length dst := by\n    rw [← issueEffR_eq]; exact congrArg Prod.fst he\n  obtain ⟨hm, hact, hreg, hud, -, -, hleaf, hnoh, hnot⟩ := hst\n  have hai := hais ar har hact\n  have hex := (metaRightM_iff hai hact).1 hm\n  obtain ⟨yi, hyi, yia⟩ := hact\n  refine ⟨.ok ⟨⟨yi, hyi, yia⟩, hex, ?_, ?_, List.pairwise_singleton _ _, ?_⟩, .ok ?_⟩\n  · intro r hr' p hp; rw [List.mem_singleton.1 hr'] at hp; exact hright p hp\n  · intro r hr' p hp; rw [List.mem_singleton.1 hr'] at hp\n    exact ⟨hreg p hp, by rw [hright p hp]; simp⟩\n  · intro r hr' p hp j _ hd\n    rw [List.mem_singleton.1 hr'] at hp\n    unfold DistribExcl at hd\n    cases hj : s.A[j]? with\n    | none => rw [hj] at hd; exact hd\n    | some y =>\n      rw [hj] at hd; obtain ⟨ya, hanc, hpy, hmy⟩ := hd\n      exact effective_ne_modify_of_desc hj ya hpy hanc hmy (hright p hp)\n  · -- `StorePre` on the state after `split`\n    set s₁ := s.addAuth (blockOf s ar region) with hs₁\n    have hy₀ : s₁.A[s.A.length]? = some (blockOf s ar region) := addAuth_self _ _\n    have hdl : dst < s.P.length := hud.lt\n    have hfd : ∀ l, l ∈ footprint s.P dst ↔ l = dst := fun l => mem_footprint_leaf hleaf hdl\n    have hu₁ : s₁.Usable dst := (S3.Usable.congr rfl rfl rfl).2 hud\n    have hne : s₁.effAnchor s.A.length ≠ s.A.length := by\n      have := effAnchor_lt (s := s₁) (x := s.A.length) (o := ar.internal)\n        (by simp [S3.org, hy₀, blockOf]) (hwf.2.1 |> fun _ => ArenasWF_lt hai hyi)\n      omega\n    have hs₂ : storeEff s₁ s.A.length dst = s' := hs'.symm\n    refine ⟨by simp [OptP, hy₀, blockOf, S3.top, s₁, S3.addAuth], hu₁, ?_, ?_, ?_, hleaf, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩\n    · rw [hs₂] at *\n      exact hasRight_store_back hy₀ rfl (by rw [← hs₂] at hg2 ⊢; exact hg2)\n    · intro l hl\n      have hlr : l ∈ region := by simpa [S3.afp, hy₀, blockOf] using hl\n      refine ⟨fun hld => hnot (by rw [(hfd l).1 hld] at hlr; exact hlr), fun q _ hown hlq => ?_⟩\n      have hreg' : l ∈ yi.footprint := by simpa [S3.afp, hyi] using hreg l hlr\n      have huq := usable_of_covered hinv.nd hyi yia hreg' hlq\n      obtain ⟨j, z, hz, za, hzh⟩ := ownedIn_holds hwf hrl hleaf hown huq\n      have := hnoh j (List.mem_range.2 (lt_of_getElem? hz))\n      rw [hz] at this; exact this za hzh\n    · rw [← effAnchorOK_store hy₀ hne]\n      have h1 := harr.1\n      rw [issueEffR_eq] at h1\n      simpa [S3.addAuth] using h1\n    · intro j hj\n      by_cases hjl : j < s.A.length\n      · rw [show s₁.A[j]? = s.A[j]? from addAuth_lt hjl]\n        exact hnoh j (List.mem_range.2 hjl)\n      · have : j = s.A.length := by\n          have := List.mem_range.1 hj; simp [s₁, S3.addAuth] at this; omega\n        subst this; rw [hy₀]; simp [OptP, blockOf]\n    · rw [hs₂]; exact hg2\n    · have h2 := harr.2; rw [issueEffR_eq] at h2; exact h2\n\nend IssueAsKernel\n\nend Ern.Derived.Arena\n'''\ns=s.replace(\"\\nend Ern.Derived.Arena\\n\", add)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\n~/.elan/bin/lake env lean Ern/Derived/Arena.lean 2>&1 | head -80","description":"Add issue-to-sequence direction and compile","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":557,"cache_read_input_tokens":292530,"output_tokens":3952,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":557,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3952,"cache_read_input_tokens":292530,"cache_creation_input_tokens":557,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":557},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01GQ95VApJSwbNq3X5nyZ6U1":{"command":"cd ~/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='Ern/Derived/Arena.lean'\ns=open(p).read()\nadd = r'''\n/-- An active `Modify` descendant of `a` covering `p` takes the effective `Modify` of `a` on `p`\naway (§43, case 3). -/\ntheorem effective_ne_modify_of_desc {s : S3} {a j p : Nat} {y : Authority} (hy : s.A[j]? = some y)\n    (ya : y.active = true) (hp : p ∈ y.footprint) (hj : a ∈ s.ancs j) (hm : y.mode = .modify) :\n    effective s a p ≠ some .modify := by\n  intro he\n  obtain ⟨x, -, -, -, hx⟩ := effective_some he\n  have hmem : Mode.modify ∈ descModes s a p := mem_descModes.2 ⟨j, y, hy, ya, hp, hj, hm⟩\n  rcases effOf_cases hx with ⟨h0, -⟩ | ⟨-, h1, -⟩\n  · rw [h0] at hmem; simp at hmem\n  · exact h1 hmem\n\n/-- The restricted right is exactly the exercise of `internal` at `Modify` (§43), the first\nprecondition of `derive` and `split` on `internal` (O1.1, O2.1): `internal` is a `Modify` authority\nheld by the arena value (`ArenaInv`, §55). -/\ntheorem metaRightM_iff {s : S3} {ar : Arena} (hai : ArenaInv s ar) (hact : s.Active ar.internal) :\n    MetaRightM s ar ↔ s.ExercisableAt ar.internal .modify := by\n  obtain ⟨y, v, hy, hm, hv⟩ := hai.2.2.2.2.2.2.1\n  have hav : arenaValue s ar = some v := by simp [arenaValue, hy, hv]\n  obtain ⟨y', hy', ya⟩ := hact\n  rw [hy] at hy'; cases hy'\n  unfold MetaRightM; rw [hav]; simp only [OptP]\n  constructor\n  · rintro ⟨b, -, hb, hall⟩\n    exact .held hy ya (.inr hm) hv hb hall\n  · intro h\n    cases h with\n    | base hy₂ _ _ hf => rw [hy] at hy₂; cases hy₂; rw [hv] at hf; cases hf\n    | held hy₂ _ _ hp hb hc =>\n      rw [hy] at hy₂; cases hy₂; rw [hv] at hp; cases hp\n      exact ⟨_, List.mem_range.2 hb.lt, hb, hc⟩\n\n/-- The effective anchor of an authority with an origin is strictly older than it. -/\ntheorem effAnchor_lt {s : S3} {x o : Nat} (ho : s.org x = some o) (hlt : o < x) :\n    s.effAnchor x < x := by\n  unfold S3.effAnchor S3.ancs\n  rw [chain_cons ho hlt]\n  exact chain_lt (by rw [chain_cons ho hlt]; exact List.getLastD_mem_cons)\n\n/-- `store` changes no `EffAnchorOK` whose effective anchor is not the stored authority. -/\ntheorem effAnchorOK_store {s : S3} {a p x : Nat} {y : Authority} (hy : s.A[a]? = some y)\n    (hne : s.effAnchor x ≠ a) (fd : Option Nat) :\n    EffAnchorOK (storeEff s a p) x fd ↔ EffAnchorOK s x fd := by\n  have he : (storeEff s a p).effAnchor x = s.effAnchor x := by\n    unfold S3.effAnchor; rw [(store_skel s a p).ancs]\n  have hP : (storeEff s a p).P = s.P := by rw [storeEff_eq hy]\n  have hF : (storeEff s a p).F = s.F := by rw [storeEff_eq hy]\n  have hA : (storeEff s a p).A[s.effAnchor x]? = s.A[s.effAnchor x]? := by\n    rw [storeEff_eq hy]; exact List.getElem?_set_ne (Ne.symm hne)\n  unfold EffAnchorOK\n  rw [he, hA, hF]\n  simp only [S3.hframe_congr hP]\n\n/-! ## `issue` as `split` (or `derive`) then `store` -/\n\nsection IssueAsKernel\n\nvariable {k : K} (hdd : DDSound k) {statics : Statics} {s : S3} (hr : Reachable k statics s)\n  {ar : Arena} (har : ar ∈ s.arenas) {region : List Nat} {dst : Nat}\ninclude hdd hr har\n\n/-- Direction `issue` → sequence (brief, question 1): an `ok` of the restricted `issue` whose\ndestination is still exercisable at `Modify` in the arrival state is the `ok` of `split` of\n`internal` on the region, then of `store` of the block into the destination, with the same\narrival state. The extra hypothesis is clause 5 of `store` (O8.5, `store_keeps_target_reachable`),\nwhich the restricted `issue` does not check: `ce_g2` shows it is needed. Clause 3 of `store` on the\nstorage owned by the destination (O8.3) follows from clause 2 of `issue` (no active authority held\nby the destination) in reached states (`ownedIn_holds`). -/\ntheorem issue_to_seq {s' : S3} {ar' : Arena} (h : IssueR ar region dst s (.ok s' ar'))\n    (hg2 : HasRight s' .modify dst) :\n    SplitStep k ar.internal [region] s (.ok (s.addAuth (blockOf s ar region))) ∧\n      StoreStep s.A.length dst (s.addAuth (blockOf s ar region)) (.ok s') := by\n  obtain ⟨hwf, hinv, -, hais⟩ := reachable_invariants hdd hr\n  have hrl := reachable_rootLive hdd hr\n  obtain ⟨hst, -, hright, harr, he⟩ := issueR_ok_iff.1 h\n  have hs' : s' = storeEff (s.addAuth (blockOf s ar region)) s.A.length dst := by\n    rw [← issueEffR_eq]; exact congrArg Prod.fst he\n  obtain ⟨hm, hact, hreg, hud, -, -, hleaf, hnoh, hnot⟩ := hst\n  have hai := hais ar har hact\n  have hex := (metaRightM_iff hai hact).1 hm\n  obtain ⟨yi, hyi, yia⟩ := hact\n  refine ⟨.ok ⟨⟨yi, hyi, yia⟩, hex, ?_, ?_, List.pairwise_singleton _ _, ?_⟩, .ok ?_⟩\n  · intro r hr' p hp; rw [List.mem_singleton.1 hr'] at hp; exact hright p hp\n  · intro r hr' p hp; rw [List.mem_singleton.1 hr'] at hp\n    exact ⟨hreg p hp, by rw [hright p hp]; simp⟩\n  · intro r hr' p hp j _ hd\n    rw [List.mem_singleton.1 hr'] at hp\n    unfold DistribExcl at hd\n    cases hj : s.A[j]? with\n    | none => rw [hj] at hd; exact hd\n    | some y =>\n      rw [hj] at hd; obtain ⟨ya, hanc, hpy, hmy⟩ := hd\n      exact effective_ne_modify_of_desc hj ya hpy hanc hmy (hright p hp)\n  · -- `StorePre` on the state after `split`\n    set s₁ := s.addAuth (blockOf s ar region) with hs₁\n    have hy₀ : s₁.A[s.A.length]? = some (blockOf s ar region) := addAuth_self _ _\n    have hdl : dst < s.P.length := hud.lt\n    have hfd : ∀ l, l ∈ footprint s.P dst ↔ l = dst := fun l => mem_footprint_leaf hleaf hdl\n    have hu₁ : s₁.Usable dst := (S3.Usable.congr rfl rfl rfl).2 hud\n    have hne : s₁.effAnchor s.A.length ≠ s.A.length := by\n      have := effAnchor_lt (s := s₁) (x := s.A.length) (o := ar.internal)\n        (by simp [S3.org, hy₀, blockOf]) (hwf.2.1 |> fun _ => ArenasWF_lt hai hyi)\n      omega\n    have hs₂ : storeEff s₁ s.A.length dst = s' := hs'.symm\n    refine ⟨by simp [OptP, hy₀, blockOf, S3.top, s₁, S3.addAuth], hu₁, ?_, ?_, ?_, hleaf, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩\n    · rw [hs₂] at *\n      exact hasRight_store_back hy₀ rfl (by rw [← hs₂] at hg2 ⊢; exact hg2)\n    · intro l hl\n      have hlr : l ∈ region := by simpa [S3.afp, hy₀, blockOf] using hl\n      refine ⟨fun hld => hnot (by rw [(hfd l).1 hld] at hlr; exact hlr), fun q _ hown hlq => ?_⟩\n      have hreg' : l ∈ yi.footprint := by simpa [S3.afp, hyi] using hreg l hlr\n      have huq := usable_of_covered hinv.nd hyi yia hreg' hlq\n      obtain ⟨j, z, hz, za, hzh⟩ := ownedIn_holds hwf hrl hleaf hown huq\n      have := hnoh j (List.mem_range.2 (lt_of_getElem? hz))\n      rw [hz] at this; exact this za hzh\n    · rw [← effAnchorOK_store hy₀ hne]\n      have h1 := harr.1\n      rw [issueEffR_eq] at h1\n      simpa [S3.addAuth] using h1\n    · intro j hj\n      by_cases hjl : j < s.A.length\n      · rw [show s₁.A[j]? = s.A[j]? from addAuth_lt hjl]\n        exact hnoh j (List.mem_range.2 hjl)\n      · have : j = s.A.length := by\n          have := List.mem_range.1 hj; simp [s₁, S3.addAuth] at this; omega\n        subst this; rw [hy₀]; simp [OptP, blockOf]\n    · rw [hs₂]; exact hg2\n    · have h2 := harr.2; rw [issueEffR_eq] at h2; exact h2\n\nend IssueAsKernel\n\nend Ern.Derived.Arena\n'''\ns=s.replace(\"\\nend Ern.Derived.Arena\\n\", add)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\n~/.elan/bin/lake env lean Ern/Derived/Arena.lean 2>&1 | head -80","description":"Add issue-to-sequence direction and compile","timeout":300000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"0f7054e7-dc2f-4831-a718-caa71837b098","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgg73d6AAhkZEX3aVBKeE","requestRef":"cdd72c1d-0dd5-40a1-9d5e-a5241c34495a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5fd1f77a-17d7-408e-b2b4-966b4d4fa593","timestamp":"2026