{"parentUuid":"3d4642ca-4d44-4d3f-95b9-f67a9b52e441","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fcfe6e6f-a978-46ba-b770-f92b3a29d346","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NG7hSJEje3u8okXCqeHtes","type":"tool_result","content":"Ern/Derived/Arena.lean:1155:62: error: omega could not prove the goal:\na possible counterexample may satisfy the constraints\n  c ≥ 0\n  b ≥ 0\n  b - c ≤ 0\n  b ≥ 0\n  a ≥ 0\n  a - b ≥ 1\n  a - b + c ≥ 0\n  a ≥ 1\nwhere\n a := ↑((run K0 [] opsArena).s.P.length - q)\n b := ↑(?m.92 - q)\n c := ↑?m.92\nErn/Derived/Arena.lean:1258:13: error: Expected type must not contain metavariables\n  IssueStatic K0 sTwo arL ?m.139 [5] 2\nErn/Derived/Arena.lean:1253:63: error: unsolved goals\nh1 : NewArenaPreNG (run K0 [] opsAlloc).s 4 4\nhr : ReachableNG K0 [] sTwo\n⊢ NewArenaPreNG (run K0 [] opsAlloc).s 4 4 ∧\n    NewArenaStep 4 4 (run K0 [] opsAlloc).s Outcome3.reject ∧\n      ReachableNG K0 [] sTwoIssued ∧\n        List.map (fun x => x.available) sTwoIssued.arenas = [[6], [5, 6]] ∧\n          IssueAt K0 1 0 [5] 3 sTwoIssued AOutcome.reject ∧\n            IssueStatic K0 sTwoIssued arL 0 [5] 3 ∧ Avail arL [5] ∧ SplitStep K0 4 [[5]] sTwoIssued Outcome3.reject\n~/.elan/bin/lake env lean Ern/Derived/Arena.lean 2>&1  2.32s user 0.24s system 154% cpu 1.653 total\nhead -60  0.00s user 0.00s system 0% cpu 1.653 total","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cc8180ec-3bea-4062-bbba-a1143c0ee198","timestamp":"2026-11-03T14:00:36.313Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Ern/Derived/Arena.lean:1155:62: error: omega could not prove the goal:\na possible counterexample may satisfy the constraints\n  c ≥ 0\n  b ≥ 0\n  b - c ≤ 0\n  b ≥ 0\n  a ≥ 0\n  a - b ≥ 1\n  a - b + c ≥ 0\n  a ≥ 1\nwhere\n a := ↑((run K0 [] opsArena).s.P.length - q)\n b := ↑(?m.92 - q)\n c := ↑?m.92\nErn/Derived/Arena.lean:1258:13: error: Expected type must not contain metavariables\n  IssueStatic K0 sTwo arL ?m.139 [5] 2\nErn/Derived/Arena.lean:1253:63: error: unsolved goals\nh1 : NewArenaPreNG (run K0 [] opsAlloc).s 4 4\nhr : ReachableNG K0 [] sTwo\n⊢ NewArenaPreNG (run K0 [] opsAlloc).s 4 4 ∧\n    NewArenaStep 4 4 (run K0 [] opsAlloc).s Outcome3.reject ∧\n      ReachableNG K0 [] sTwoIssued ∧\n        List.map (fun x => x.available) sTwoIssued.arenas = [[6], [5, 6]] ∧\n          IssueAt K0 1 0 [5] 3 sTwoIssued AOutcome.reject ∧\n            IssueStatic K0 sTwoIssued arL 0 [5] 3 ∧ Avail arL [5] ∧ SplitStep K0 4 [[5]] sTwoIssued Outcome3.reject\n~/.elan/bin/lake env lean Ern/Derived/Arena.lean 2>&1  2.32s user 0.24s system 154% cpu 1.653 total\nhead -60  0.00s user 0.00s system 0% cpu 1.653 total","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":true,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/Derived/Arena.lean","hunks":[{"oldStart":1063,"oldLines":4,"newStart":1063,"newLines":213,"lines":["   ⟨fun h => effective_ne_modify_of_desc hy ya hly hj hm (h l hl),","    fun h => effective_ne_modify_of_desc hy ya hly hj hm (h.2.2.1 region (List.mem_singleton_self _) l hl)⟩"," ","+/-! ## Counterexamples on reached states","+","+Runs from `S3.init []` with the test contracts `K0` (no `SharedMutable` leaf) or `KA` (leaf 0","+`SharedMutable`); every verdict by `decide`. -/","+","+/-- Reachability of a run whose steps are all `ok`, under `K0`. -/","+theorem reach_run {os : List Op} (h : (prun K0 (PS.init []) os).isSome = true) :","+    Reachable K0 [] (run K0 [] os).s :=","+  pReach_reachable (KT_dd _ _ _ _ _) (run_reach (by decide) h)","+","+/-- Common prefix: frame 1 with the leaves 0 (arena value), 1 (storage), 2 and 3 (destinations), of","+root authorities 0 to 3; `internal` 4 derived from 1 at `Modify` and stored into 0; `newArena 1 4`. -/","+def opsArena : List Op :=","+  [.enter [] [lf, lf, lf, lf], .derive 1 1 .modify, .store 4 0, .newArena 1 4]","+","+/-- The entry registered by `opsArena`. -/","+def arD : Arena := ⟨1, 4, [1], []⟩","+","+/-- **G2** (brief: \"la clause G2 de `store` … n'introduit aucun rejet que `issue` n'a pas\"): the","+authority 5, derived from the root of the destination 2, is stored into the storage leaf 1, so that","+2 is exercisable at `Modify` only through 5, hence through `internal` on 1. The restricted `issue` of","+`[1]` into 2 is `ok`, and so is the kernel `issue`; in the arrival state the block on 1, held by 2,","+and 5, held by 1, block each other, and 2 is no longer exercisable at `Modify`. `split` is `ok`, and","+`store` of the block into 2 is rejected by its clause 5 (O8.5). An indirect cycle, which §88 allows","+(\"des blocages indirects compatibles avec la sûreté peuvent subsister\"). -/","+def opsG2 : List Op := opsArena ++ [.derive 2 2 .modify, .store 5 1]","+","+theorem ce_g2 :","+    Reachable K0 [] (run K0 [] opsG2).s ∧ (run K0 [] opsG2).s.arenas = [arD] ∧","+    IssueR arD [1] 2 (run K0 [] opsG2).s","+      (.ok (issueEffR (run K0 [] opsG2).s arD [1] 2).1 (issueEffR (run K0 [] opsG2).s arD [1] 2).2) ∧","+    IssueAt K0 0 0 [1] 2 (run K0 [] opsG2).s","+      (.ok (arenaSet (issueEff (run K0 [] opsG2).s arD [1] 2).1 0","+        (issueEff (run K0 [] opsG2).s arD [1] 2).2)) ∧","+    ¬ HasRight (issueEffR (run K0 [] opsG2).s arD [1] 2).1 .modify 2 ∧","+    SplitStep K0 4 [[1]] (run K0 [] opsG2).s","+      (.ok ((run K0 [] opsG2).s.addAuth (blockOf (run K0 [] opsG2).s arD [1]))) ∧","+    StoreStep (run K0 [] opsG2).s.A.length 2","+      ((run K0 [] opsG2).s.addAuth (blockOf (run K0 [] opsG2).s arD [1])) .reject :=","+  ⟨reach_run (by decide), by decide, .ok (by decide) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide),","+    .ok (ar := arD) (by decide) (.ok (by decide) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide)), by decide,","+    .ok (by decide), .reject (by decide)⟩","+","+/-- **Init** (sequence accepting more than `issue`): the destination 2 is written (`write3`) before","+the emission. The restricted `issue` of `[1]` into 2 is rejected by clause 2 (§77.2, \"non `Init`\");","+`split` then `store` of the block into 2 are `ok` (O8.2: \"Le fait que ses données soient déjà `Init`","+n'interdit pas à lui seul l'opération\"). -/","+def opsInit : List Op := opsArena ++ [.write 2 [2]]","+","+theorem ce_init :","+    Reachable K0 [] (run K0 [] opsInit).s ∧ (run K0 [] opsInit).s.arenas = [arD] ∧","+    IssueR arD [1] 2 (run K0 [] opsInit).s .reject ∧","+    SplitStep K0 4 [[1]] (run K0 [] opsInit).s","+      (.ok ((run K0 [] opsInit).s.addAuth (blockOf (run K0 [] opsInit).s arD [1]))) ∧","+    StoreStep (run K0 [] opsInit).s.A.length 2","+      ((run K0 [] opsInit).s.addAuth (blockOf (run K0 [] opsInit).s arD [1]))","+      (.ok (storeEff ((run K0 [] opsInit).s.addAuth (blockOf (run K0 [] opsInit).s arD [1]))","+        (run K0 [] opsInit).s.A.length 2)) :=","+  ⟨reach_run (by decide), by decide, .reject (by decide), .ok (by decide), .ok (by decide)⟩","+","+/-- The entry of `opsAvail` once `[1]` is issued (block 5) and the block released. -/","+def arDu : Arena := ⟨1, 4, [], [([1], 5)]⟩","+","+/-- **Availability** (the role of the metadata, §77.4): after the emission of `[1]` into 2 and the","+release of the block, `internal` has its effective `Modify` on 1 again but the region is still","+issued. The restricted `issue` of `[1]` into 3 fails; `split` then `store` into 3 are `ok`. -/","+def opsAvail : List Op := opsArena ++ [.issue 0 0 [1] 2, .release 5]","+","+theorem ce_avail :","+    Reachable K0 [] (run K0 [] opsAvail).s ∧ (run K0 [] opsAvail).s.arenas = [arDu] ∧","+    IssueR arDu [1] 3 (run K0 [] opsAvail).s (.fail (run K0 [] opsAvail).s arDu) ∧","+    SplitStep K0 4 [[1]] (run K0 [] opsAvail).s","+      (.ok ((run K0 [] opsAvail).s.addAuth (blockOf (run K0 [] opsAvail).s arDu [1]))) ∧","+    StoreStep (run K0 [] opsAvail).s.A.length 3","+      ((run K0 [] opsAvail).s.addAuth (blockOf (run K0 [] opsAvail).s arDu [1]))","+      (.ok (storeEff ((run K0 [] opsAvail).s.addAuth (blockOf (run K0 [] opsAvail).s arDu [1]))","+        (run K0 [] opsAvail).s.A.length 3)) :=","+  ⟨reach_run (by decide), by decide, .fail (by decide) (by decide), .ok (by decide),","+    .ok (by decide)⟩","+","+/-- **Empty region**: the restricted `issue` of the empty region is `ok`; no place has an empty","+footprint (`exists_mem_footprint`), so `derive` (O1), which takes a place, cannot produce the block,","+while `split` on one region can (`issue_as_kernel_split`). -/","+theorem ce_empty_region :","+    IssueR arD [] 2 (run K0 [] opsArena).s","+      (.ok (issueEffR (run K0 [] opsArena).s arD [] 2).1 (issueEffR (run K0 [] opsArena).s arD [] 2).2) ∧","+    ∀ q < (run K0 [] opsArena).s.P.length, footprint (run K0 [] opsArena).s.P q ≠ [] := by","+  refine ⟨.ok (by decide) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide), fun q hq he => ?_⟩","+  have hw := (reachable_invariants (KT_dd _ _ _ _ _) (reach_run (os := opsArena) (by decide))).1","+  obtain ⟨l, hl⟩ := exists_mem_footprint hw (_ - q + 1) q (by omega) hq","+  rw [he] at hl; simp at hl","+","+/-- **`internal` stored into the arena value** (`reset`): `internal` 4 was placed into the arena","+value 0 by `store` (O8), which adds it to `D 0`. The restricted `reset` and the kernel `reset` are","+rejected by their clause 3 (§78.3, the kernel reading `internal` within its subtree of origins) for","+as long as 0 is usable; `derive` of `internal` on the storage then `release` are `ok`. -/","+theorem ce_reset_anchor :","+    Reachable K0 [] (run K0 [] opsArena).s ∧ (run K0 [] opsArena).s.arenas = [arD] ∧","+    4 ∈ (run K0 [] opsArena).s.D 0 ∧","+    ¬ ResetPreR (run K0 [] opsArena).s arD ∧ ResetAtStep K0 0 0 (run K0 [] opsArena).s .reject ∧","+    DeriveStep 4 1 .modify (run K0 [] opsArena).s","+      (.ok (deriveEff (run K0 [] opsArena).s 4 1 .modify)) ∧","+    ReleaseStep (run K0 [] opsArena).s.A.length (deriveEff (run K0 [] opsArena).s 4 1 .modify)","+      (.ok (releaseEff (deriveEff (run K0 [] opsArena).s 4 1 .modify) (run K0 [] opsArena).s.A.length)) :=","+  ⟨reach_run (by decide), by decide, by decide, by decide, .reject (by decide), .ok (by decide),","+    .ok (by decide)⟩","+","+/-- An arena value that holds `internal` through `store` blocks the restricted `reset` while it is","+usable. -/","+theorem reset_blocked_by_stored_internal {s : S3} {ar : Arena} {v : Nat} (hv : s.Usable v)","+    (hx : ar.internal ∈ s.D v) : ¬ ResetPreR s ar :=","+  fun h => (h.2.2 v (List.mem_range.2 hv.lt) hv _ hx).1 rfl","+","+/-- Prefix with an allocated storage: frame 1 with the leaves 0 (arena value), 1 (allocator","+value), 2 and 3 (destinations); `alloc` of the storage 4, of parts 5 and 6, owned by 0, of root","+authority 4 held by 0; `newArena 4 4`. `internal` is a root, in no `D`. -/","+def opsAlloc : List Op :=","+  [.enter [] [lf, lf, lf, lf], .write 1 [1],","+    .alloc 1 0 [(none, none, 0), (some 4, none, 0), (some 4, none, 0)], .write 0 [0], .newArena 4 4]","+","+/-- The entry registered by `opsAlloc`. -/","+def arL : Arena := ⟨4, 4, [5, 6], []⟩","+","+/-- **Empty derivation** (`reset`): `split` of `internal` on the empty region creates an active","+derivation of empty footprint. The restricted `reset` and the kernel `reset` are rejected by their","+clause 2 (§78.2); `derive` of `internal` on the storage then `release` are `ok`. -/","+def opsEmpty : List Op := opsAlloc ++ [.split 4 [[]]]","+","+theorem ce_reset_empty :","+    Reachable K0 [] (run K0 [] opsEmpty).s ∧ (run K0 [] opsEmpty).s.arenas = [arL] ∧","+    ¬ ResetPreR (run K0 [] opsEmpty).s arL ∧ ResetAtStep K0 0 0 (run K0 [] opsEmpty).s .reject ∧","+    DeriveStep 4 4 .modify (run K0 [] opsEmpty).s","+      (.ok (deriveEff (run K0 [] opsEmpty).s 4 4 .modify)) ∧","+    ReleaseStep (run K0 [] opsEmpty).s.A.length (deriveEff (run K0 [] opsEmpty).s 4 4 .modify)","+      (.ok (releaseEff (deriveEff (run K0 [] opsEmpty).s 4 4 .modify) (run K0 [] opsEmpty).s.A.length)) :=","+  ⟨reach_run (by decide), by decide, by decide, .reject (by decide), .ok (by decide),","+    .ok (by decide)⟩","+","+/-- Without such a derivation, the same arena is reset by both: the restricted `reset` holds. -/","+theorem reset_alloc_ok : ResetPreR (run K0 [] opsAlloc).s arL := by decide","+","+/-- The state `a6` of case 16 (`Ern.MM03`) is reached. -/","+theorem a6_reachable : Reachable KA [] a6 := by","+  have r0 : Reachable KA [] a0 := .enter (.init (by decide)) (.ok (by decide))","+  have r1 : Reachable KA [] a1 := .write r0 (show Write3Step 1 [1] a0 (.ok a1) from .ok (by decide))","+  have r2 : Reachable KA [] a2 := .alloc r1","+    (show AllocStep KA 1 0 [(none, none, 0), (some 3, none, 0), (some 3, none, 0)] a1 (.ok a2) from","+      .ok (by decide) trivial)","+  have r3 : Reachable KA [] a3 := .newArena (.write r2 (show Write3Step 0 [0] a2 (.ok a2w) from","+    .ok (by decide))) (show NewArenaStep 3 3 a2w (.ok a3) from .ok (by decide))","+  have r4 : Reachable KA [] (deriveEff a3 0 0 .observe) :=","+    .derive r3 (show DeriveStep 0 0 .observe a3 (.ok _) from .ok (by decide))","+  have r5 : Reachable KA [] (deriveEff (deriveEff a3 0 0 .observe) 2 2 .modify) :=","+    .derive r4 (show DeriveStep 2 2 .modify (deriveEff a3 0 0 .observe) (.ok _) from .ok (by decide))","+  exact .enter r5 (show EnterStep [4, 5] [(none, none, 0)] _ (.ok a6) from .ok (by decide))","+","+/-- **`writeShared` branch** (brief, question 1, counterexample to keep): in `a6`, case 16 of the","+kernel, the callee frame has only the `Observe` authority 4 on the arena value 0, whose leaf is","+`SharedMutable` under `KA`, and no block is issued. The kernel `issue` of `[4]` into 6 and the kernel","+`reset` are `ok` through the `writeShared` branch of `MetaRight`; `internal` 3 is exercisable at no","+`Modify` (`MetaRightM` fails), so `derive` of `internal` on the region (place 4) or on the storage","+(place 3), and `split` on the region, are rejected; the restricted operations are rejected too. -/","+theorem ce_writeShared :","+    Reachable KA [] a6 ∧ a6.arenas = [ar7] ∧ ar7.issued = [] ∧","+    IssueAt KA 0 4 [4] 6 a6 (.ok a7) ∧ ResetAtStep KA 0 4 a6 (.ok (resetAtEff a6 0)) ∧","+    ¬ MetaRightM a6 ar7 ∧","+    DeriveStep 3 4 .modify a6 .reject ∧ SplitStep KA 3 [[4]] a6 .reject ∧","+    DeriveStep 3 3 .modify a6 .reject ∧","+    IssueR ar7 [4] 6 a6 .reject ∧ ¬ ResetPreR a6 ar7 :=","+  ⟨a6_reachable, by decide, rfl,","+    .ok (ar := ar7) (by decide) (.ok (by decide) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide)),","+    .ok (by decide), by decide, .reject (by decide), .reject (by decide), .reject (by decide),","+    .reject (by decide), by decide⟩","+","+/-- **Two administrations** (`newArena_as_library`): the unguarded registration of `internal` 4 a","+second time (`NewArenaPreNG` holds, the kernel guard rejects); the emission of `[5]` through entry 0","+is `ok`; the emission of `[5]` through entry 1, whose metadata still has 5 available, is rejected by","+the effective right (§77.5), as is `split` of `internal` on `[5]`: the kernel (I1) rejects the double","+emission, and the metadata of entry 1 no longer separates `fail` from `reject`. -/","+def sTwo : S3 := newArenaEff (run K0 [] opsAlloc).s 4 4","+","+def sTwoIssued : S3 := arenaSet (issueEff sTwo arL [5] 2).1 0 (issueEff sTwo arL [5] 2).2","+","+theorem ce_two_admins :","+    NewArenaPreNG (run K0 [] opsAlloc).s 4 4 ∧ NewArenaStep 4 4 (run K0 [] opsAlloc).s .reject ∧","+    ReachableNG K0 [] sTwoIssued ∧ sTwoIssued.arenas.map (·.available) = [[6], [5, 6]] ∧","+    IssueAt K0 1 0 [5] 3 sTwoIssued .reject ∧ IssueStatic K0 sTwoIssued arL 0 [5] 3 ∧","+    Avail arL [5] ∧ SplitStep K0 4 [[5]] sTwoIssued .reject := by","+  have h1 : NewArenaPreNG (run K0 [] opsAlloc).s 4 4 := by decide","+  have hr : ReachableNG K0 [] sTwo :=","+    .newArenaNG (reachableNG_of_reachable (reach_run (by decide))) h1","+  refine ⟨h1, .reject (by decide), .step hr (.issue (.ok (ar := arL) (by decide)","+    (.ok (by decide) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide)))), by decide,","+    .reject (ar := arL) (by decide) (.noRight (by decide) (by decide) (by decide)), by decide,","+    by decide, .reject (by decide)⟩","+","+/-- **Inexact metadata with the guard**: in a reached state, a frame that can exercise `internal`","+derives from it directly (`derive` of 4 on 5 at `Observe`); the region `[5]` is available in the","+metadata and its emission is rejected by the effective right. The guard does not make the metadata","+exact either. -/","+def opsObs : List Op := opsAlloc ++ [.derive 4 5 .observe]","+","+theorem ce_avail_reject :","+    Reachable K0 [] (run K0 [] opsObs).s ∧ (run K0 [] opsObs).s.arenas = [arL] ∧","+    IssueAt K0 0 0 [5] 2 (run K0 [] opsObs).s .reject ∧ IssueStatic K0 (run K0 [] opsObs).s arL 0 [5] 2 ∧","+    Avail arL [5] :=","+  ⟨reach_run (by decide), by decide,","+    .reject (ar := arL) (by decide) (.noRight (by decide) (by decide) (by decide)), by decide, by decide⟩","+"," end Ern.Derived.Arena"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/Derived/Arena.lean"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"8645d559-2887-4318-89de-c03c952a1d63","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/derivability_0.1","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3d4642ca-4d44-4d3f-95b9-f67a9b52e441","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","git