{"parentUuid":"a89d50d3-5181-4816-ab88-c366da5f550a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgg7jJGRoFbXhRzhLXuJN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017m8WePBtdjesRdCLNr2gmS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/Devlab/ernlang/ern && git status --short; git checkout formal/Ern/.gitkeep 2>/dev/null; git add formal/Ern/Derived/Arena.lean && git commit -q -m \"Derivability Q1: arena operations against kernel sequences\n\nWhy: the derivability brief asks whether issue (O18) and reset (O19) of the\ncandidate Spec 1, with MetaRight restricted to Modify on the arena value, are\nrealised by O1-O16 plus metadata, and whether any safety property depends on\nthe newArena guard (section 56).\n\nWhat: Ern/Derived/Arena.lean defines the restricted issue (IssueR, from the\ncandidate text: option 2 and the anchor of the destination) and reset\n(ResetPreR); proves issue_as_kernel(_split) and reset_as_kernel in both\ndirections with the clauses on which they differ, newArena_as_library (all\nsection 57 invariants on states reached without the guard), and keeps the\ncounterexamples (G2, Init, availability, empty region, stored internal,\nempty derivation, writeShared, two administrations).\n\nProof: lake build of the module succeeds without warnings; axiom sweep of\nits 145 constants finds nothing outside propext and Quot.sound.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git log --oneline -1; echo \"7. Arena.lean counterexamples ce_g2, ce_init, ce_avail, ce_empty_region, ce_reset_anchor, ce_reset_empty, ce_writeShared, ce_two_admins, ce_avail_reject; axcheck 145/84 clean; committed.\" >> /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/d1/log.md","description":"Commit the Arena module"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_cr