{"parentUuid":"5fbb55bb-911b-43d4-a7af-5ffed3296be8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgg7shbrJGzNscdsRRrkJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Writing `Ern/Lib/DataStack.lean`: state, operations (with the §56 guard on both registries), reachability of its kernel part, then the theorems."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8215,"cache_read_input_tokens":386596,"output_tokens":12748,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":7780},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8215,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":12748,"cache_read_input_tokens":386596,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8215,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8215},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"9c79ca69-4ece-4fb3-a027-12666a27d19a","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgg7sh2cuz4hP1a7KpYFh","requestRef":"a9fffdd8-5bad-41dc-8845-f3b514ef8bbe","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"953ed646-7fb9-48f2-b87e-19271de70659","timestamp":"2026-11-03T14:04:18.934Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/derivability_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
{"parentUuid":"953ed646-7fb9-48f2-b87e-19271de70659","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgg7shbrJGzNscdsRRrkJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KBDJCowMT53fDjrUVK6GBH","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/Lib/DataStack.lean","content":"import Ern.Derived.Arena\nimport Ern.MM23\n\n/-!\n# DataStack, a library instance over the kernel (derivability pass 0.1, question 2)\n\nA stack administers a storage through an authority `internal` held by the stack value, as an arena\ndoes (candidate Spec 1 §36, §46), with library metadata: the ordered leaves of the storage, the\ntop, the issued blocks and the live marks. Its operations are built on kernel steps and on the\nderived `issue` and `reset` of question 1 (`Ern.Derived.Arena`):\n\n* `push`: the derived `issue` at the top, `split` of `internal` on the cells then `store` of the\n  block into the destination; `fail` when no room is left;\n* `mark`: a mark (stack, fresh identifier, top), metadata only;\n* `rewind`: the derived `reset` on the cells above the mark, `split` of `internal` on them then\n  `release` of the derived authority; `fail` for a mark that is not live in the stack;\n* `grow`: in place, `release` of the last block, then the derived `issue` of a region of the same\n  base and of larger size into the same destination; `fail` when no room is left.\n\nEvery `ok` step of the library takes kernel steps of `Reachable` only (`dexec_reach`). The theorems\nof the brief are `rewind_rejects_live_above`, `mark_no_aba`, `rewind_keeps_older_marks`,\n`grow_same_base`, `grow_keeps_prefix_init` and `grow_keeps_prefix_bytes` (through the refinement\n`Ern.MM23`, unchanged). The decisions the brief does not settle are listed in the report\n(`formal/reports/Derivability_v0.1.md`, (c) and (f)).\n-/\n\nnamespace Ern.Lib.DataStack\n\nopen Ern.MM03 Ern.HandlePool Ern.MM03.Horrors Ern.Derived.Arena\n\n/-- A block issued by a stack: base and size in the cells of the stack, authority, destination. -/\nstructure Blk where\n  base : Nat\n  size : Nat\n  auth : Nat\n  dst : Nat\nderiving DecidableEq, Repr\n\n/-- A mark (brief: \"(pile, identifiant frais, sommet)\"). -/\nstructure Mark where\n  stack : Nat\n  id : Nat\n  top : Nat\nderiving DecidableEq, Repr\n\n/-- A stack (brief: \"stockage, `internal`, sommet, liste ordonnée des marques vivantes\"); `cells`\nare the ordered leaves of the storage, its footprint at creation; `blocks` the issued blocks,\noldest first. The stack value is the holder of `internal`. -/\nstructure Stack where\n  storage : Nat\n  internal : Nat\n  cells : List Nat\n  top : Nat\n  blocks : List Blk\n  marks : List Mark\nderiving DecidableEq, Repr\n\n/-- State of the library: the kernel state, the stacks (the identity of a stack is its index) and\nthe next fresh mark identifier. -/\nstructure DS where\n  s : S3\n  stacks : List Stack\n  fresh : Nat\n\n/-- Outcome of a library operation; `fail` leaves the state unchanged (§58). -/\ninductive Out where\n  | ok (d : DS)\n  | fail\n  | reject\n\n/-- The `n` cells of the stack from the index `b`. -/\ndef cellsOf (st : Stack) (b n : Nat) : List Nat := (st.cells.drop b).take n\n\n/-- The cells above the mark `m`, those that `rewind m` returns (brief: \"les régions au-dessus de\n`m`\"): the regions issued after `m` lie there. -/\ndef above (st : Stack) (m : Mark) : List Nat := cellsOf st m.top (st.top - m.top)\n\n/-- The stack seen as an administration of its storage, for `MetaRightM` and `blockOf`. -/\ndef Stack.arena (st : Stack) : Arena := ⟨st.storage, st.internal, [], []⟩\n\n/-- No active authority is held by the destination (O8.2, §77.2). -/\ndef NoHeld (s : S3) (dst : Nat) : Prop :=\n  ∀ j ∈ List.range s.A.length, OptP (s.A[j]?) (fun z => z.active = true → z.holder ≠ .place dst) True\n\ninstance (s : S3) (dst : Nat) : Decidable (NoHeld s dst) := by unfold NoHeld; infer_instance\n\n/-- Static preconditions of `push`, checked before the room (§58, §77.4): the stack is live, the\ncurrent frame has exercisable `Modify` on the stack value (`MetaRightM`), and the destination is a\nusable leaf under exercisable `Modify` holding no active authority. -/\ndef PushStatic (s : S3) (st : Stack) (dst : Nat) : Prop :=\n  s.Active st.internal ∧ MetaRightM s st.arena ∧ s.Usable dst ∧ isLeaf s.P dst ∧\n    HasRight s .modify dst ∧ NoHeld s dst\n\ninstance (s : S3) (st : Stack) (dst : Nat) : Decidable (PushStatic s st dst) := by\n  unfold PushStatic; infer_instance\n\n/-- The derived `issue` (question 1, `issue_as_kernel_split`): `split` of `internal` on `r`, then\n`store` of the block into `dst`. -/\ndef IssueSeq (k : K) (s : S3) (st : Stack) (r : List Nat) (dst : Nat) : Prop :=\n  SplitPre k s st.internal [r] ∧ StorePre (s.addAuth (blockOf s st.arena r)) s.A.length dst\n\ninstance (k : K) [∀ r r', Decidable (k.DeclaredDisjoint r r')] (s : S3) (st : Stack)\n    (r : List Nat) (dst : Nat) : Decidable (IssueSeq k s st r dst) := by\n  unfold IssueSeq; infer_instance\n\n/-- Arrival state of the derived `issue`. -/\ndef issueSeqEff (s : S3) (st : Stack) (r : List Nat) (dst : Nat) : S3 :=\n  storeEff (s.addAuth (blockOf s st.arena r)) s.A.length dst\n\n/-- The derived `reset` on the cells above `m` (question 1, `reset_as_kernel`): `split` of\n`internal` on them, then `release` of the derived authority. -/\ndef RewindSeq (k : K) (s : S3) (st : Stack) (m : Mark) : Prop :=\n  SplitPre k s st.internal [above st m] ∧\n    ReleasePre (s.addAuth (blockOf s st.arena (above st m))) s.A.length\n\ninstance (k : K) [∀ r r', Decidable (k.DeclaredDisjoint r r')] (s : S3) (st : Stack) (m : Mark) :\n    Decidable (RewindSeq k s st m) := by\n  unfold RewindSeq; infer_instance\n\n/-- The guard of §56 for `internal` `i`: no live arena and no live stack already uses it. -/\ndef Guard56 (d : DS) (i : Nat) : Prop :=\n  (∀ ar ∈ d.s.arenas, d.s.Active ar.internal → ar.internal ≠ i) ∧\n    ∀ x ∈ d.stacks, d.s.Active x.internal → x.internal ≠ i\n\ninstance (d : DS) (i : Nat) : Decidable (Guard56 d i) := by unfold Guard56; infer_instance\n\nsection Ops\nvariable (k : K) [∀ r r', Decidable (k.DeclaredDisjoint r r')] [DecidablePred k.SharedMutable]\n  [DecidablePred k.Pinned] [DecidablePred k.ExternalDone] [DecidablePred k.Deallocable]\n  [∀ p a, Decidable (k.FreeCompat p a)] [∀ p ls s, Decidable (k.Satisfiable p ls s)]\n\n/-- Creation of a stack on `storage` administered by `internal` (as O17, §76): the preconditions of\n`newArena` and the guard of §56 on both registries, arenas and stacks. -/\ndef newStack (d : DS) (storage i : Nat) : Out :=\n  if NewArenaPreNG d.s storage i ∧ Guard56 d i then\n    .ok { d with stacks := d.stacks ++ [⟨storage, i, footprint d.s.P storage, 0, [], []⟩] }\n  else .reject\n\n/-- `push size dst` on the stack `j` (brief): the derived `issue` of the `size` cells at the top into\n`dst`; `fail` when fewer than `size` cells are left. -/\ndef push (d : DS) (j size dst : Nat) : Out :=\n  match d.stacks[j]? with\n  | none => .reject\n  | some st =>\n    if PushStatic d.s st dst then\n      if st.top + size ≤ st.cells.length then\n        if IssueSeq k d.s st (cellsOf st st.top size) dst then\n          .ok { d with\n            s := issueSeqEff d.s st (cellsOf st st.top size) dst\n            stacks := d.stacks.set j { st with top := st.top + size,\n              blocks := st.blocks ++ [⟨st.top, size, d.s.A.length, dst⟩] } }\n        else .reject\n      else .fail\n    else .reject\n\n/-- `mark` on the stack `j` (brief): `ok`, a mark (stack, fresh identifier, top) appended to the\nlive marks. -/\ndef mark (d : DS) (j : Nat) : Out :=\n  match d.stacks[j]? with\n  | none => .reject\n  | some st => .ok { d with\n      stacks := d.stacks.set j { st with marks := st.marks ++ [⟨j, d.fresh, st.top⟩] }\n      fresh := d.fresh + 1 }\n\n/-- `rewind m` on the stack `j` (brief): `fail` when `m` is not a live mark of the stack; the derived\n`reset` on the cells above `m`, rejected when an active authority derived from `internal` covers\none of them (`rewind_rejects_live_above`); `ok`: the top returns to the top of `m`, the blocks above\n`m` are forgotten, `m` and the later marks are removed, the older marks stay. -/\ndef rewind (d : DS) (j : Nat) (m : Mark) : Out :=\n  match d.stacks[j]? with\n  | none => .reject\n  | some st =>\n    if m ∈ st.marks then\n      if RewindSeq k d.s st m then\n        .ok { d with\n          s := releaseEff (d.s.addAuth (blockOf d.s st.arena (above st m))) d.s.A.length\n          stacks := d.stacks.set j { st with top := m.top,\n            blocks := st.blocks.filter (·.base < m.top),\n            marks := st.marks.takeWhile (· ≠ m) } }\n      else .reject\n    else .fail\n\n/-- `grow b extra` on the stack `j` (brief: in place only): `b` is the authority of the last block,\nat the top, `extra` is positive and `b` can be released; `fail` when fewer than `extra` cells follow\nthe block; otherwise `release` of `b`, then the derived `issue` of the region of the same base and\nof size `size + extra` into the destination of the block. -/\ndef grow (d : DS) (j b extra : Nat) : Out :=\n  match d.stacks[j]? with\n  | none => .reject\n  | some st =>\n    match st.blocks.getLast? with\n    | none => .reject\n    | some x =>\n      if 0 < extra ∧ x.auth = b ∧ x.base + x.size = st.top ∧ ReleasePre d.s b then\n        if x.base + x.size + extra ≤ st.cells.length then\n          if IssueSeq k (releaseEff d.s b) st (cellsOf st x.base (x.size + extra)) x.dst then\n            .ok { d with\n              s := issueSeqEff (releaseEff d.s b) st (cellsOf st x.base (x.size + extra)) x.dst\n              stacks := d.stacks.set j { st with top := x.base + x.size + extra,\n                blocks := st.blocks.dropLast ++ [⟨x.base, x.size + extra, d.s.A.length, x.dst⟩] } }\n          else .reject\n        else .fail\n      else .reject\n\n/-- Operations of a run of the library: a kernel or arena step, or a stack operation. -/\ninductive DOp where\n  | kernel (o : Op)\n  | newStack (storage i : Nat)\n  | push (j size dst : Nat)\n  | mark (j : Nat)\n  | rewind (j : Nat) (m : Mark)\n  | grow (j b extra : Nat)\n\n/-- A step of the library. A kernel `newArena` also consults the registry of the stacks (§56). -/\ndef dexec (d : DS) : DOp → Out\n  | .kernel o =>\n    match o with\n    | .newArena st i =>\n      if ∀ x ∈ d.stacks, d.s.Active x.internal → x.internal ≠ i then\n        match kexec k d.s (.newArena st i) with\n        | some s' => .ok { d with s := s' }\n        | none => .reject\n      else .reject\n    | o =>\n      match kexec k d.s o with\n      | some s' => .ok { d with s := s' }\n      | none => .reject\n  | .newStack st i => newStack k d st i\n  | .push j size dst => push k d j size dst\n  | .mark j => mark d j\n  | .rewind j m => rewind k d j m\n  | .grow j b extra => grow k d j b extra\n\n/-- A run of the library: `some` of the final state when every step is `ok`. -/\ndef drun (d : DS) : List DOp → Option DS\n  | [] => some d\n  | o :: os =>\n    match dexec k d o with\n    | .ok d' => drun d' os\n    | _ => none\n\nend Ops\n\n/-- The initial state of the library. -/\ndef DS.init : DS := ⟨S3.init [], [], 0⟩\n\nend Ern.Lib.DataStack\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8215,"cache_read_input_tokens":386596,"output_tokens":12748,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":7780},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8215,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":12748,"cache_read_input_tokens":386596,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8215,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8215},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01KBDJCowMT53fDjrUVK6GBH":{"file_path":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/Lib/DataStack.lean","content":"import Ern.Derived.Arena\nimport Ern.MM23\n\n/-!\n# DataStack, a library instance over the kernel (derivability pass 0.1, question 2)\n\nA stack administers a storage through an authority `internal` held by the stack value, as an arena\ndoes (candidate Spec 1 §36, §46), with library metadata: the ordered leaves of the storage, the\ntop, the issued blocks and the live marks. Its operations are built on kernel steps and on the\nderived `issue` and `reset` of question 1 (`Ern.Derived.Arena`):\n\n* `push`: the derived `issue` at the top, `split` of `internal` on the cells then `store` of the\n  block into the destination; `fail` when no room is left;\n* `mark`: a mark (stack, fresh identifier, top), metadata only;\n* `rewind`: the derived `reset` on the cells above the mark, `split` of `internal` on them then\n  `release` of the derived authority; `fail` for a mark that is not live in the stack;\n* `grow`: in place, `release` of the last block, then the derived `issue` of a region of the same\n  base and of larger size into the same destination; `fail` when no room is left.\n\nEvery `ok` step of the library takes kernel steps of `Reachable` only (`dexec_reach`). The theorems\nof the brief are `rewind_rejects_live_above`, `mark_no_aba`, `rewind_keeps_older_marks`,\n`grow_same_base`, `grow_keeps_prefix_init` and `grow_keeps_prefix_bytes` (through the refinement\n`Ern.MM23`, unchanged). The decisions the brief does not settle are listed in the report\n(`formal/reports/Derivability_v0.1.md`, (c) and (f)).\n-/\n\nnamespace Ern.Lib.DataStack\n\nopen Ern.MM03 Ern.HandlePool Ern.MM03.Horrors Ern.Derived.Arena\n\n/-- A block issued by a stack: base and size in the cells of the stack, authority, destination. -/\nstructure Blk where\n  base : Nat\n  size : Nat\n  auth : Nat\n  dst : Nat\nderiving DecidableEq, Repr\n\n/-- A mark (brief: \"(pile, identifiant frais, sommet)\"). -/\nstructure Mark where\n  stack : Nat\n  id : Nat\n  top : Nat\nderiving DecidableEq, Repr\n\n/-- A stack (brief: \"stockage, `internal`, sommet, liste ordonnée des marques vivantes\"); `cells`\nare the ordered leaves of the storage, its footprint at creation; `blocks` the issued blocks,\noldest first. The stack value is the holder of `internal`. -/\nstructure Stack where\n  storage : Nat\n  internal : Nat\n  cells : List Nat\n  top : Nat\n  blocks : List Blk\n  marks : List Mark\nderiving DecidableEq, Repr\n\n/-- State of the library: the kernel state, the stacks (the identity of a stack is its index) and\nthe next fresh mark identifier. -/\nstructure DS where\n  s : S3\n  stacks : List Stack\n  fresh : Nat\n\n/-- Outcome of a library operation; `fail` leaves the state unchanged (§58). -/\ninductive Out where\n  | ok (d : DS)\n  | fail\n  | reject\n\n/-- The `n` cells of the stack from the index `b`. -/\ndef cellsOf (st : Stack) (b n : Nat) : List Nat := (st.cells.drop b).take n\n\n/-- The cells above the mark `m`, those that `rewind m` returns (brief: \"les régions au-dessus de\n`m`\"): the regions issued after `m` lie there. -/\ndef above (st : Stack) (m : Mark) : List Nat := cellsOf st m.top (st.top - m.top)\n\n/-- The stack seen as an administration of its storage, for `MetaRightM` and `blockOf`. -/\ndef Stack.arena (st : Stack) : Arena := ⟨st.storage, st.internal, [], []⟩\n\n/-- No active authority is held by the destination (O8.2, §77.2). -/\ndef NoHeld (s : S3) (dst : Nat) : Prop :=\n  ∀ j ∈ List.range s.A.length, OptP (s.A[j]?) (fun z => z.active = true → z.holder ≠ .place dst) True\n\ninstance (s : S3) (dst : Nat) : Decidable (NoHeld s dst) := by unfold NoHeld; infer_instance\n\n/-- Static preconditions of `push`, checked before the room (§58, §77.4): the stack is live, the\ncurrent frame has exercisable `Modify` on the stack value (`MetaRightM`), and the destination is a\nusable leaf under exercisable `Modify` holding no active authority. -/\ndef PushStatic (s : S3) (st : Stack) (dst : Nat) : Prop :=\n  s.Active st.internal ∧ MetaRightM s st.arena ∧ s.Usable dst ∧ isLeaf s.P dst ∧\n    HasRight s .modify dst ∧ NoHeld s dst\n\ninstance (s : S3) (st : Stack) (dst : Nat) : Decidable (PushStatic s st dst) := by\n  unfold PushStatic; infer_instance\n\n/-- The derived `issue` (question 1, `issue_as_kernel_split`): `split` of `internal` on `r`, then\n`store` of the block into `dst`. -/\ndef IssueSeq (k : K) (s : S3) (st : Stack) (r : List Nat) (dst : Nat) : Prop :=\n  SplitPre k s st.internal [r] ∧ StorePre (s.addAuth (blockOf s st.arena r)) s.A.length dst\n\ninstance (k : K) [∀ r r', Decidable (k.DeclaredDisjoint r r')] (s : S3) (st : Stack)\n    (r : List Nat) (dst : Nat) : Decidable (IssueSeq k s st r dst) := by\n  unfold IssueSeq; infer_instance\n\n/-- Arrival state of the derived `issue`. -/\ndef issueSeqEff (s : S3) (st : Stack) (r : List Nat) (dst : Nat) : S3 :=\n  storeEff (s.addAuth (blockOf s st.arena r)) s.A.length dst\n\n/-- The derived `reset` on the cells above `m` (question 1, `reset_as_kernel`): `split` of\n`internal` on them, then `release` of the derived authority. -/\ndef RewindSeq (k : K) (s : S3) (st : Stack) (m : Mark) : Prop :=\n  SplitPre k s st.internal [above st m] ∧\n    ReleasePre (s.addAuth (blockOf s st.arena (above st m))) s.A.length\n\ninstance (k : K) [∀ r r', Decidable (k.DeclaredDisjoint r r')] (s : S3) (st : Stack) (m : Mark) :\n    Decidable (RewindSeq k s st m) := by\n  unfold RewindSeq; infer_instance\n\n/-- The guard of §56 for `internal` `i`: no live arena and no live stack already uses it. -/\ndef Guard56 (d : DS) (i : Nat) : Prop :=\n  (∀ ar ∈ d.s.arenas, d.s.Active ar.internal → ar.internal ≠ i) ∧\n    ∀ x ∈ d.stacks, d.s.Active x.internal → x.internal ≠ i\n\ninstance (d : DS) (i : Nat) : Decidable (Guard56 d i) := by unfold Guard56; infer_instance\n\nsection Ops\nvariable (k : K) [∀ r r', Decidable (k.DeclaredDisjoint r r')] [DecidablePred k.SharedMutable]\n  [DecidablePred k.Pinned] [DecidablePred k.ExternalDone] [DecidablePred k.Deallocable]\n  [∀ p a, Decidable (k.FreeCompat p a)] [∀ p ls s, Decidable (k.Satisfiable p ls s)]\n\n/-- Creation of a stack on `storage` administered by `internal` (as O17, §76): the preconditions of\n`newArena` and the guard of §56 on both registries, arenas and stacks. -/\ndef newStack (d : DS) (storage i : Nat) : Out :=\n  if NewArenaPreNG d.s storage i ∧ Guard56 d i then\n    .ok { d with stacks := d.stacks ++ [⟨storage, i, footprint d.s.P storage, 0, [], []⟩] }\n  else .reject\n\n/-- `push size dst` on the stack `j` (brief): the derived `issue` of the `size` cells at the top into\n`dst`; `fail` when fewer than `size` cells are left. -/\ndef push (d : DS) (j size dst : Nat) : Out :=\n  match d.stacks[j]? with\n  | none => .reject\n  | some st =>\n    if PushStatic d.s st dst then\n      if st.top + size ≤ st.cells.length then\n        if IssueSeq k d.s st (cellsOf st st.top size) dst then\n          .ok { d with\n            s := issueSeqEff d.s st (cellsOf st st.top size) dst\n            stacks := d.stacks.set j { st with top := st.top + size,\n              blocks := st.blocks ++ [⟨st.top, size, d.s.A.length, dst⟩] } }\n        else .reject\n      else .fail\n    else .reject\n\n/-- `mark` on the stack `j` (brief): `ok`, a mark (stack, fresh identifier, top) appended to the\nlive marks. -/\ndef mark (d : DS) (j : Nat) : Out :=\n  match d.stacks[j]? with\n  | none => .reject\n  | some st => .ok { d with\n      stacks := d.stacks.set j { st with marks := st.marks ++ [⟨j, d.fresh, st.top⟩] }\n      fresh := d.fresh + 1 }\n\n/-- `rewind m` on the stack `j` (brief): `fail` when `m` is not a live mark of the stack; the derived\n`reset` on the cells above `m`, rejected when an active authority derived from `internal` covers\none of them (`rewind_rejects_live_above`); `ok`: the top returns to the top of `m`, the blocks above\n`m` are forgotten, `m` and the later marks are removed, the older marks stay. -/\ndef rewind (d : DS) (j : Nat) (m : Mark) : Out :=\n  match d.stacks[j]? with\n  | none => .reject\n  | some st =>\n    if m ∈ st.marks then\n      if RewindSeq k d.s st m then\n        .ok { d with\n          s := releaseEff (d.s.addAuth (blockOf d.s st.arena (above st m))) d.s.A.length\n          stacks := d.stacks.set j { st with top := m.top,\n            blocks := st.blocks.filter (·.base < m.top),\n            marks := st.marks.takeWhile (· ≠ m) } }\n      else .reject\n    else .fail\n\n/-- `grow b extra` on the stack `j` (brief: in place only): `b` is the authority of the last block,\nat the top, `extra` is positive and `b` can be released; `fail` when fewer than `extra` cells follow\nthe block; otherwise `release` of `b`, then the derived `issue` of the region of the same base and\nof size `size + extra` into the destination of the block. -/\ndef grow (d : DS) (j b extra : Nat) : Out :=\n  match d.stacks[j]? with\n  | none => .reject\n  | some st =>\n    match st.blocks.getLast? with\n    | none => .reject\n    | some x =>\n      if 0 < extra ∧ x.auth = b ∧ x.base + x.size = st.top ∧ ReleasePre d.s b then\n        if x.base + x.size + extra ≤ st.cells.length then\n          if IssueSeq k (releaseEff d.s b) st (cellsOf st x.base (x.size + extra)) x.dst then\n            .ok { d with\n              s := issueSeqEff (releaseEff d.s b) st (cellsOf st x.base (x.size + extra)) x.dst\n              stacks := d.stacks.set j { st with top := x.base + x.size + extra,\n                blocks := st.blocks.dropLast ++ [⟨x.base, x.size + extra, d.s.A.length, x.dst⟩] } }\n          else .reject\n        else .fail\n      else .reject\n\n/-- Operations of a run of the library: a kernel or arena step, or a stack operation. -/\ninductive DOp where\n  | kernel (o : Op)\n  | newStack (storage i : Nat)\n  | push (j size dst : Nat)\n  | mark (j : Nat)\n  | rewind (j : Nat) (m : Mark)\n  | grow (j b extra : Nat)\n\n/-- A step of the library. A kernel `newArena` also consults the registry of the stacks (§56). -/\ndef dexec (d : DS) : DOp → Out\n  | .kernel o =>\n    match o with\n    | .newArena st i =>\n      if ∀ x ∈ d.stacks, d.s.Active x.internal → x.internal ≠ i then\n        match kexec k d.s (.newArena st i) with\n        | some s' => .ok { d with s := s' }\n        | none => .reject\n      else .reject\n    | o =>\n      match kexec k d.s o with\n      | some s' => .ok { d with s := s' }\n      | none => .reject\n  | .newStack st i => newStack k d st i\n  | .push j size dst => push k d j size dst\n  | .mark j => mark d j\n  | .rewind j m => rewind k d j m\n  | .grow j b extra => grow k d j b extra\n\n/-- A run of the library: `some` of the final state when every step is `ok`. -/\ndef drun (d : DS) : List DOp → Option DS\n  | [] => some d\n  | o :: os =>\n    match dexec k d o with\n    | .ok d' => drun d' os\n    | _ => none\n\nend Ops\n\n/-- The initial state of the library. -/\ndef DS.init : DS := ⟨S3.init [], [], 0⟩\n\nend Ern.Lib.DataStack\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"9c79ca69-4ece-4fb3-a027-12666a27d19a","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cgg7sh2cuz4hP1a7KpYFh","requestRef":"a9fffdd8-5bad-41dc-8845-f3b514ef8bbe","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"9b3302ae-f189-4917-86b3-8dc50f69f642","timestamp":"2026-11-03T14:04:53.317Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/derivability_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
{"type":"file-history-delta","messageId":"9b3302ae-f189-4917-86b3-8dc50f69f642","snapshotMessageId":"83ab6425-8578-4a53-9a95-0eff28ce9908","trackingPath":"formal/Ern/Lib/DataStack.lean","backup":{"backupFileName":null,"version":1,"backupTime":"2026-11-03T14:04:53.343Z","realParentDir":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/Lib"},"timestamp":"2026-11-03T14:04:53.343Z"}
{"parentUuid":"9b3302ae-f189-4917-86b3-8dc50f69f642","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fcfe6e6f-a978-46ba-b770-f92b3a29d346","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KBDJCowMT53fDjrUVK6GBH","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/Lib/DataStack.lean (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"7e80f60d-8d73-4b7d-842f-768bfe28f3d8","timestamp":"2026-11-03T14:04:53.347Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/Lib/DataStack.lean","content":"import Ern.Derived.Arena\nimport Ern.MM23\n\n/-!\n# DataStack, a library instance over the kernel (derivability pass 0.1, question 2)\n\nA stack administers a storage through an authority `internal` held by the stack value, as an arena\ndoes (candidate Spec 1 §36, §46), with library metadata: the ordered leaves of the storage, the\ntop, the issued blocks and the live marks. Its operations are built on kernel steps and on the\nderived `issue` and `reset` of question 1 (`Ern.Derived.Arena`):\n\n* `push`: the derived `issue` at the top, `split` of `internal` on the cells then `store` of the\n  block into the destination; `fail` when no room is left;\n* `mark`: a mark (stack, fresh identifier, top), metadata only;\n* `rewind`: the derived `reset` on the cells above the mark, `split` of `internal` on them then\n  `release` of the derived authority; `fail` for a mark that is not live in the stack;\n* `grow`: in place, `release` of the last block, then the derived `issue` of a region of the same\n  base and of larger size into the same destination; `fail` when no room is left.\n\nEvery `ok` step of the library takes kernel steps of `Reachable` only (`dexec_reach`). The theorems\nof the brief are `rewind_rejects_live_above`, `mark_no_aba`, `rewind_keeps_older_marks`,\n`grow_same_base`, `grow_keeps_prefix_init` and `grow_keeps_prefix_bytes` (through the refinement\n`Ern.MM23`, unchanged). The decisions the brief does not settle are listed in the report\n(`formal/reports/Derivability_v0.1.md`, (c) and (f)).\n-/\n\nnamespace Ern.Lib.DataStack\n\nopen Ern.MM03 Ern.HandlePool Ern.MM03.Horrors Ern.Derived.Arena\n\n/-- A block issued by a stack: base and size in the cells of the stack, authority, destination. -/\nstructure Blk where\n  base : Nat\n  size : Nat\n  auth : Nat\n  dst : Nat\nderiving DecidableEq, Repr\n\n/-- A mark (brief: \"(pile, identifiant frais, sommet)\"). -/\nstructure Mark where\n  stack : Nat\n  id : Nat\n  top : Nat\nderiving DecidableEq, Repr\n\n/-- A stack (brief: \"stockage, `internal`, sommet, liste ordonnée des marques vivantes\"); `cells`\nare the ordered leaves of the storage, its footprint at creation; `blocks` the issued blocks,\noldest first. The stack value is the holder of `internal`. -/\nstructure Stack where\n  storage : Nat\n  internal : Nat\n  cells : List Nat\n  top : Nat\n  blocks : List Blk\n  marks : List Mark\nderiving DecidableEq, Repr\n\n/-- State of the library: the kernel state, the stacks (the identity of a stack is its index) and\nthe next fresh mark identifier. -/\nstructure DS where\n  s : S3\n  stacks : List Stack\n  fresh : Nat\n\n/-- Outcome of a library operation; `fail` leaves the state unchanged (§58). -/\ninductive Out where\n  | ok (d : DS)\n  | fail\n  | reject\n\n/-- The `n` cells of the stack from the index `b`. -/\ndef cellsOf (st : Stack) (b n : Nat) : List Nat := (st.cells.drop b).take n\n\n/-- The cells above the mark `m`, those that `rewind m` returns (brief: \"les régions au-dessus de\n`m`\"): the regions issued after `m` lie there. -/\ndef above (st : Stack) (m : Mark) : List Nat := cellsOf st m.top (st.top - m.top)\n\n/-- The stack seen as an administration of its storage, for `MetaRightM` and `blockOf`. -/\ndef Stack.arena (st : Stack) : Arena := ⟨st.storage, st.internal, [], []⟩\n\n/-- No active authority is held by the destination (O8.2, §77.2). -/\ndef NoHeld (s : S3) (dst : Nat) : Prop :=\n  ∀ j ∈ List.range s.A.length, OptP (s.A[j]?) (fun z => z.active = true → z.holder ≠ .place dst) True\n\ninstance (s : S3) (dst : Nat) : Decidable (NoHeld s dst) := by unfold NoHeld; infer_instance\n\n/-- Static preconditions of `push`, checked before the room (§58, §77.4): the stack is live, the\ncurrent frame has exercisable `Modify` on the stack value (`MetaRightM`), and the destination is a\nusable leaf under exercisable `Modify` holding no active authority. -/\ndef PushStatic (s : S3) (st : Stack) (dst : Nat) : Prop :=\n  s.Active st.internal ∧ MetaRightM s st.arena ∧ s.Usable dst ∧ isLeaf s.P dst ∧\n    HasRight s .modify dst ∧ NoHeld s dst\n\ninstance (s : S3) (st : Stack) (dst : Nat) : Decidable (PushStatic s st dst) := by\n  unfold PushStatic; infer_instance\n\n/-- The derived `issue` (question 1, `issue_as_kernel_split`): `split` of `internal` on `r`, then\n`store` of the block into `dst`. -/\ndef IssueSeq (k : K) (s : S3) (st : Stack) (r : List Nat) (dst : Nat) : Prop :=\n  SplitPre k s st.internal [r] ∧ StorePre (s.addAuth (blockOf s st.arena r)) s.A.length dst\n\ninstance (k : K) [∀ r r', Decidable (k.DeclaredDisjoint r r')] (s : S3) (st : Stack)\n    (r : List Nat) (dst : Nat) : Decidable (IssueSeq k s st r dst) := by\n  unfold IssueSeq; infer_instance\n\n/-- Arrival state of the derived `issue`. -/\ndef issueSeqEff (s : S3) (st : Stack) (r : List Nat) (dst : Nat) : S3 :=\n  storeEff (s.addAuth (blockOf s st.arena r)) s.A.length dst\n\n/-- The derived `reset` on the cells above `m` (question 1, `reset_as_kernel`): `split` of\n`internal` on them, then `release` of the derived authority. -/\ndef RewindSeq (k : K) (s : S3) (st : Stack) (m : Mark) : Prop :=\n  SplitPre k s st.internal [above st m] ∧\n    ReleasePre (s.addAuth (blockOf s st.arena (above st m))) s.A.length\n\ninstance (k : K) [∀ r r', Decidable (k.DeclaredDisjoint r r')] (s : S3) (st : Stack) (m : Mark) :\n    Decidable (RewindSeq k s st m) := by\n  unfold RewindSeq; infer_instance\n\n/-- The guard of §56 for `internal` `i`: no live arena and no live stack already uses it. -/\ndef Guard56 (d : DS) (i : Nat) : Prop :=\n  (∀ ar ∈ d.s.arenas, d.s.Active ar.internal → ar.internal ≠ i) ∧\n    ∀ x ∈ d.stacks, d.s.Active x.internal → x.internal ≠ i\n\ninstance (d : DS) (i : Nat) : Decidable (Guard56 d i) := by unfold Guard56; infer_instance\n\nsection Ops\nvariable (k : K) [∀ r r', Decidable (k.DeclaredDisjoint r r')] [DecidablePred k.SharedMutable]\n  [DecidablePred k.Pinned] [DecidablePred k.ExternalDone] [DecidablePred k.Deallocable]\n  [∀ p a, Decidable (k.FreeCompat p a)] [∀ p ls s, Decidable (k.Satisfiable p ls s)]\n\n/-- Creation of a stack on `storage` administered by `internal` (as O17, §76): the preconditions of\n`newArena` and the guard of §56 on both registries, arenas and stacks. -/\ndef newStack (d : DS) (storage i : Nat) : Out :=\n  if NewArenaPreNG d.s storage i ∧ Guard56 d i then\n    .ok { d with stacks := d.stacks ++ [⟨storage, i, footprint d.s.P storage, 0, [], []⟩] }\n  else .reject\n\n/-- `push size dst` on the stack `j` (brief): the derived `issue` of the `size` cells at the top into\n`dst`; `fail` when fewer than `size` cells are left. -/\ndef push (d : DS) (j size dst : Nat) : Out :=\n  match d.stacks[j]? with\n  | none => .reject\n  | some st =>\n    if PushStatic d.s st dst then\n      if st.top + size ≤ st.cells.length then\n        if IssueSeq k d.s st (cellsOf st st.top size) dst then\n          .ok { d with\n            s := issueSeqEff d.s st (cellsOf st st.top size) dst\n            stacks := d.stacks.set j { st with top := st.top + size,\n              blocks := st.blocks ++ [⟨st.top, size, d.s.A.length, dst⟩] } }\n        else .reject\n      else .fail\n    else .reject\n\n/-- `mark` on the stack `j` (brief): `ok`, a mark (stack, fresh identifier, top) appended to the\nlive marks. -/\ndef mark (d : DS) (j : Nat) : Out :=\n  match d.stacks[j]? with\n  | none => .reject\n  | some st => .ok { d with\n      stacks := d.stacks.set j { st with marks := st.marks ++ [⟨j, d.fresh, st.top⟩] }\n      fresh := d.fresh + 1 }\n\n/-- `rewind m` on the stack `j` (brief): `fail` when `m` is not a live mark of the stack; the derived\n`reset` on the cells above `m`, rejected when an active authority derived from `internal` covers\none of them (`rewind_rejects_live_above`); `ok`: the top returns to the top of `m`, the blocks above\n`m` are forgotten, `m` and the later marks are removed, the older marks stay. -/\ndef rewind (d : DS) (j : Nat) (m : Mark) : Out :=\n  match d.stacks[j]? with\n  | none => .reject\n  | some st =>\n    if m ∈ st.marks then\n      if RewindSeq k d.s st m then\n        .ok { d with\n          s := releaseEff (d.s.addAuth (blockOf d.s st.arena (above st m))) d.s.A.length\n          stacks := d.stacks.set j { st with top := m.top,\n            blocks := st.blocks.filter (·.base < m.top),\n            marks := st.marks.takeWhile (· ≠ m) } }\n      else .reject\n    else .fail\n\n/-- `grow b extra` on the stack `j` (brief: in place only): `b` is the authority of the last block,\nat the top, `extra` is positive and `b` can be released; `fail` when fewer than `extra` cells follow\nthe block; otherwise `release` of `b`, then the derived `issue` of the region of the same base and\nof size `size + extra` into the destination of the block. -/\ndef grow (d : DS) (j b extra : Nat) : Out :=\n  match d.stacks[j]? with\n  | none => .reject\n  | some st =>\n    match st.blocks.getLast? with\n    | none => .reject\n    | some x =>\n      if 0 < extra ∧ x.auth = b ∧ x.base + x.size = st.top ∧ ReleasePre d.s b then\n        if x.base + x.size + extra ≤ st.cells.length then\n          if IssueSeq k (releaseEff d.s b) st (cellsOf st x.base (x.size + extra)) x.dst then\n            .ok { d with\n              s := issueSeqEff (releaseEff d.s b) st (cellsOf st x.base (x.size + extra)) x.dst\n              stacks := d.stacks.set j { st with top := x.base + x.size + extra,\n                blocks := st.blocks.dropLast ++ [⟨x.base, x.size + extra, d.s.A.length, x.dst⟩] } }\n          else .reject\n        else .fail\n      else .reject\n\n/-- Operations of a run of the library: a kernel or arena step, or a stack operation. -/\ninductive DOp where\n  | kernel (o : Op)\n  | newStack (storage i : Nat)\n  | push (j size dst : Nat)\n  | mark (j : Nat)\n  | rewind (j : Nat) (m : Mark)\n  | grow (j b extra : Nat)\n\n/-- A step of the library. A kernel `newArena` also consults the registry of the stacks (§56). -/\ndef dexec (d : DS) : DOp → Out\n  | .kernel o =>\n    match o with\n    | .newArena st i =>\n      if ∀ x ∈ d.stacks, d.s.Active x.internal → x.internal ≠ i then\n        match kexec k d.s (.newArena st i) with\n        | some s' => .ok { d with s := s' }\n        | none => .reject\n      else .reject\n    | o =>\n      match kexec k d.s o with\n      | some s' => .ok { d with s := s' }\n      | none => .reject\n  | .newStack st i => newStack k d st i\n  | .push j size dst => push k d j size dst\n  | .mark j => mark d j\n  | .rewind j m => rewind k d j m\n  | .grow j b extra => grow k d j b extra\n\n/-- A run of the library: `some` of the final state when every step is `ok`. -/\ndef drun (d : DS) : List DOp → Option DS\n  | [] => some d\n  | o :: os =>\n    match dexec k d o with\n    | .ok d' => drun d' os\n    | _ => none\n\nend Ops\n\n/-- The initial state of the library. -/\ndef DS.init : DS := ⟨S3.init [], [], 0⟩\n\nend Ern.Lib.DataStack\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9b3302ae-f189-4917-86b3-8dc50f69f642","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/derivability_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
