{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-03T14:34:32.229Z","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>w3maal1mh</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01LnhVhnbarCy7qytHmQzAzJ</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/tasks/w3maal1mh.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Dynamic workflow \"Adversarial review of Derived/Arena.lean and Lib/DataStack.lean against the candidate Spec 1 and the brief\" completed</summary>\n<result>[{\"key\":\"issue\",\"review\":{\"summary\":\"Review of question 1, issue (formal/Ern/Derived/Arena.lean: restricted issue, the kernel sequence, issue_to_seq / seq_to_issue / issue_as_kernel_split / issue_as_kernel, ce_g2 / ce_init / ce_avail / ce_empty_region).\\n\\nThe equivalence theorems hold up. `issue_as_kernel_split`, `issue_as_kernel`, `issue_to_seq`, `seq_to_issue` and the four ce_* theorems depend only on propext and Quot.sound. Neither file contains sorry, admit, native_decide, axiom or noncomputable.\\n\\n- **Same arrival state.** It is really stated: `StoreStep … (.ok s')` uses the s' of `IssueR`, and `seq_to_issue` gives `IssueR … (.ok s₂ _)`. `issueEffR_eq` is a structural equality.\\n- **Not vacuous.** On the reached state of opsArena, `IssueR arD [1] 3` is ok and `HasRight` on 3 holds in its arrival state (checked by decide). The hypotheses `hg2`, `hav` and `hni` are each needed: ce_g2, ce_avail and ce_init.\\n- **No further deviation can exist.** The iff is machine-checked, so for reached states with `ar ∈ s.arenas` the only gaps between `IssueR` and split/derive then store are O8.5 (`HasRight` on the arrival state), availability and `Init`. The counterexamples the brief asks for (sequence accepts while `IssueR` rejects with the region available and the destination not `Init`, or `IssueR` accepts with the destination still exercisable while the sequence rejects) cannot exist.\\n- **O8.3.** The owned-storage clause of store is discharged in reached states by `ownedIn_holds` through `RootLive`.\\n- **Kernel versus restricted issue.** The differences are documented: `MetaRightM` (`metaRightM_iff`), destination outside the region (option 2, in the `IssueStaticR` and `issueStaticR_iff` docstrings) and the anchor added to `D dst` (`issueEffR` docstring). The extra `EffAnchorOK` conjunct of `ArrivalR` changes no outcome: `AnchorOrderHeld` on the arrival state already implies it, as the `seq_to_issue` proof uses.\\n\\nThe findings are about `IssueR` against §77 itself, not about the equivalence: one major and two minor, listed below.\",\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"Q1I-1\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"location\":\"formal/Ern/Derived/Arena.lean:97-111 (IssueR, through kernel Avail at Ern/MM03.lean:7104 and the issueEff filter at :7080-7087); docstring of ce_empty_region at :1145-1149\",\"cause\":\"spec\",\"claim\":\"`IssueR` reads availability leaf by leaf: a region counts as available when each of its leaves is in `ar.available`. The candidate text gives `available` as a set of regions and tests whether the region belongs to it. The text does not say which reading is meant, and the two readings give different outcomes. This interpretation is reported neither in the docstrings nor in the report. Under the leaf reading, the overlap clause of §77.5 can never be reached in a reached state, a region that partly overlaps an active emission gets `fail` where the region-set reading gives `reject`, and the empty region is always available.\",\"evidence\":\"Spec text. §46 types the field as `available: Set&lt;Region&gt;`; §77.4 says \\\"Si les conditions statiques tiennent mais que `region` n'appartient plus à `available`, l'opération produit `fail`\\\". §77.5 sits after the availability check and says \\\"Si la région est disponible, le mode effectif de `internal` … à défaut, l'issue est `reject`. La région ne peut chevaucher une région émise encore active.\\\" The effect says \\\"La région quitte `available`\\\".\\n\\nFormal side: kernel `Avail ar region := ∀ l ∈ region, l ∈ ar.available`. The `IssueR` docstring only says \\\"`fail` … when the region is not available (§77.4)\\\".\\n\\nCheck 1 (scratch b.lean, decide): reached state `run K0 [] (opsAlloc ++ [.issue 0 0 [5] 2])`. `reach_run` holds and `arenas = [⟨4, 4, [6], [([5], 5)]⟩]`. Block 5 is `([5], active, origin 4)`. The following typecheck: `IssueR arQ [5, 6] 3 s (.fail s arQ)` and `¬ IssueRight s arQ [5, 6]`. Under a region-set reading where issuing [5] removes only the region [5], [5,6] is still available and §77.5 gives `reject`. Under the leaf reading, ArenaInv clause 4 makes every region that overlaps an active emission unavailable, so the overlap sentence of §77.5 never applies.\\n\\nCheck 2 (scratch a.lean, decide): state `run K0 [] (opsArena ++ [.issue 0 0 [1] 2])`, whose arena is `⟨1, 4, [], [([1], 5)]⟩` (available empty). `IssueR arIss [] 3 s (.ok …)` typechecks and `Avail arIss [] ` holds, so the empty region is available although `available = []`. ce_empty_region states that this `ok` is acceptable without flagging the reading. The report's question section (f) does not list it.\"},{\"id\":\"Q1I-2\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"formal/Ern/Derived/Arena.lean:51-63 (IssueStaticR docstring and definition) and :97-111 (IssueR)\",\"cause\":\"coverage\",\"claim\":\"The first sentence of §77.1, \\\"L'entrée `arena` existe\\\", is not a clause of `IssueStaticR` or `IssueR`. Nothing writes the new metadata `ar'` back into the state either. Nothing ties `IssueR` to a registered entry: it accepts any `Arena` value, and its arrival state keeps the stale entry in `s.arenas`. The equivalence theorems are unaffected, since they all assume `har : ar ∈ s.arenas`. There is no restricted counterpart of the kernel's `IssueAt`.\",\"evidence\":\"Spec §77.1: \\\"L'entrée `arena` existe et est vivante ; `internal` est active.\\\" The `IssueStaticR` docstring reads clause 1 as \\\"restricted metadata right and `internal` active\\\" only.\\n\\nScratch a.lean, decide:\\n- `arFake := ⟨1, 4, [1], [([7], 9)]⟩`. `arFake ∉ (run K0 [] opsArena).s.arenas` holds, yet `IssueR arFake [1] 3 (run K0 [] opsArena).s (.ok …)` typechecks.\\n- On `run K0 [] opsAvail`, the registered entry fails (ce_avail), but the made-up value `⟨1, 4, [1], []⟩` gives `IssueR … (.ok …)`.\\n- `#eval (issueEffR (run K0 [] opsArena).s arD [1] 3).1.arenas.map (fun a =&gt; (a.available, a.issued))` prints `[([1], [])]`: the arrival state still lists [1] as available and nothing as issued.\"},{\"id\":\"Q1I-3\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"formal/Ern/Derived/Arena.lean:51-56 (IssueStaticR docstring) and :57-63\",\"cause\":\"spec\",\"claim\":\"The static part of §77.3 (\\\"restrictions statiques de validité et de non-échappement applicables à la destination\\\") has no counterpart in the formalization. The docstring says these restrictions \\\"are those of the kernel (`IssueStatic`, `issueStaticR_iff`)\\\", but `IssueStatic` has no conjunct for clause 3: its eight conjuncts encode §77.1 and §77.2 only. The text does not say what these restrictions are, and reading them as empty is an interpretation that is not flagged as one. This matters for classification: any such restriction is checked before `fail`, so leaving it empty can turn a static `reject` into `fail`. Under the kernel's `NoEscape`, which constrains only root anchors, the block (origin `internal`) is trivially non-escaping, so this may change no outcome. That is not stated or proven.\",\"evidence\":\"Spec §77.3: \\\"Les restrictions **statiques** de validité et de non-échappement applicables à la destination sont satisfaites. Le contrôle de `AnchorOrder` qui dépend de la nouvelle ancre est effectué sur **l'état d'arrivée simulé** …\\\".\\n\\nKernel `IssueStatic` (Ern/MM03.lean:7091-7097) is `MetaRight ∧ Active internal ∧ region ⊆ afp internal ∧ Usable dst ∧ HasRight dst ∧ dst not Init ∧ isLeaf dst ∧ dst holds no active authority`. Its docstring cites only \\\"MM-03.3 §6; A10 … J1\\\".\\n\\n`grep -n 'NoEscape' Ern/MM03.lean` finds it used in transfer (:1251, :1274) and depend (:1308), never in issue. The report does not list this reading among its questions.\"}]},\"verdicts\":[{\"id\":\"Q1I-1\",\"real\":true,\"severity\":\"major\",\"reason\":\"Confirmed. `IssueR` decides `fail` with the kernel's `Avail ar region := ∀ l ∈ region, l ∈ ar.available`. That is a leaf-by-leaf reading, possible only because the kernel `Arena.available` is a `List Nat` of leaves. The candidate text types the field as `Set&lt;Region&gt;` and tests whether the region belongs to it, so the text is open to more than one reading. §78 also says \\\"la totalité des régions du\n... (truncated 48887 chars, full result in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/tasks/w3maal1mh.output)</result>\n<diagnostics>Per-agent results: /Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/subagents/workflows/wf_c3e42f5b-0d8/journal.jsonl — one {\"type\":\"result\",...} line per completed agent with its full return value.\nIf the result above is empty or unexpected, Read this file BEFORE diagnosing — do not assume agents returned non-empty results.\nTo re-run with edited post-processing: Workflow({scriptPath: '/Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/workflows/scripts/derivability-review-wf_c3e42f5b-0d8.js', resumeFromRunId: 'wf_c3e42f5b-0d8'}) — agents whose (prompt, opts) are unchanged replay from cache.</diagnostics>\n<usage><agent_count>8</agent_count><agents_done>8</agents_done><agents_error>0</agents_error><agents_skipped>0</agents_skipped><agents_empty_result>0</agents_empty_result><subagent_tokens>1301739</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>173</tool_uses><duration_ms>1129148</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
