{"parentUuid":"2cd51b08-355e-4714-8ad8-aabfbea58ff4","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"04d7bf8f-72b3-4331-acc7-9edddd89b24a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017uUNN5wnhggs3qAEkkgadc","type":"tool_result","content":"/-! ## Restricted `issue` (candidate Spec 1 §77) -/\n\n/-- Static preconditions of the restricted `issue` (candidate Spec 1 §77, clauses 1 and 2, with\n`MetaRightM`): clause 1, restricted metadata right and `internal` active; clause 2, the region\nwithin the administered storage, the destination a usable leaf, under exercisable `Modify`, not\n`Init`, holding no active authority, and not in the region (\"Prévention locale de l'auto-blocage\",\n§88). The static restrictions of clause 3 are those of the kernel (`IssueStatic`,\n`issueStaticR_iff`); its `AnchorOrder` check is on the arrival state (`ArrivalR`). -/\n  unfold ArrivalR; infer_instance\n\n/-- The restricted `issue` as a relation (candidate Spec 1 §77; §58): `reject` when a static\nprecondition fails; `fail`, the state unchanged, when the region is not available (§77.4);\n`reject` when `internal` lacks effective `Modify` on the region (§77.5) or an arrival check fails\n(§77.3, §77.6); `ok` otherwise. The disjointness of §77.5 from the active emissions is not\nrestated: it follows from the effective right (`issue_disjoint_redundant`, A11). -/\ninductive IssueR (ar : Arena) (region : List Nat) (dst : Nat) (s : S3) : IOutcome → Prop where\n  | ok : IssueStaticR s ar region dst → Avail ar region → IssueRight s ar region →\n      ArrivalR s ar region dst →\n      IssueR ar region dst s (.ok (issueEffR s ar region dst).1 (issueEffR s ar region dst).2)\n1160-  ⟨reach_run (by decide), by decide, .fail (by decide) (by decide), .ok (by decide),\n1161-    .ok (by decide)⟩\n1162-\n1163-/-- **Empty region**: the restricted `issue` of the empty region is `ok`; no place has an empty\n1164-footprint (`exists_mem_footprint`), so `derive` (O1), which takes a place, cannot produce the block,\n1165-while `split` on one region can (`issue_as_kernel_split`). -/\n1166:theorem ce_empty_region :","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4ae23298-a9d9-49c4-9e7d-c28c34678de8","timestamp":"2026-11-03T14:36:55.786Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"/-! ## Restricted `issue` (candidate Spec 1 §77) -/\n\n/-- Static preconditions of the restricted `issue` (candidate Spec 1 §77, clauses 1 and 2, with\n`MetaRightM`): clause 1, restricted metadata right and `internal` active; clause 2, the region\nwithin the administered storage, the destination a usable leaf, under exercisable `Modify`, not\n`Init`, holding no active authority, and not in the region (\"Prévention locale de l'auto-blocage\",\n§88). The static restrictions of clause 3 are those of the kernel (`IssueStatic`,\n`issueStaticR_iff`); its `AnchorOrder` check is on the arrival state (`ArrivalR`). -/\n  unfold ArrivalR; infer_instance\n\n/-- The restricted `issue` as a relation (candidate Spec 1 §77; §58): `reject` when a static\nprecondition fails; `fail`, the state unchanged, when the region is not available (§77.4);\n`reject` when `internal` lacks effective `Modify` on the region (§77.5) or an arrival check fails\n(§77.3, §77.6); `ok` otherwise. The disjointness of §77.5 from the active emissions is not\nrestated: it follows from the effective right (`issue_disjoint_redundant`, A11). -/\ninductive IssueR (ar : Arena) (region : List Nat) (dst : Nat) (s : S3) : IOutcome → Prop where\n  | ok : IssueStaticR s ar region dst → Avail ar region → IssueRight s ar region →\n      ArrivalR s ar region dst →\n      IssueR ar region dst s (.ok (issueEffR s ar region dst).1 (issueEffR s ar region dst).2)\n1160-  ⟨reach_run (by decide), by decide, .fail (by decide) (by decide), .ok (by decide),\n1161-    .ok (by decide)⟩\n1162-\n1163-/-- **Empty region**: the restricted `issue` of the empty region is `ok`; no place has an empty\n1164-footprint (`exists_mem_footprint`), so `derive` (O1), which takes a place, cannot produce the block,\n1165-while `split` on one region can (`issue_as_kernel_split`). -/\n1166:theorem ce_empty_region :","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"bfe838d9-2f39-4d1a-ac19-1405c8e992cb","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/derivability_0.1","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2cd51b08-355e-4714-8ad8-aabfbea58ff4","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/derivability_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","id":"192e2be3-fe4d-4230-b709-4fde4ae414a8","timestamp":"2026-11-03T14:36:55.824Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"d1aa6c2254c890b11835611a868b353c28b0e75545aafd34fb8d8155d691dfb1","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"xhigh"}},"base":"92b4321f-9c6d-49e8-8281-139f5d0b155d","keep":230,"tail":["c84330635e30781c5d94e7271a1ea995318249d30dde8bdcf2d24cc9d529b0a2","3b0223d6a1d978a6af6051a05a54484ada357e9a9279f3fdba044dd7c89a95cf"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",231,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"043875494de783fac9a3c42fd30ddfe00ba6f8faa81263db89c70ebfdb02abd3"}
{"parentUuid":"4ae23298-a9d9-49c4-9e7d-c28c34678de8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggAStrRKYfchjRMFK8nx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TLdERoJ19MEVMnsbZBeiy3","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='Ern/Derived/Arena.lean'\ns=open(p).read()\nreps=[\n(\"\"\"`MetaRightM`): clause 1, restricted metadata right and `internal` active; clause 2, the region\"\"\",\n\"\"\"`MetaRightM`): clause 1, restricted metadata right and `internal` active (the existence of the\nentry is the lookup of `IssueAtR`; the theorems take an entry `ar ∈ s.arenas`); clause 2, the region\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"(§77.3, §77.6); `ok` otherwise. The disjointness of §77.5 from the active emissions is not\nrestated: it follows from the effective right (`issue_disjoint_redundant`, A11). -/\"\"\",\n\"\"\"(§77.3, §77.6); `ok` otherwise. The disjointness of §77.5 from the active emissions is not\nrestated: it follows from the effective right (`issue_disjoint_redundant`, A11).\n\nAvailability is the kernel `Avail`, read leaf by leaf: the kernel keeps `available` as a list of\nleaves, where §46 types it `Set<Region>` and §77.4 tests whether the region belongs to it. The text\ndoes not settle which reading holds, and the readings classify differently: under the leaf reading a\nregion that partly overlaps an active emission fails (§77.4) instead of reaching §77.5, and the\nempty region is always available (`ce_avail_leaf`; report, (f)). -/\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"/-- **Empty region**: the restricted `issue` of the empty region is `ok`; no place has an empty\nfootprint (`exists_mem_footprint`), so `derive` (O1), which takes a place, cannot produce the block,\nwhile `split` on one region can (`issue_as_kernel_split`). -/\"\"\",\n\"\"\"/-- **Empty region**: the restricted `issue` of the empty region is `ok` (the empty region is\navailable under the leaf reading of `available`, `ce_avail_leaf`); no place has an empty footprint\n(`exists_mem_footprint`), so `derive` (O1), which takes a place, cannot produce the block, while\n`split` on one region can (`issue_as_kernel_split`). -/\"\"\"),\n]\nfor a,b in reps:\n    assert s.count(a)==1,a[:80]; s=s.replace(a,b)\n# IssueAtR after issueR_reject_iff (before \"## The kernel sequence for `issue`\")\nanchor=\"/-! ## The kernel sequence for `issue` -/\"\nassert s.count(anchor)==1\nins='''/-- The restricted `issue` on the entry `i` of the state (§77.1, \"L'entrée `arena` existe\"): the\n`IssueR` of the recorded entry, whose new metadata is written back, as the kernel `IssueAt`; a\nmissing entry is rejected. -/\ninductive IssueAtR (i : Nat) (region : List Nat) (dst : Nat) (s : S3) : AOutcome → Prop where\n  | ok {ar : Arena} {s' : S3} {ar' : Arena} : s.arenas[i]? = some ar →\n      IssueR ar region dst s (.ok s' ar') → IssueAtR i region dst s (.ok (arenaSet s' i ar'))\n  | fail {ar : Arena} {s' : S3} {ar' : Arena} : s.arenas[i]? = some ar →\n      IssueR ar region dst s (.fail s' ar') → IssueAtR i region dst s (.fail s)\n  | reject {ar : Arena} : s.arenas[i]? = some ar → IssueR ar region dst s .reject →\n      IssueAtR i region dst s .reject\n  | none : s.arenas[i]? = none → IssueAtR i region dst s .reject\n\n'''\ns=s.replace(anchor, ins+anchor)\n# ce_avail_leaf after ce_empty_region theorem: find the reset anchor CE docstring start\nanchor2=\"/-- **`internal` stored into the arena value** (`reset`)\"\nassert s.count(anchor2)==1\nce='''/-- The entry of `opsAlloc` once `[5]` is issued into 2 (block 5). -/\ndef arLi : Arena := ⟨4, 4, [6], [([5], 5)]⟩\n\n/-- **Leaf reading of `available`** (Q1I-1 of the review): after the emission of `[5]` (block 5,\nactive), the region `[5, 6]` partly overlaps the active emission. With `available` read leaf by leaf\n(the kernel `Avail`), it is unavailable and the restricted `issue` fails (§77.4); with `available`\na set of regions from which only `[5]` left, `[5, 6]` would be available and §77.5 would reject it,\n`internal` lacking the effective right on 5. The empty region is available though `available`\nholds no region of it. -/\ndef opsLeaf : List Op := opsAlloc ++ [.issue 0 0 [5] 2]\n\ntheorem ce_avail_leaf :\n    Reachable K0 [] (run K0 [] opsLeaf).s ∧ (run K0 [] opsLeaf).s.arenas = [arLi] ∧\n    IssueR arLi [5, 6] 3 (run K0 [] opsLeaf).s (.fail (run K0 [] opsLeaf).s arLi) ∧\n    ¬ IssueRight (run K0 [] opsLeaf).s arLi [5, 6] ∧ Avail arLi [] :=\n  ⟨reach_run (by decide), by decide, .fail (by decide) (by decide), by decide, by decide⟩\n\n'''\ns=s.replace(anchor2, ce+anchor2)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\n~/.elan/bin/lake env lean Ern/Derived/Arena.lean 2>&1 | head -30","description":"Add IssueAtR, leaf-availability docs and counterexample","timeout":900000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1078,"cache_read_input_tokens":556478,"output_tokens":2094,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1078,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2094,"cache_read_input_tokens":556478,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1078,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1078},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01TLdERoJ19MEVMnsbZBeiy3":{"command":"cd ~/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='Ern/Derived/Arena.lean'\ns=open(p).read()\nreps=[\n(\"\"\"`MetaRightM`): clause 1, restricted metadata right and `internal` active; clause 2, the region\"\"\",\n\"\"\"`MetaRightM`): clause 1, restricted metadata right and `internal` active (the existence of the\nentry is the lookup of `IssueAtR`; the theorems take an entry `ar ∈ s.arenas`); clause 2, the region\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"(§77.3, §77.6); `ok` otherwise. The disjointness of §77.5 from the active emissions is not\nrestated: it follows from the effective right (`issue_disjoint_redundant`, A11). -/\"\"\",\n\"\"\"(§77.3, §77.6); `ok` otherwise. The disjointness of §77.5 from the active emissions is not\nrestated: it follows from the effective right (`issue_disjoint_redundant`, A11).\n\nAvailability is the kernel `Avail`, read leaf by leaf: the kernel keeps `available` as a list of\nleaves, where §46 types it `Set<Region>` and §77.4 tests whether the region belongs to it. The text\ndoes not settle which reading holds, and the readings classify differently: under the leaf reading a\nregion that partly overlaps an active emission fails (§77.4) instead of reaching §77.5, and the\nempty region is always available (`ce_avail_leaf`; report, (f)). -/\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"/-- **Empty region**: the restricted `issue` of the empty region is `ok`; no place has an empty\nfootprint (`exists_mem_footprint`), so `derive` (O1), which takes a place, cannot produce the block,\nwhile `split` on one region can (`issue_as_kernel_split`). -/\"\"\",\n\"\"\"/-- **Empty region**: the restricted `issue` of the empty region is `ok` (the empty region is\navailable under the leaf reading of `available`, `ce_avail_leaf`); no place has an empty footprint\n(`exists_mem_footprint`), so `derive` (O1), which takes a place, cannot produce the block, while\n`split` on one region can (`issue_as_kernel_split`). -/\"\"\"),\n]\nfor a,b in reps:\n    assert s.count(a)==1,a[:80]; s=s.replace(a,b)\n# IssueAtR after issueR_reject_iff (before \"## The kernel sequence for `issue`\")\nanchor=\"/-! ## The kernel sequence for `issue` -/\"\nassert s.count(anchor)==1\nins='''/-- The restricted `issue` on the entry `i` of the state (§77.1, \"L'entrée `arena` existe\"): the\n`IssueR` of the recorded entry, whose new metadata is written back, as the kernel `IssueAt`; a\nmissing entry is rejected. -/\ninductive IssueAtR (i : Nat) (region : List Nat) (dst : Nat) (s : S3) : AOutcome → Prop where\n  | ok {ar : Arena} {s' : S3} {ar' : Arena} : s.arenas[i]? = some ar →\n      IssueR ar region dst s (.ok s' ar') → IssueAtR i region dst s (.ok (arenaSet s' i ar'))\n  | fail {ar : Arena} {s' : S3} {ar' : Arena} : s.arenas[i]? = some ar →\n      IssueR ar region dst s (.fail s' ar') → IssueAtR i region dst s (.fail s)\n  | reject {ar : Arena} : s.arenas[i]? = some ar → IssueR ar region dst s .reject →\n      IssueAtR i region dst s .reject\n  | none : s.arenas[i]? = none → IssueAtR i region dst s .reject\n\n'''\ns=s.replace(anchor, ins+anchor)\n# ce_avail_leaf after ce_empty_region theorem: find the reset anchor CE docstring start\nanchor2=\"/-- **`internal` stored into the arena value** (`reset`)\"\nassert s.count(anchor2)==1\nce='''/-- The entry of `opsAlloc` once `[5]` is issued into 2 (block 5). -/\ndef arLi : Arena := ⟨4, 4, [6], [([5], 5)]⟩\n\n/-- **Leaf reading of `available`** (Q1I-1 of the review): after the emission of `[5]` (block 5,\nactive), the region `[5, 6]` partly overlaps the active emission. With `available` read leaf by leaf\n(the kernel `Avail`), it is unavailable and the restricted `issue` fails (§77.4); with `available`\na set of regions from which only `[5]` left, `[5, 6]` would be available and §77.5 would reject it,\n`internal` lacking the effective right on 5. The empty region is available though `available`\nholds no region of it. -/\ndef opsLeaf : List Op := opsAlloc ++ [.issue 0 0 [5] 2]\n\ntheorem ce_avail_leaf :\n    Reachable K0 [] (run K0 [] opsLeaf).s ∧ (run K0 [] opsLeaf).s.arenas = [arLi] ∧\n    IssueR arLi [5, 6] 3 (run K0 [] opsLeaf).s (.fail (run K0 [] opsLeaf).s arLi) ∧\n    ¬ IssueRight (run K0 [] opsLeaf).s arLi [5, 6] ∧ Avail arLi [] :=\n  ⟨reach_run (by decide), by decide, .fail (by decide) (by decide), by decide, by decide⟩\n\n'''\ns=s.replace(anchor2, ce+anchor2)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\n~/.elan/bin/lake env lean Ern/Derived/Arena.lean 2>&1 | head -30","description":"Add IssueAtR, leaf-availability docs and counterexample","timeout":900000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"41ff3033-29c4-47ba-a6aa-a9a03f3afe4c","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CggAStYq1jAoEDysZL3YH","requestRef":"192e2be3-fe4d-4230-b709-4fde4ae414a8","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c64f03ea-3797-4e35-9038-30ccf5135f80","timestamp":"2026-11-03T14:37:11.434Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/derivability_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
