{"parentUuid":"a22d0885-a15a-4056-81ed-d18b51116e27","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggAxYrUyJ4S5Ts3kQav7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01D1ZyseTfD5sWfmdSChxVAY","name":"Workflow","input":{"script":"export const meta = {\n  name: 'derivability-followup',\n  description: 'Narrow adversarial check of the review fixes (commit b22aef9) and of the French report',\n  phases: [{ title: 'Review' }, { title: 'Verify' }],\n}\n\nconst SP = '/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/d1/followup'\nconst COMMON = `\nYou are an adversarial, read-only reviewer of a Lean 4 formalization (Lean v4.35, no Mathlib). Repository /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern, Lake project formal/, branch formal/derivability_0.1. Do NOT modify repository files. Scratch files only under ${SP}/<your-label>/ (create it); check claims with: cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && ~/.elan/bin/lake env lean <scratch.lean> (modules are built; import Ern.Lib.DataStack or Ern.Derived.Arena; #eval and decide work on concrete states, see the cases at the end of each module for how runs are built).\nNormative text: /Users/guygouri/Downloads/ERN_Spec1_Memory_Model_specification_normative_candidate_corrigee.md (French candidate Spec 1; §46, §58, §77 O18, §78 O19 matter here). Rules: /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/AGENTS.md (Review section). The kernel Ern/MM03.lean is unchanged.\nThe last commit b22aef9 fixed review findings: (DS-1) MarksWF now includes Nodup of marks, mark_no_aba covers every mark removed by rewind (m :: post), new rewind_removes; (F1) ResetPreR includes liveness, theorems lost the hact hypothesis, new ResetAtPreR; (Q1I-2) new IssueAtR; (Q1I-1) availability leaf reading documented, new ce_avail_leaf; (DS-5, DS-4) push now checks the static clauses of the restricted issue (IssueStaticR: not Init, dst outside the requested cells, MetaRightM, ...) before fail; (Q2-GROW-ORDER) grow checks Active internal and MetaRightM before fail; (wording) grow_same_base now on the arrival state; docstrings corrected; new cases case_rewind_reading, case_static_before_fail. See: git -C /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern show b22aef9 --stat and git diff 59c276f b22aef9 -- formal/Ern.\nReport only findings with concrete evidence (spec quote, reproduced run output, command output). No evidence, no finding. Do not ask for additions beyond the task. Severity blocking | major | minor; cause formalization | coverage | spec.\n`\nconst FINDINGS = { type: 'object', properties: { findings: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', properties: { id: { type: 'string' }, severity: { type: 'string', enum: ['blocking', 'major', 'minor'] }, location: { type: 'string' }, cause: { type: 'string', enum: ['formalization', 'coverage', 'spec'] }, claim: { type: 'string' }, evidence: { type: 'string' } }, required: ['id', 'severity', 'location', 'cause', 'claim', 'evidence'] } }, summary: { type: 'string' } }, required: ['findings', 'summary'] }\nconst VERDICTS = { type: 'object', properties: { verdicts: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', properties: { id: { type: 'string' }, real: { type: 'boolean' }, severity: { type: 'string', enum: ['blocking', 'major', 'minor'] }, reason: { type: 'string' }, evidence: { type: 'string' } }, required: ['id', 'real', 'severity', 'reason', 'evidence'] } } }, required: ['verdicts'] }\n\nconst DIMS = [\n  { key: 'datastack-fixes', prompt: `Focus: formal/Ern/Lib/DataStack.lean changes. (1) mark_no_aba and rewind_removes: is the statement now what the brief asks (\"une marque retirée ne redevient jamais valide, même si le sommet revient à la même position\") for every removed mark; is MarksWF satisfiable, preserved by every DOp (dexec_marksWF), established for library runs (drun_init_marksWF); try to break it with runs. (2) push: the docstring claims that this realisation through kernel steps \"differs from the restricted issue only by clause 5 of store (O8.5)\". Check whether this claim is proven or only argued, and whether it is true: compare push's conditions (PushStatic, room, IssueSeq) with IssueR's (IssueStaticR, Avail, IssueRight, ArrivalR) for the stack seen as an arena; find a run where push and the restricted issue would disagree for a reason other than O8.5 (e.g. availability metadata vs room, region inclusion in the storage, MetaRightM). (3) grow: static clauses before fail now include MetaRightM; grow_same_base's new conjuncts. (4) The two new cases are non-vacuous and show what their docstrings say. (5) Run lake build (no warnings), the forbidden-word grep from the repo root (grep -rnE '\\\\b(sorry|admit|native_decide)\\\\b|^\\\\s*axiom\\\\b' --include='*.lean' --exclude-dir=.lake .), and #print axioms of mark_no_aba, rewind_removes, grow_same_base, case_static_before_fail, case_rewind_reading.` },\n  { key: 'arena-fixes', prompt: `Focus: formal/Ern/Derived/Arena.lean changes. (1) ResetPreR now includes s.Active ar.internal; check reset_to_seq, seq_to_reset, reset_as_kernel (no hact) are still the brief's statements and not weakened, and that ResetAtPreR/resetAtPreR_iff match §78.1 and the kernel ResetAtPre. (2) IssueAtR mirrors the kernel IssueAt and §77.1. (3) ce_avail_leaf: reached, shows what its docstring says (leaf reading gives fail where a region-set reading would give reject through §77.5); are the IssueR and ce_empty_region docstrings accurate. (4) Any theorem docstring that still mentions a removed hypothesis or contradicts its statement. (5) #print axioms of reset_as_kernel, issue_as_kernel_split, ce_avail_leaf, newArena_as_library.` },\n  { key: 'report', prompt: `Focus: the French report formal/reports/Derivability_v0.1.md against the code of both modules (formal/Ern/Derived/Arena.lean, formal/Ern/Lib/DataStack.lean). The brief requires sections: (a) status of issue_as_kernel, reset_as_kernel, newArena_as_library; (b) the writeShared counterexample; (c) deviations in either direction; (d) status of the DataStack theorems; (e) amendments of Spec 1 text that follow from the results, clause by clause; (f) questions. Check: every theorem or definition name cited exists and says what the report says (open the statements); counts of constants/theorems (verify with an axiom sweep: write a scratch file importing both modules that iterates env.constants for modules Ern.Derived.Arena and Ern.Lib.DataStack and counts constants and theorems, see /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/d1/axcheck2.lean, and check no constant depends on axioms beyond propext and Quot.sound); cross references between sections ((e) n, (f) n, écart n) point to the right item; spec quotes in the report are verbatim from the spec file; no claim stronger than what is proven; amendments in (e) follow from results and present alternatives instead of choosing where the result does not decide.` },\n]\n\nphase('Review')\nconst results = await pipeline(\n  DIMS,\n  d => agent(COMMON + '\\n' + d.prompt + '\\nReturn your findings.', { label: `review:${d.key}`, phase: 'Review', schema: FINDINGS }),\n  (rev, d) => {\n    if (!rev || !rev.findings || rev.findings.length === 0) return { key: d.key, review: rev, verdicts: [] }\n    return agent(COMMON + `\\nYou are a verifier. For EACH finding below (focus \"${d.key}\"), try hard to REFUTE it: reread code and spec, reproduce the run yourself. real=false if wrong, already documented, outside the brief, or without evidence; real=true only if reproduced or confirmed. Re-assess severity.\\n\\nFindings:\\n${JSON.stringify(rev.findings, null, 1)}`,\n      { label: `verify:${d.key}`, phase: 'Verify', schema: VERDICTS })\n      .then(v => ({ key: d.key, review: rev, verdicts: v ? v.verdicts : null }))\n  },\n)\nreturn results\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":799,"cache_read_input_tokens":605774,"output_tokens":3909,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":653},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":799,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3909,"cache_read_input_tokens":605774,"cache_creation_input_tokens":799,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":799},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01D1ZyseTfD5sWfmdSChxVAY":{"script":"export const meta = {\n  name: 'derivability-followup',\n  description: 'Narrow adversarial check of the review fixes (commit b22aef9) and of the French report',\n  phases: [{ title: 'Review' }, { title: 'Verify' }],\n}\n\nconst SP = '/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/d1/followup'\nconst COMMON = `\nYou are an adversarial, read-only reviewer of a Lean 4 formalization (Lean v4.35, no Mathlib). Repository /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern, Lake project formal/, branch formal/derivability_0.1. Do NOT modify repository files. Scratch files only under ${SP}/<your-label>/ (create it); check claims with: cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && ~/.elan/bin/lake env lean <scratch.lean> (modules are built; import Ern.Lib.DataStack or Ern.Derived.Arena; #eval and decide work on concrete states, see the cases at the end of each module for how runs are built).\nNormative text: /Users/guygouri/Downloads/ERN_Spec1_Memory_Model_specification_normative_candidate_corrigee.md (French candidate Spec 1; §46, §58, §77 O18, §78 O19 matter here). Rules: /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/AGENTS.md (Review section). The kernel Ern/MM03.lean is unchanged.\nThe las