t still mentions a removed hypothesis or contradicts its statement. (5) #print axioms of reset_as_kernel, issue_as_kernel_split, ce_avail_leaf, newArena_as_library.` },\n  { key: 'report', prompt: `Focus: the French report formal/reports/Derivability_v0.1.md against the code of both modules (formal/Ern/Derived/Arena.lean, formal/Ern/Lib/DataStack.lean). The brief requires sections: (a) status of issue_as_kernel, reset_as_kernel, newArena_as_library; (b) the writeShared counterexample; (c) deviations in either direction; (d) status of the DataStack theorems; (e) amendments of Spec 1 text that follow from the results, clause by clause; (f) questions. Check: every theorem or definition name cited exists and says what the report says (open the statements); counts of constants/theorems (verify with an axiom sweep: write a scratch file importing both modules that iterates env.constants for modules Ern.Derived.Arena and Ern.Lib.DataStack and counts constants and theorems, see /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/d1/axcheck2.lean, and check no constant depends on axioms beyond propext and Quot.sound); cross references between sections ((e) n, (f) n, écart n) point to the right item; spec quotes in the report are verbatim from the spec file; no claim stronger than what is proven; amendments in (e) follow from results and present alternatives instead of choosing where the result does not decide.` },\n]\n\nphase('Review')\nconst results = await pipeline(\n  DIMS,\n  d => agent(COMMON + '\\n' + d.prompt + '\\nReturn your findings.', { label: `review:${d.key}`, phase: 'Review', schema: FINDINGS }),\n  (rev, d) => {\n    if (!rev || !rev.findings || rev.findings.length === 0) return { key: d.key, review: rev, verdicts: [] }\n    return agent(COMMON + `\\nYou are a verifier. For EACH finding below (focus \"${d.key}\"), try hard to REFUTE it: reread code and spec, reproduce the run yourself. real=false if wrong, 